05/02/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"I am writing to bring to your attention an issue regarding unauthorized hard inquiries on my XXXX and XXXX credit reports dated XX/XX/2023. These inquiries indicate an attempt to open an account in my name, which I did not authorize or initiate. 

While I do currently hold a Capital One account, I wish to clarify that I am not disputing the existence of this account. However, I must emphasize that the hard inquiries on my credit reports are unauthorized and have resulted in significant distress and disruption to my financial affairs. 

I recently became aware that I am a victim of identity theft, and I have taken immediate steps to address this matter. Enclosed with this letter, you will find a copy of the police report documenting the identity theft incident. 

I kindly request that Capital One takes swift action to investigate and rectify this situation. Specifically, I ask that you contact both XXXX and XXXX credit reporting agencies to request the removal of the unauthorized hard inquiries from my credit reports. These inquiries are adversely affecting my credit score and financial well-being, and their removal is essential to restoring the integrity of my credit profile. 

I trust that Capital One will handle this matter with the utmost urgency and professionalism. Your cooperation in resolving this issue promptly will be greatly appreciated.",None,CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION,NY,11213,None,Consent provided,Web,05/02/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8909982
05/02/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"On XX/XX/year>, my Citi credit card number was used to make 3 fraudulent purchases at XXXX online. Each purchase was for {$250.00}, for a total of {$770.00}. 

I noticed these charges on XX/XX/year>, and reported them to Citi as fraudulent purchases. Citi said they would refund the {$770.00}. 

Later, I learned that XXXX told Citi that the online order was picked up ( in XXXX ; I live in New York ), and therefore was a legitimate purchase. Citi provided me with the information that XXXX provided them. ( See attached file XXXX ) The purchase was made using a fake email address. The items, large boxes of flooring, were picked up in XXXX XXXX, where I do not live. 

Citi reversed their decision, and charged me the full {$770.00} again. They didn't contact me to tell me this, I discovered it myself later when my credit card statement seemed too high. 

I have since called Citi multiple times over the past 2 years, explaining that this was obviously a fraudulent purchase, based on the evidence they already have. Every time, they tell me that they have to re-open the account and re-start the investigation process. Citi assures me they have all the information they need ( which is true ), they can see it was a fraudulent purchase, and will contact me when the investigation is complete. 

Then, nothing happens. Multiple times, I have called Citi back a couple of months later, and they tell me the same thing again ; they have to re-open the account and start the investigation, etc... They can see it was a fraudulent charge and they will contact me when the investigation is complete, etc... 

I have been doing this every few months since 2022, when this first began. I have files the dispute forms Citi requited, and provided them with all the information they have asked for. I would like Citi to finally resolve my fraud dispute case and refund me the {$770.00} I am owed.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,145XX,None,Consent provided,Web,05/02/24,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8907547
