05/13/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account status incorrect,"I am writing to file a formal complaint regarding inaccurate information listed on my credit report, which has led to significant harm to my credit score and financial standing. Pursuant to the provisions outlined in 15 USC 1681 b 2, 15 U.S. Code 6802, and 18 USC 8, I am seeking redress under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), specifically codified in 15 U.S.C. 1681 et seq.

The inaccurate information on my credit report pertains to closed accounts previously removed from credit reports, Incorrect credit score, and added collection from unknown collector whom I do not owe. Despite my attempts to rectify these errors through this credit reporting agency, the erroneous information persists, adversely affecting my ability to access credit and financial services. 

As per the FCRA, consumers like me have the right to accurate and up-to-date credit reporting, and any inaccuracies must be promptly investigated and corrected by the credit reporting agencies. However, despite my efforts to dispute these inaccuracies, this reporting agency have failed to comply with their obligations under the law, thereby causing ongoing harm to my financial well-being. 

Furthermore, the persistence of these inaccuracies violates my rights under 15 U.S. Code 6802, which stipulates obligations with respect to disclosures of personal information, and 18 U.S. Code 8, defining the obligations or other securities of the United State.

In light of the foregoing, I am requesting that the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau launch an immediate investigation into the matter and take appropriate action against the credit reporting agency responsible for these inaccuracies. I also request that all erroneous information be promptly removed from my credit report and that I be provided with a corrected copy of my credit report at no cost. 

PLEASE REMOVE THE FOLLOWING ITEM IMMEDIATELY UNKNOWN COLLECTION. 
{$240.00} Thank you for your attention to this matter. I trust that the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau will take the necessary steps to address this issue and ensure that consumers like me are protected from the adverse effects of inaccurate credit reporting. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11554,None,Consent provided,Web,05/13/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8989290
