04/18/24,Mortgage,Home equity loan or line of credit (HELOC),Trouble during payment process,Trying to communicate with the company to fix an issue while managing or servicing your loan,"I contacted ThirdFederal on XX/XX/year> to close my HELOC account. They stated they would not close the account until a {$65.00} administrative fee was paid. The fee was not due for another 30 days and is a yearly administrative fee. When I explained I should not be forced to pay a fee for an account that will not be staying open I was told I needed to pay it. 

This is a predatory practice as I had no other option but to pay the fee or risk damage to my credit. I have now paid a administrative fee to keep the HELOC open for another 12 months even though my desire was to close it. 

