05/18/23,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Problem with a credit reporting company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"This letter is a formal complaint that Equifax has been reporting inaccurate and incomplete credit information on my Credit Report. I understand that mistakes happen but your inaccurate information could cost me in higher interest rates and I have enough expenses as it is. I have previously disputed this item with Equifax Reference number : XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX Bankruptcy- Filed date XX/XX/2022 and in response Equifax verified the item as accurate, stating that they have verified the information with the court. I contacted the court and their response is enclosed. It is clear they do not report to you or any credit bureau for that matter, therefore the original response verifying the item with the court was either an error or a lie. Either way, the reporting requirements do not comply with FCRA 611 ( 15 U.S.C 1681I ) and the information must be deleted immediately. 
The U. S. Bankruptcy Court items listed on my credit file and per the FCRA 623 ( a ) ( 5 ) : If the Credit Bureau can not VALIDATE the information with the ORIGINAL CREDITOR, they must remove said information from the consumer credit file. The County Recorder of Deeds and the Bankruptcy Courts have both mailed me letters which clearly state that they do NOT provide any information to credit reporting agencies, nor do they ever validate and/or confirm public records. It is the credit reporting agencies, and/or other third-party providers such as XXXX who collect information regarding public cases from public records.

Public records information is NEVER validated by the Recorder of Deeds nor the U. S. Court system due to the Fair Credit Reporting Agency PRIVACY LAW. My inquiry to the County Recorder of Deeds and U. S. Bankruptcy Courts confirmed Equifax has never validated or verified these public record entries on my credit report, neither will they ever be by them. They further stated while they are NOT liable or responsible for any MISUSE or INCORRECT public records, nor the distribution of said information, public records may, and oftentimes are, reported by third party sources unawares to the consumer, and in most cases, incorrectly. 

If they fail to respond within 30 days of receipt of this letter will result in a small claims action against Equifax. I will be seeking no less than {$5000.00} in damages for, but not limited to 1 ) Defamation ; 2 ) Negligent Enhancement of Identity Fraud ; 3 ) Violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act and Consumer.

***I would like the bankruptcy information to be deleted immediately.

Attached is the letter from the court. the COURT does not verify with THIRD PARTY AGENCIES or CREDIT BUREAUS. ***",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11758,None,Consent provided,Web,05/18/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6993848
