03/20/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Other personal consumer report,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I believe my information was involved in some type of data breach - Transunion has been releasing my information to companies for rental pre-screenings that are not mine. I've had my credit frozen since XX/XX/2023 and Transunion told me, if the companies had my information on file the freeze won't prevent this type of credit pull - because it's not considered new, and they said they can not help me as these are not hard inquiries. 

XX/XX/2023 - XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX Transunion XXXX XXXX XX/XX/2023 - XXXX XXXX XXXX via Transunion XXXX XXXX XX/XX/2023 - XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXa Transunion XXXX XXXX XX/XX/2023 and XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXX/XX/2023 - XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXX/XX/XXXX XXXX Transunion XXXX XX/XX/2023 - XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,11222,None,Consent provided,Web,03/20/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8584994
03/14/24,Debt collection,Other debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt is not yours,"I am writing to address the inclusion of unauthorized transactions in my consumer report, for which I did not provide authorization or instruction. Consequently, I formally request the blocking and removal of these accounts without any error or misrepresentation of facts. Below are the specific accounts in question : It appears that your organization may be in violation of 15 U.S.C 1681a 2 ( A ) ( i ), which prohibits a consumer report from containing : "" ( A ) subject to section 1681s-3 of this title, any -- - ( i ) report containing information solely as to transactions or experiences between the consumer and the person making the report! '' This statute explicitly states that XXXX making the report should not be included in my consumer report, as transactions or experiences associated with the line of credit extended between the consumer and the reporting entity should not be encompassed in the consumer report. 

I urge you to promptly update my utilization to 5 % or below within 10 calendar days or expunge all utilization from the mentioned accounts.

Furthermore, I request that you provide all documents on which you rely for reporting the referenced accounts, in accordance with the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( 15 U.S.C. 1681g ). The information you are reporting is detrimental to my reputation and is adversely impacting my creditworthiness.

Therefore, I demand the removal of these accounts from my file within 30 days, as mandated by the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( 15 U.S.C. 1681i ), or verification of these accounts.

Additionally, in addition to the removal of erroneous and unverified information, kindly eliminate all non-account holding inquiries older than 30 days.

Failure to provide a satisfactory response with the deletion of the mentioned utilization and inquiries will result in legal action being taken against your company, for which I will seek {$1000.00} per violation : Defamation of Character Civil Liability Fair Credit Reporting Act 15 U.S.C 1681 violations for willful noncompliance - 616. Civil liability for willful noncompliance [ 15 U.S.C. 1681n ]",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11701,None,Consent provided,Web,03/14/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8546690
