15 U.S. Code 1666b - Timing of payments ( a ) Time to make payments A creditor may not treat a payment on a credit card account under an open end consumer credit plan as late for any purpose, unless the creditor has adopted reasonable procedures designed to ensure that each periodic statement including the information required by 1637 ( b ) Statement required with each billing cycle is mailed or delivered to the consumer not later than 21 days before the payment due date.

