05/18/23,Credit card or prepaid card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers",Didn't receive advertised or promotional terms,"Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, I hope this email finds you well. I am writing to file a complaint regarding a recent issue I encountered with American Express regarding their failure to provide me with the promised welcome offer for my credit card. Additionally, I have concerns about the fraudulent promotion advertisement they used during the application process. 

I applied for an American Express credit card on XXXX XXXX with the understanding that I would be eligible to receive a welcome bonus of XXXX Membership Rewards ( MR ) points upon meeting the specified criteria. However, after six months of fulfilling all the requirements, American Express informed me that I was not eligible for the welcome bonus. According to their explanation, I should have received a pop-up message during the application process notifying me of my ineligibility, but I never received any such message. I can confidently confirm that I would have declined to proceed with the application had I been aware of this information. 

The misleading and fraudulent promotion advertisement employed by American Express is deeply disappointing. As a responsible consumer, I carefully reviewed the terms and conditions of the offer before applying, and I fulfilled all the necessary requirements within the designated timeframe. It is disheartening to be denied the promised welcome bonus of XXXX MR points after investing time and effort into meeting the obligations. 

In light of this situation, I kindly request your intervention and assistance in addressing this matter with American Express. I believe that American Express should honor their promotional promises and rectify this issue by providing me with the welcome bonus of XXXX MR points that I am entitled to. 

I urge the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau to take appropriate action to ensure that American Express addresses this deceptive marketing practice and resolves the issue to the satisfaction of affected customers. 

Thank you for your attention to this matter. I look forward to your prompt assistance and a fair resolution. Should you require any additional information or documentation from my end, please do not hesitate to contact me at [ your contact number ] or [ your email address ]. 

Sincerely, XXXX.",None,AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY,NY,11361,None,Consent provided,Web,05/18/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6995506
