03/20/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"I want to emphasize that the inclusion of erroneously reported late payment remarks on my accounts not only raises concerns but also constitutes a clear breach of the regulations outlined in the 15 USC 1666. This statute, which is part of the Fair Credit Billing Act, specifically safeguards consumers from unjust billing practices and requires accurate reporting of payment histories. Each payment linked to these accounts has been diligently and promptly made within the designated timeframes. Therefore, any deviation from this precise reporting not only undermines my financial integrity but also violates the legal protections afforded under this statute. It is imperative to rectify this situation promptly to ensure compliance with the law and uphold the rights of consumers.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,11510,None,Consent provided,Web,03/20/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8588474
