03/19/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Statement Regarding Unauthorized Sharing of Personal Information To Whom It May Concern, I am writing to address a concerning issue regarding the unauthorized sharing of my personal information by XXXX XXXX  on my consumer report. This unauthorized sharing of information has come to my attention and raises serious concerns regarding the protection of my privacy rights and compliance with applicable laws and regulations. 

XXXX XXXX XXXX actions in sharing my personal information on my consumer report without my authorization are in direct violation of several laws and regulations designed to safeguard consumer privacy and ensure fair credit reporting practices. Specifically, these actions may contravene the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act ( GLBA ), Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) regulations, and potentially state privacy laws. 

The FCRA mandates the accuracy, fairness, and privacy of consumer credit reports, including the permissible purposes for accessing and sharing consumer information. The unauthorized sharing of my personal information by XXXX XXXX may violate the FCRA 's provisions related to permissible purposes and the accuracy of consumer reports. 

Similarly, the XXXX requires financial institutions to protect the privacy and security of customers ' nonpublic personal information. XXXX XXXX XXXX unauthorized sharing of my information may breach the XXXX 's privacy requirements and regulatory standards set forth by the CFPB. 

Additionally, state privacy laws may provide further protections for consumer privacy rights and impose additional requirements on the collection, use, and sharing of personal information. 

I demand immediate action to address this unauthorized sharing of my personal information by XXXXXXXX XXXX and to rectify any inaccuracies or violations of my privacy rights on my consumer report. Furthermore, I expect XXXXXXXX XXXX to implement measures to prevent similar unauthorized sharing of personal information in the future and to comply fully with all applicable laws and regulations governing consumer privacy and fair credit reporting practices. 

Please provide confirmation once the necessary actions have been taken to address this matter and ensure the accuracy and privacy of my consumer report. 

Sincerely, XXXX",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,109XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/19/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8579056
03/19/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"I am writing to seek your assistance regarding unresolved errors on my credit report that have negatively impacted my financial standing. Despite my repeated attempts to rectify these issues with the credit bureau, the errors remain on my credit report and they are greatly damaging my credit score. 

The payment history of XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  account XXXX erroneously shows a 60-day and a 90-day late payment from XXXX to XXXX on XXXX. I have always make payments on time. This is an apparent reporting error not only because I made payments on time but the data show does not make sense. There's no 30 days late payment on XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX, how can it be 60 days late on XXXX of XXXX? 

I have sent numerous letters to the credit bureau to correct these mistakes, requesting for investigation into this matter and have them removed from my credit history. Unfortunately, I have not received any communication from the bureau regarding the status of their investigation or any steps taken to rectify these inaccuracies. 

This lack of response and action from the credit bureau has left me feeling that my consumer rights are being neglected. Under the law, I am entitled to an accurate representation of my credit history. Therefore, I am reaching out to the CFPB to intervene and ensure a thorough investigation is conducted into these errors. I am seeking your help to have these inaccuracies removed from my credit report promptly. 

I appreciate your attention to this matter and look forward to your support in resolving this issue. Please find attached all the documents for reference. 

Thank you, XXXX XXXX",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,11355,None,Consent provided,Web,03/19/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8579136
