05/20/23,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"As a consumer, I have a right to privacy. I did not give any creditor or credit reporting agency written or verbal consent to furnish any of my personal information to XXXX. I recently received a copy of my XXXX, Equifax and XXXX credit report, and I noticed some late payments posted on my credit report. 

XXXX : 5 Missed payments XXXX  XXXX : XXXX Missed Payments XXXX  : 2 Missed Payments XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  2 Missed Payments XXXX XXXX XXXX : 1 Missed Payment Your company is in clear violation of the law. Under 15 USC 1681b - permissible purpose of consumer reports, THE LAW CLEARLY STATES : ( b ) IN GENERAL Subject to subsection ( c ) any consumer reporting agency may furnish a consumer report under the following circumstances and no other : ( 2 ) In accordance with the written instructions of the consumer to whom it relates.

Did I give you written instructions to furnish this on my credit report?

Furthermore, the FAIR CREDIT REPORTING ACT 15 USC 1681 ( 2 ) ( a ) ( i ) Exclusions from a consumer credit report clearly states : ( 2 ) EXCLUSIONS Except as provided in paragraph ( 3 ), the term consumer report does not include ( A ) Subject to section 1681s-3 of this title, any ( i ) report containing information solely as to transactions or experiences between the consumer and the person making the report ; Transactions in this matter includes payment history, because it's my transactions with the line of credit that the person "" corporation '' extended to me the consumer.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10310,None,Consent provided,Web,05/20/23,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,7005165
