10/04/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"The credit reporting agency is in violation of 15 USC 1681a ( 2 ) I by reporting transactions between myself and XXXX XXXX on my credit report. The law clearly states the term credit report does not include report containing information solely as to transactions or experiences between the consumer and the person making the report. The word person refers to a corporation. So XXXX XXXX is the person and I am the consumer. The credit reporting agency should not be displaying this information such as late payments on my credit file. The credit reporting agency has also violated 15 USC 1681b ( 2 ) which states any consumer reporting agency may furnish a consumer report under the following circumstances and no other, in accordance to with the written instructions of the consumer to whom it relates. I never wrote any credit reporting agency asking them to furnish anything on my credit report. In fact, I've done the opposite. I have written several letters opting out and asking the credit reporting agency not to furnish information on my credit file without my permission. I have been a victim of fraud and identity left in the past and I am asking the credit reporting agency to abide by the FCRA and respect my privacy.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11210,None,Consent provided,Web,10/04/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,10347435
