04/16/24,Mortgage,Conventional home mortgage,Trouble during payment process,"Escrow, taxes, or insurance","As per our mortgage agreement with PenFed, it is the fiduciary responsibility of our mortgage servicer to properly accrue and submit tax payments on our behalf. Penfed and their partner XXXX were deficient in this responsibility which resulted in an escrow account underage. 

We contacted PenFed in XXXX to alert them to an error we identified with our escrow withholding. This was not a timing issue, but an error. PenFed did not correct this error which resulted in an escrow account balance underage that we continue to be asked to cover. 

When we brought this error to PenFeds attention in XXXX, it was their responsibility to investigate and correct. In XXXX, Penfed insisted that their calculation was correct and our concerns were baseless. As the concern we raised ultimately was validated, it appears that PenFed and XXXX failed in their responsibility to properly investigate our account, or the investigation was inadequate. 

Our concern was proven valid after PenFed stated the withholding was accurate. This is evidence that PenFeds conclusion of the underage being caused by a timing issue resulted from an inadequately performed or not performed investigation. 

To state it clearly, this was an error by PenFed and/or XXXX. They failed to properly investigate the concern when it was brought to their attention in XXXX which only compounded the error. The issue could have been remediated in XXXX when it was initially brought to their attention, but instead is still impacting our payments in XXXX. 

In XXXX, XXXX we were again alerted to an escrow shortfall that we are being asked to cover.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,PENTAGON FEDERAL CREDIT UNION,NY,11762,Servicemember,Consent provided,Web,04/16/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8784284
