04/13/24,Mortgage,FHA mortgage,Struggling to pay mortgage,Foreclosure,"Good day, I purchased a house in XXXX. The originator of the loan was XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. This company went out of business and I started to receive correspondences from XXXX XXXX XXXX. I paid my mortgage and was having some issues with them receiving payments because I was paying cash at the bank and some monies was not being applied to my mortgage. Around XX/XX/XXXX I paid my mortgage and it was refused. I went to the bank to to find out what the issue was and they could not answer my questions. They suggested I called the corporate number. I called and to no avail was left on the phone for long periods of time. This went on for months and when I did speak to a account manager I was told that they were not sure what happened and not sure why the payment was not accepted. I explained that they are refusing my payment. months later I started to receive correspondences from another bank Carrington mtg. They stated that they are now the holders of the mortgage. I spoke to an account manager who stated that XXXX sold them the loan and that I will now have to pay them. I told them I didn't know who they were and why they were calling and writing to me. I started to receive threatening letters for foreclosure and demands for payments. I requested assistance from a neighborhood agency to help with modification and clarification. I received assistance from XXXX and in XXXX a check for over $ XXXX was sent to Carrington. Before the check was sent I had a conversation with a rep who stated I had $ XXXX remaining on my mortgage and with a $ XXXX payment and adjustments I will have a balance of $ XXXX. They received the funds and did not apply it accordingly. They sent a letter stating I still owe $ XXXX. i asked how the funds were applied and if I could speak to a manager to get some adjustment. I was told that the Manager was not available. I receive correspondence saying the manager can not reduce the payments or change the way the funds were applied. I am writing because I have no where else to turn. I spent my who childhood and youth working so that I can have a piece of the American dream and now it's being ripped from me. I need assistance as soon as possible to stop this foreclosure and thievery.",None,"CARRINGTON MORTGAGE SERVICES, LLC",NY,122XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/13/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8764428
