03/29/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Opening an account,Didn't receive terms that were advertised,"I am writing to address a distressing matter concerning the closure of my Wells Fargo account and the failure to receive the promised {$320.00} bonus under a promotional offer. On XX/XX/XXXX, I opened a Everyday Checking account with Wells Fargo in response to a promotional offer that entailed receiving a {$320.00} bonus upon making a direct deposit of {$1000.00} or more. I promptly fulfilled this requirement on XX/XX/XXXX, fully expecting to receive the bonus as per the terms outlined by Wells Fargo. However, before I had the chance to receive the promised bonus, my account was abruptly closed on XX/XX/XXXX, citing inactivity within a mere 60-day period. While I acknowledge that there was indeed no activity within this timeframe, the duration of 60 days is unreasonably short. What exacerbates this situation is the lack of any prior warning or notification from Wells Fargo regarding the impending closure, depriving me of the opportunity to take corrective action. The closure of my account results in the forfeiture of the {$320.00} bonus that I rightfully earned by fulfilling the terms of the promotional offer. It is deeply disappointing and disheartening to have been denied this incentive due to circumstances beyond my control. I demand immediate redress from Wells Fargo. Firstly, I expect the promised {$320.00} bonus to be promptly credited to me, as originally agreed upon. Additionally, I urge Wells Fargo to review its policy regarding account closure and provide customers with adequate notice and opportunity to address any concerns before taking such drastic actions. Furthermore, I request a thorough investigation into this matter to ascertain why I did not receive the bonus despite fulfilling all the stipulated requirements. It is imperative that Wells Fargo upholds its commitment to customer satisfaction and transparency in all its dealings.",Comp