03/13/24,Credit card,Store credit card,Fees or interest,Problem with fees,"I am writing to bring to your immediate attention a highly distressing matter regarding my New York and Company credit card account. Regrettably, despite my repeated attempts to resolve this issue, I have yet to receive any satisfactory resolution from Comenity Bank, the issuer of my credit card. 

In 2021 my New York and Company credit card was unlawfully compromised by an unauthorized individual. Despite promptly reporting this fraudulent activity to this company, relevant authorities, including the FBI Internet Complaint Center and all three major credit bureaus, and submitting a prior complaint to the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ), the situation remains unresolved. 

The unauthorized user made substantial purchases using my credit card, resulting in a significant financial burden. Despite my diligent efforts to mitigate the impact of this fraud, New York and Company continues to charge and bill me for these fraudulent transactions. Moreover, for the past three years, I have been inexplicably locked out of my online account, rendering me unable to make payments or access essential account information. 

Furthermore, I have not received any written billing statements or been issued a replacement credit card. This lack of communication has made it exceedingly difficult for me to keep track of payment due dates, leading to recurring very high late fees and additional financial strain. As an individual with a documented disability that affects my memory and concentration, this oversight has had a profoundly detrimental impact on my financial well-being and health. 

I implore you to urgently investigate this matter and take immediate corrective action to rectify the situation. I request that you : Cease all billing for fraudulent transactions immediately. 
Provide me with a detailed account of all charges incurred on my credit card since the fraudulent activity occurred. 
Issue a replacement credit card and restore my access to the online account management portal. 
Waive all late fees accrued as a result of the failure to provide billing notices and account access. 
Implement measures to prevent similar incidents of fraud in the future and enhance customer account security protocols. 

Failure to address these concerns timely may compel me to escalate this issue through additional channels, including legal action and further complaints to regulatory authorities.",None,"Bread Financial Holdings, Inc.",NY,14221,None,Consent provided,Web,03/13/24,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8538909
