03/12/24,Prepaid card,General-purpose prepaid card,Trouble using the card,Trouble using the card to spend money in a store or online,"This issue is regarding an unspent credit of {$120.00} available/ remaining on an "" Award Card '' that was issued as a replacement to a compromised "" Gift Card '' back in XXXX. 

[ XXXX ] As per New York state law, there is a 5-year expiration date from purchase before funds on a gift card can expire. 

[ XXXX ] I had previously purchased a gift card for use, and it was unfortunately compromised. Blackhawk Network ( hereinafter "" BHN '' ) / Pathward ( previously known as XXXX ) did provide a replacement. 

[ XXXX ] However, on the replacement card, it is marked as an "" Award Card '' with a very short valid period of until XX/XX/XXXX. 

[ XXXX ] On XX/XX/XXXX at XXXX, I initiated a call to XXXX, the customer support number for BHN XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX issued gift cards, to see if I can have a new card issued or somehow get access to the {$120.00} remaining. * * Note : Attached is a full audio recording of the entire conversation between myself and the representative I spoke with, which includes discussion of [ XXXX ] .... 

[ XXXX ] Customer service rep did confirm that any available amount remaining will be automatically lost, and refused to provide any option to access the funds, citing that the replacement card is an "" Award Card '' and thus, New York State 's Gift Card law does not apply.

This scenario, in my opinion, is : - ( 1 ) a very obvious attempt at circumventing the spirit of the Gift Card expiration law by using clever legal language, especially given that the funds are still unused and available on the "" now expired card. '' - ( 2 ) could be considered a violation of New York State 's Abandoned Property Law- since the bank is aware that funds were paid, but was "" expired and left unused. '' As per the Abandoned Property Law, funds should be transferred to New York State Comptrollers Office of Unclaimed Funds- not simply kept.",None,Blackhawk Network Holdings Inc.,NY,11803,None,Consent provided,Web,03/12/24,Closed with explanation,No,N/A,8529801
