03/07/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"On XX/XX/XXXX, I leased a Hyundai XXXX  XXXX. The salespersons pressured me into paying {$550.00} a month based on my credit, when I had expected to pay {$200.00} less. I initially went to purchase a XXXX XXXX and the salesperson pressured me to lease a XXXX. It placed me in an unfair situation because I needed a vehicle to travel from XXXX XXXX, NY to XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX at least 3 times a week. 

Nonetheless, because of my credit, they made me feel grateful I was able to get anything since I needed a vehicle and would not get any other vehicle. Before leaving the dealership I was asked if I wanted to receive the option to receive emails or mail to my home address. I gave them my email address. 

First, email I ever received came in on XX/XX/XXXX. And it said "" Thanks For Letting Us Care For Your Hyundai ''. Therefore they knew how to get in touch with me. This particular entity was "" XXXX XXXX '' The second email on XX/XX/XXXX subject "" Your account has been updated ''. This was "" Hyundai Motor America '', They said "" Dear XXXX XXXX, Thanks for stopping by your local Hyundai dealership to add the following vehicle to your MyHyundai account : MODEL YEAR:XXXX MODEL NAME : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX '' The third email on XX/XX/XXXX subject "" Hyundai Consumer Affairs Case # : XXXX '' was regarding my "" Blue Link Pin ''. This was "" MyHyundai '' or "" HMAUSA '' at the Hyundai Customer Care Center. 

It was not until my XXXX email when Hyundai Motor Finance emailed me on XX/XX/XXXX and told me to pay {$550.00}. However, I had already been two payments behind for XXXX and XXXX of XXXX. They did not tell me to pay {$1100.00} which is 2 * {$550.00}. But when I received the email it occurred to me that they did not simply debit the card they already had on file for me. By XXXX of XXXX, I had already had a negative on my Hyundai balance and they had reported it to the credit bureau agencies before telling me I did not pay XXXX or XXXX. And in XXXX, they didn't tell me when they first reached out to me. 

This was frustrating because now my credit was shot and I was trying to purchase a home. I immediately spoke to XXXX XXXX and then filed with the credit bureau agencies when they would not help. The CBAs sided with Hyundai because I did not pay. However, at the time I had no way of articulating how conniving I believed a car company would be. They set me up with high leasing costs and no information to reference how much I paid versus what the balance was with respect to principal and interest. Now, I had an outstanding amount to pay. Luckily, I was able to pay it all off in XXXX of XXXX. But I felt the damage was already done, especially since I was applying for a home loan. 

The issue continued to follow me. Because, I was already paying high insurance while paying high fees for the lease the problem came to a head on XX/XX/XXXX when I dropped the collision. The worst mistake. I forgot to add it back when I was able to balance costs. On XX/XX/XXXX I had a car accident and insurance did not cover the car. I requested a detailed cost of the vehicle via email on XX/XX/XXXX and then via phone call on XX/XX/XXXX and complained separately about the handling of the vehicle. I never received one. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, I asked for a detailed cost breakdown. I have never received information. However, because the car was totaled and a dispute ensued the account was charged off. I now have horrible credit based on this interaction with Hyundai.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,HYUNDAI CAPITAL AMERICA,NY,138XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/07/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8498567
