05/10/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Closing an account,Company closed your account,"I received a phone call today from the Chase Executive office, XXXX XXXX XXXX ( XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX ), informing me that my Chase relationship, including my personal business account and all my credit cards, has ended due to what he called potential excessive and illicit transactions. 

I have never made any illicit transactions. 

XXXX XXXX said the decision was final, no explanation was necessary, and there was no means of appealing. XXXX XXXX mentioned that the bank could do this because I signed a clause in the legal agreement upon opening my account with Chase. 

XXXX XXXX provided me with no other details. He said he didn't need to tell me the reason for the actions or their timing or whether this impacted my future banking relationships with Chase or other banks. 

