05/09/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"In XX/XX/XXXX, I discovered a discrepancy on my credit report involving a Capital One account indicating a 120-day late payment, purportedly opened in XX/XX/XXXX. Despite my vigilant monitoring of credit activities, I did not receive any notifications regarding this account. This lack of notification stemmed from the account being associated with two previously closed Capital One accounts, which intermittently sent notifications. Upon identifying this anomaly in XXXX, I promptly took corrective measures to address the issue. This included initiating the closure of the account and requesting its removal from my credit reports. Subsequently, I undertook a systematic approach to address the matter, involving the submission of an identity theft report to the FTC, filing a police report, and engaging with the relevant credit bureaus and Capital One. To facilitate a thorough investigation into the fraudulent activity, I requested comprehensive documentation from Capital One, including the account application, transaction statements, associated business information, and digital identifiers of the alleged account holder. This request was made in accordance with established protocols and regulations governing identity theft investigations. It is pertinent to note that the nature of the account in question was a business card, associated with a business entity not affiliated with my own. This further underscores the seriousness of the fraudulent activity and its potential implications. Despite my efforts to resolve the matter amicably and in accordance with legal provisions, I have encountered challenges in obtaining the requested information from Capital One. Furthermore, the recent communication from Capital One asserting the validity of the account without providing substantiating evidence is concerning. In light of these developments, I believe that Capital One has violated the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). I remain committed to cooperating with all relevant parties to achieve a satisfactory outcome and mitigate any adverse impact on my credit standing.",None,CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION,NY,14626,None,Consent provided,Web,05/09/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8974523
