04/28/24,Student loan,Private student loan,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"I applied for an income driven repayment calculation/modification to lower my monthly payment. The email correspondence was toon quite a bit of time and took days or weeks for replies from the servicer. The servicer has/had limited phone hours in comparison to my schedule and even when I found time to call wait times were long and difficult to manage. Finally I thought everything was set as I was told by the loan servicer. However processing by the servicer took longer than suggested time and even though the consolidation finally went through loans were reported 30, 60, and 90 days past due. I called the servicer, Nelnet, and was told 2 loans were reported late in error but that it would be corrected. I didn't need to provide any additional information, paperwork, or documentation ; it was simply an error on their end. Still months later all three major bureaus have me as 30, 60, and 90 days late on my student loan during that time. Nelnet representatives told me they would handle the correction due to me. Still nothing has been done. As an adult in my 40s this is the only derogatory mark on my credit and it prevents plans for my family of taking place ( i.e. college for my child and smaller home purchase ). My credit scores at all three bureaus have dropped over 100 points solely because of this error.",None,"Nelnet, Inc.",NY,142XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/28/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8876191
04/03/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"On XX/XX/XXXX, Chase posted a {$27.00} charge onto my Chase Sapphire Reserve credit card with a transaction date of XX/XX/XXXX, purportedly for "" XXXX XXXX Guest Visit. '' Access to XXXX XXXX XXXXounges is a benefit of the Chase Sapphire Reserve product. The benefit is spelled out at https : XXXX In part, the website provides that : "" With a Chase Sapphire Reserve credit card, primary cardmembers and authorized users can activate complimentary XXXX XXXX XXXX membership. After that, they can access airport lounges with up to 2 guests for no additional fee. '' I am the primary cardmember, and my spouse is an authorized user. We have XXXX children. Each of us brought a child into a XXXX XXXX lounge. Based on the foregoing, no fees should have applied, since neither me nor my wife brought more than two guests. 

However, when I called Chase to dispute this transaction, I was told that the fee was for a guest exceeding the limit of 2, and that I could not dispute the transaction because it was an internal Chase charge. 

I explained that I brought one guest into the lounge, and that my spouse brought one guest into the lounge. The representative claimed to understand the matter and said that the charge would be reversed. However, three weeks later I received a letter from Chase stating that the charge was imposed for an additional guest beyond the limit of two. It was as though the conversation with the representative never happened.

I called Chase back and explained the situation to six agents. Each indicated that they understood that no fee should have been imposed but said they were powerless to dispute or remove it. 

It is outrageous that a credit card could place a charge and refuse to provide a mechanism to dispute it. At no point did either my spouse or I bring more than two guests into a XXXX XXXX lounge. I brought one guest, and she brought one guest. No fee should be due ; however, due to Chase 's unwillingness to offer us a dispute resolution process, we have no means of disputing this improper charge.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,10990,None,Consent provided,Web,04/03/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8677723
