03/12/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Problem using a debit or ATM card,"On or about XX/XX/2023, check number XXXX in the amount of {$9900.00} was mailed via US Mail and made out to XXXX XXXX was apparently stolen and cashed at a XXXX XXXX  ATM machine in XXXX. XXXX XXXX  called XXXX XXXX to notify them that a check made out to XXXX XXXX was deposited by someone that does not appear to be from XXXX XXXX, and they wanted to confirm. XXXX XXXX called my office advising of this fact and I immediately called my Chase Bank on XX/XX/2023 to restrict my checking account number ending with ... XXXX and replace it with account ending with ... XXXX. Chase Bank Case number is XXXX. 

Four- and one-half months has gone by and all I keep getting from Chase Bank what the status is for the stolen check is that XXXX XXXX is not responding to chase Bank 's constant calls, emails or letters. I called XXXX XXXX, and they gave me very little information about the stolen check. Both Banks simply said to me that it could take 6 to 8 months before a decision is made. In the meantime, XXXX XXXX keeps sending me notices of payment due.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11791,Older American,Consent provided,Web,03/12/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8535020
