03/30/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Problem making or receiving payments,"On XX/XX/year> I was contacted by someone claiming to be XXXX XXXX and was told that there was a problem with the cashing of my automatic monthly payment. Was told that it could be rectified if I make a faux payment using an account called XXXX and was told it was in my checking account, which led me to believe that it was a Chase approved app and I was told to use this app in order to clear up the problem with XXXX XXXX. Seeing that the app was in Payments and Transfers within my account, I believed I could trust using it. The person who was helping me thru the steps required, who was later found to be a scammer, had me enter an amount of {$670.00} which was only supposed to be a faux entry that would allow XXXX XXXX to straighten out my supposed problem. At first I was hesitant to do it, but the realized it was safely set up in my Chase account which was highlighted by the call from the scammer. I went through the process only because the app was in a Chase protected account, which then turned out to not be true. 
The {$670.00} was transferred to an account called XXXX which was a scam account. 
Chase claims no responsibility and refused to return my {$670.00}, even though I explained that the only reason the phony charge went through was because I believed that Chase was totally involved. Had I never had this app from XXXX in my account, I would never have paid out the {$670.00}. I never gave authorization for Chase to place the XXXX XXXX in my account structure but they did it without my permission or knowledge. After all this occurred I wanted to delete the XXXX app and Chase did it.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11209,Older American,Consent provided,Web,03/30/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8661885
