04/09/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"I have recently pulled my consumer report and I have found numerous inaccurate and unauthorized reporting from XXXX XXXX XXXX BANK to credit bureaus which is a complete violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act and the Privacy Act of 1974! The banking system is dependent upon fair and accurate credit reporting. Inaccurate credit reports directly impair the efficiency of the banking system, and unfair credit reporting methods undermine the public confidence which is essential to the continued functioning of the banking system. According to 15 USC 6802 Except as otherwise provided in this subchapter, a financial institution may not, directly or through any affiliate, disclose to a nonaffiliated third party any nonpublic personal information, unless such financial institution provides or has provided to the consumer a notice that complies with section XXXX of this title. XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  is continuing to report negative items on my consumer report. XXXX XXXX is committing securities fraud and theft. XXXX XXXX has threatened, harassed, and even attempted to extort me for this alleged I debt they claim I owe them. XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  is reporting as a charge off on my consumer and they are still claiming I owe a debt. How is this accurate if a charge off is considered income? When it comes time for XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  to do their quarterly taxes, they're going to report the charge off as income and receive a tax deduction. By law you can't attempt to collect on a debt that has already been paid! That is THEFT! Not only that, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, has a continues to sell this alleged debt along with MY NONPUBLIC information to collection agencies WITHOUT MY WRITTEN, OR VERBAL CONSENT. I pulled XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, SEC filings, more specifically the XXXX and XXXX, with in SEC filed Prospectus, and Trust Indenture Forms. In the forms forms state XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, is securitizing card loan agreements as asset backed securities and capitalizing off of it by trading and putting these loans in a pool and selling them on the secondary market. I also stated in my letter for XXXX XXXX to the immediately notify all credit bureaus that the account is PAID AS AGREED. In the letter, I also stated that I was aware of the fraud and theft that XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  is committing and that I am putting them on notice because I will be filing complaints with the SEC, XXXX, IRS, and further legal action. XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  has refused to remove and is continuing to report negatively on my consumer report! I demand my account be updated PAID AS AGREED immediately Or at receipt of notice to we Opt out of all reporting on any account by the holder per 15 U.S. Code 6802 - Obligations with respect to disclosures of personal information.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,14304,None,Consent provided,Web,04/09/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8729641
06/09/23,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"To whom it may concern i am putting you on notice and reporting an Identity theft report pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( 4 ) ______________________________________________________________________ the term identity theft report has the meaning given that term by rule of the Bureau, I am not denying my account or stating this account isn't mine. I am not asking for verification as defined pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( l ) ( 2 ) ( A ) information in the consumers application for the credit or other information bearing on the credit worthiness of the consumer ; or pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( l ) ( 2 ) ( B ) of the information in the consumers application for the credit to determine that the consumer meets the specific criteria bearing on credit worthiness or insurability. I am demanding you to remove my account information as you have no permissible purpose to furnish a consumer report in regards to i the consumer This is a report that alleges an identity theft which is a requirement pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( 4 ) ( A ) of a identify theft report, and pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( 3 ) Identity theft fraud committed using the identifying information of another person, _____________________________________________________________________ 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( 3 ) Identity theft.

The term identity theft means a fraud committed using the identifying information of another person, subject to such further definition as the Bureau may prescribe, by regulation This report was filed by, i the consumer with an appropriate Federal Law enforcement, government agency making this report Valid pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( 4 ) ( B ) I am aware pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( 4 ) ( C ) i may be charged with criminal penalties relating to the filing of false information if, in fact, the information in the report is false I am a consumer pursuant to 12 CFR 1022.3 ( f ), 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( c ), i do understand XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX thinks they are a Furnisher of information and states they are required to furnishing accurate information, in fact pursuant to 12 CFR 1022.41 ( c ) ( 2 ) you can not be a Furnisher because you acting as consumer reporting agency as defined pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681a of the FCRA , My Identifying information pursuant to 12 CFR 1022.3 ( g ) ( 1 ) which is my name social security number, government identification number date of birth, pursuant to 12 CFR 1022.3 ( g ) 3 ) my account number which is a unique electronic identification number Used To identify me the consumer specifically, in conjunction with information regarding my transactions and experiences, which would be a consumer report pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( d ) ( 1 ) ( A ) and XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX is a consumer reporting agency due to the fact such information is bearing on my consumer credit worthiness, credit standing, credit capacity, character, general reputation, and was collected for the purpose of serving as a factor in establishing the consumers eligibility for credit and has a direct reflection on my credit score pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681g ( f ) ( 2 ) ( A ) ( i ) _________________________________________________________________________ Credit score means a numerical value or a categorization derived from a statistical tool or modeling system used by a person who makes or arranges a loan to predict the likelihood of certain credit behaviors, including default ( and the numerical value or the categorization derived from such analysis may also be referred to as a risk predictor or risk score ) 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( d ) ( 1 ) In general.The term consumer report means ANY written, oral, or other communication of any information by a consumer reporting agency bearing on a consumers credit worthiness, credit standing, credit capacity, character, general reputation, personal characteristics, or mode of living which is used or expected to be used or collected in whole or in part for the purpose of serving as a factor in establishing the consumers eligibility for ( A ) credit or insurance to be used primarily for personal, family, or household purposes ; ( B ) employment purposes ; or ( C ) any other purpose authorized under section 1681b of this title.

Transunion, Pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681 ( b ) ( f ) ( 1 ) You have failed to obtain a consumer report for a purpose for which the consumer report is authorized to be furnished under 15 U.S. Code 1681 ( b ) in conjunction pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681 ( b ) ( f ) ( 2 ) you have no certified purposes in accordance with section 1681e of the Fair Credit Reporting Act as a prospective user of the report through a general or specific certification, you have failed pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681e ( a ) to maintain reasonable procedures designed to avoid to limit the furnishing of consumer reports to the purposes listed under section 1681b of this title. In conjunction Pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681n ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ) you have willfully fails to comply with three requirements imposed under the Fair Credit Reporting Act failed to respect my privacy as a consumer and you are committing identity theft using my identifiable information unauthorized and by law you are liable to i XXXX XXXX in an amount equal to the sum of {$1000.00} damages sustained by the consumer as a result of the failure In addition you have obtained information on, i the consumer under false pretenses from XXXX XXXX XXXX Bank who is in fact acting as consumer report agency resulting in you may be fined under title 18 pursuant 15 U.S. Code 1681q Please understand if you refuse to remove my account from my consumer report i would be authorized pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681p to bring this matter up to any appropriate United States district court, without regard to the amount in controversy, and may be awarded pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681n ( 2 ) a amount of punitive damages as the court may allow ; I HAVE ATTACHED MY CONSUMER REPORT FOR PROOF OF REPORTING PLEASE SEE EXHIBIT Z",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,XXXXX,None,Consent provided,Web,06/09/23,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,7093110
