03/19/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Upon reviewing my credit report, I noticed that these late payments listed below are inaccurately reported, which is adversely effecting my creditworthiness. 
XXXX XXXX XXXX with account number XXXX XXXX XXXX with account number XXXX Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act : 15 USC 1681 Section 602 guarantees my right to privacy. This ensures the confidentiality of my credit report and mandates that information on it must be reported in a way that is fair and accurate to protect the consumer 's privacy.

15 USC 1681 Section 604a Section 2 stipulates that a consumer reporting agency can not furnish a report containing information on a consumer 's credit worthiness, credit standing, credit capacity, character, general reputation, personal characteristics, or mode of living without the consumer 's written instructions.

In light of these provisions, I challenge the authenticity and validity of the late payments recorded on my account and request your agency to produce evidence or documentation that validates this reporting in accordance with my written instructions.

Moreover, in alignment with 15 USC 1666b, a creditor may not treat a payment on a credit card account under an open- end consumer credit plan as late for any purpose unless they have adopted reasonable procedures designed to ensure that each periodic statement contains the required information. Hence, I demand proof that the said procedures were correctly adhered to in my case.

If you can not produce the necessary documents validating these late payment entries, or if the entries are found to be inaccurate, I kindly demand that they be deleted immediately or be updated to reflect as "" Paid on Time '' or "" OK ''.

It is essential for credit reporting agencies to ensure that all consumer reports are accurate, and any inaccuracies are dealt with in a swift manner. I trust that you will handle this matter with the urgency and attention it demands.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,NY,10458,None,Consent provided,Web,03/19/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8567784
04/14/24,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",Domestic (US) money transfer,Fraud or scam,None,"This is a follow up to the following complaint that was closed on XX/XX/year>. 

COMPLAINT ID XXXX SUBMITTED ON XX/XX/year> My personal experience with the last complaint that I submitted was very negative. I went through all the appropriate channels, but no one was able or willing to assist me in any way. I acknowledge that XXXX 's senior management did something on XX/XX/year> to stop the cyber-criminal after I pointed out to them that he created a XXXX ad with their corporate logo to lure additional victims. The next day I noticed that the cyber-criminal 's fake XXXX ad disappeared, his web-site has not been updated since that date, and his fake customer service number now connects people with XXXX 's actual customer service department. 

I have since spent much time educating myself and my family members about financial fraud and scams. I also read numerous articles about people who fell victim to all sorts of scams and fraud. I understand that the problem of scams and fraud is out of control, and many billions of dollars are lost each year to this growing problem. I am also aware that senior citizens are more vulnerable than people of other age groups to falling victim, since they tend to be less educated about cybersecurity. 

The common theme in the stories that I read is that people were scammed or defrauded out of a lot of money since it was taken from them before they knew what was happening or had a chance to react. Subsequently reaching out to law enforcement or their bank 's fraud unit was generally not helpful at all. In the rare instances that the bank was willing to reimburse the victim, the criminal was never apprehended and was emboldened to repeat his crime over and over again. 

The reality is that the only way to stop scams and fraud from happening repeatedly is to simply slow down the movement of money. Imagine how many billions of dollars could be saved each year if banks simply enacted the following control measures to protect their customers from scams and fraud : XXXX. XXXX transfers to new email addresses or mobile phone numbers - automatic 5-day fraud hold with status pending before funds are released 2. Wire transfers - automatic 5-day fraud hold with status pending before funds are released 3. All paper checks - automatic 5-day fraud hold with status pending before funds are released 4. Debit card payments to new recipients - automatic 5-day fraud hold with status pending before funds are released Of course, I acknowledge that there is no way to completely prevent fraud with physical cash, since there is no way to slow down the physical movement of cash. The only way to prevent that type of fraud is to simply eliminate physical cash.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION",NY,11691,None,Consent provided,Web,04/14/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8765270
