03/07/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Unable to get your credit report or credit score,Other problem getting your report or credit score,"To whom it may concern, I am writing today as I have encountered an issue with the Experian Credit Bureau. I am a XXXX  individual who went through the legal name change process to update my first and middle name through New York State Courts. My last name, social security number, date of birth, address, phone number and email address all have stayed the same. I have updated my legal name on all my creditors, bank accounts, employment, Social Security Administration, NYS License and Birth Certificate. I called Experian who I pay monthly to monitor my credit as I have their app and inquired about updating my legal name with them. The Experian Supervisor instructed me to upload my updated my legal name documents to Experian/upload. I uploaded my court order, my updated Social Security Card and my updated New York State License. After 3 business days I received an email that they have updated my Experian account to reflect my updated first name. I logged into my Experian app today as I do daily to check my credit report and it showed that I no longer have a FICO score. I called Experian customer service and received no help. I escalated the inquiry to an Experian Supervisor who told me they can't help me resolve the issue, that the creditors need report with my updated name. I have updated my name with all of my creditors and they have been reporting my legal name to Experian. I am XXXX XXXX XXXX and have worked hard to earn a good credit score of XXXX. I pay my bills on time every month. I need this problem rectified as soon as possible as it is causing issues with my ability to run my credit for purchases.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,NY,119XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/07/24,Closed with 