04/19/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Overcharged for something you did purchase with the card,"On Friday, XX/XX/XXXX at approximately XXXX I was walking with a friend in XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX near XXXX XXXX XXXX we had a few minutes to grab food before we had to catch a train home, and we stopped at a food cart/vendor called XXXXXXXX XXXX  ( XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ). Something we both immediately noticed was that there were no prices listed for the items pictured on his cart, but nonetheless the food smelled good and we ordered XXXX XXXX which the man said were {$6.00} each. 

Regretfully I was a XXXX XXXX and did not think to ask to see the screen ( I used the touch pay feature with XXXXXXXX XXXX ) or get a receipt or ANYTHING. It should have been {$12.00} but as we got closer to the train several blocks away, I received a notification that I was charged {$37.00} for these XXXX sandwiches! I did not sign for that, so this man mustve forged my name and signature. I had no choice but to get on my train or have to wait another hour for another and we simply couldnt. 

The following day I called my credit company Capital One and was told I needed to seek out this merchant to resolve the case in order to get refunded. After being persistent I was told they would credit me {$25.00} to cover what was added to the charge I initially expected, and informed me I would receive paperwork I needed to respond to within 7-10 business days. I never received this information, but instead I was sent a sort of resolution letter to my online banking app, which stated theyve closed the case and are charging me the full amount. Since I paid my credit bill in full on time, I definitely did pay this and it doesnt seem right or fair. I was essentially robbed, and Im sure this sort of pretense is commonplace for people who can not make it back to the city and investigate the whereabouts of a specific vendor cart.",None,CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION,NY,117XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/19/24,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8810990
