08/30/24,Debt collection,I do not know,Written notification about debt,Didn't receive notice of right to dispute,"Re : SPRING OAKS CAPITAL LLC XXXX To Whom It May Concern : I am writing in response to your response to my dispute on XXXX, regarding the alleged debt on the above-referenced account. I am formally requesting that you immediately cease all collection efforts on this account until you can provide conclusive proof that you complied with all relevant debt collection laws and regulations. 

Specifically, I demand that you provide evidence of the following : Proof of Mailing : Provide a copy of the actual letter you claim was mailed on XX/XX/2022, along with a certified mail receipt or other evidence demonstrating that it was sent to my correct address. 
Validation of Debt : Provide a detailed breakdown of the debt, including the original creditor, date of origination, amount owed, and any interest or fees accrued. 
Failure to provide this evidence within 30 days of the date of this letter will be considered a violation of the following laws : Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ) : Failure to provide validation of the debt within 30 days of my request. ( 15 U.S.C. 1692g ) Continuing collection efforts without providing proof of the initial communication and my right to dispute the debt. ( 15 U.S.C. 1692g ( a ) ) New York General Business Law 349 : Engaging in deceptive or misleading practices in the collection of consumer debts.

New York City Administrative Code 20-701 : Failure to provide notice of the consumer 's right to dispute the debt and request verification. 

Please be advised that if you continue collection efforts without providing the requested evidence, I will not hesitate to pursue all available legal remedies.",None,"Spring Oaks Capital, LLC",NY,11224,None,Consent provided,Web,08/30/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,9974682
