09/02/24,Debt collection,Credit card debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt is not yours,"I am lodging a formal complaint against Radius Global Solutions, XXXX ( Account Reference # XXXX ) for severe violations of my consumer rights. I requested debt validation under 12 CFR 1006.34 ( c ) ( 4 ) ( i ). Instead of complying with this legal requirement, Radius Global Solutions, LLC sent irrelevant verification documents that fail to meet the validation standards. This is a blatant attempt to mislead and deceive me. 

The company also unlawfully reported this account to credit bureaus without providing proper validation, violating 12 CFR 1006.34 ( b ) ( 5 ), 12 CFR 1006.34 ( d ), and 15 USC 1681s-2 ( 7 ) ( A ). These actions have damaged my credit report and financial standing. 

Furthermore, despite my explicit directive to cease all communication, Radius Global Solutions, XXXX has continued to contact me, egregiously violating FDCPA 1692K. This persistent harassment, combined with their failure to validate the debt, demonstrates a flagrant disregard for consumer protection laws. 

I demand the immediate removal of this account from my credit reports. Radius Global Solutions, LLCs actions are not only unlawful but also deceptive and harmful. I expect the CFPB to take swift and decisive action against these violations.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Radius Global Solutions LLC,NY,11435,None,Consent provided,Web,09/02/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9995512
03/11/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX, PA XXXX Experian XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, TX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, VA XXXX Subject : Dispute of Account # [ XXXX ] To Whom It May Concern, I am writing to formally dispute the accuracy of the information reported on my credit report by XXXX, Experian, and XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX regarding Account # [ XXXX ]. 

I have identified several inaccuracies regarding this account : XXXX. Discrepancy in Last Active Date : XXXX reports the last active date as XX/XX/XXXX. 
Experian reports the last active date as XX/XX/XXXX. 
This discrepancy raises concerns about the accuracy and validity of the reported information. 

XXXX. Discrepancy in Dates Opened : XXXX reports the date opened as XX/XX/XXXX. 
Experian reports the date opened as XX/XX/XXXX. 
These discrepancies further cast doubt on the accuracy of the reported account information. 

Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), I have the right to dispute inaccurate information on my credit report. Based on the discrepancies outlined above and my rights under the FCRA, I request that the account # [ XXXX ] be thoroughly investigated and removed from my consumer reports. 

Please conducte a comprehensive investigation into this matter and provide me with a written response detailing the actions taken to rectify the inaccuracies. 

I expect prompt action in resolving this matter and appreciate your attention to this dispute. 

