03/31/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am writing to file a formal complaint against XXXX XXXX  and XXXX XXXX XXXX regarding the misuse of my credit report, which violates federal laws and my consumer rights. 

I want to emphasize that I have already opted out previously from having my information reported, yet XXXX XXXX  and XXXX XXXX XXXX disregarded this opt-out and unlawfully reported information on my credit report, which is a clear violation of federal law and my rights. 

Furthermore, pursuant to 15 USC 1681 ( b ), which outlines permissible purposes for obtaining a consumer 's credit report, XXXX XXXX  and XXXX XXXX XXXX did not obtain my written consent to furnish any information on my credit report, nor did they provide me with the option to opt out. This is a direct violation of my rights under this federal law. 

Their actions also violate the Privacy Act of 1974, which mandates the protection of individuals ' personal information held by federal agencies and certain other organizations. By unlawfully reporting my information without my consent and ignoring my opt-out request, XXXX XXXX  and XXXX XXXX XXXX have infringed upon my privacy rights. 

Moreover, it is unlawful to report transaction history on a credit report without proper authorization, as stated in 16 CFR 313.7. This regulation prohibits the disclosure of sensitive personal information without the consumer 's consent, further highlighting the severity of these violations.

Additionally, 16 CFR 433.2, which addresses the preservation of consumer claims and defenses, is relevant in this context. This regulation ensures that consumers have the ability to assert their rights and defenses, including the right to dispute inaccurate or unauthorized information on their credit reports. 

I demand that XXXX XXXX  and XXXX XXXX XXXX immediately remove the inaccurate reporting from my credit report and update it to reflect that the debt is paid in full. Furthermore, I demand that they provide the following documents : the account lXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX, and XXXX XXXX XXXX Failure to provide these documents would indicate that they can not prove that anything is owed at all. 

Moreover, I want to highlight that XXXX XXXX  and XXXX XXXX XXXX have committed identity theft by mishandling my social security number, which is a serious violation of my privacy and security. 

Neither XXXX XXXX  XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX has the right to use the non-mailable addresses they have on file, and all communication must only be through the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ). 

Failure to comply with these demands may result in further legal action. I expect immediate action to rectify these violations and ensure that my consumer rights are upheld in the future.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11233,None,Consent provided,Web,03/31/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8660473
07/30/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account status incorrect,"My accounts was never late! I have had exceptional payment history with XXXX XXXX  and all payments were placed on Autopay. This late payment that is reporting is a result on a systematic error on their end processing my payment. 

This was clearly a billing error made my the company and is not a reflection of my payment experience which violates USC Code 1681eb. This error has caused severe hard to my XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX 

I demand the late payment reported to be removed/updated. 

They are not in compliance with the following law. 15 USC 1666b and its requirements set the standards and the guidance for a creditor to treat a payment as late, yet they are reporting a payment as late and they did not comply with the law! 

15 USC 1666b ( a ) Time to make payments A creditor may not treat a payment on a credit card account under an open end consumer credit plan as late for any purpose, unless the creditor has adopted reasonable procedures designed to ensure that each periodic statement including the information required by section 1637 ( b ) of this title is mailed or delivered to the consumer not later than 21 days before the payment due date. 

I have requested proof that this information was mailed or delivered 21 days before the payment due date and this information was requested in good faith pursuant rule 1002 and It was never provided. 

This is unfair, illegal, fraudulent, and not equitable to me as a consumer!",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,11420,None,Consent provided,Web,07/30/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,9663686
