08/28/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Deposits and withdrawals,"I opened a checking account with Capital One lately and I received my first direct deposit from an employer. When I go to my banking phone app I notice something that says : Your funds are currently not available for withdrawal. please call us at XXXX. 

I called the number and spoke to an agent and the agent told me to go a Capital One branch. I went to a branch and the asks me for my ID, I provided my Employment Authorization Card which I used to open the account in the first place. The agent told me to provide another form of ID, and he asked me specifically for my password. On the next day, I came back to the bank with my passport. I met with another agent who asked me for my Social Security Card and I was upset and asked why they didnt asked me that yesterday. I came back to my place and bring back my social security card some minutes later. I met with another agent to whom I handed my Social Security card. She called on the phone multiple times, I waited for a long time just for the agent to let me know that my Social Security is so new that they had a hard time verifying it, and that was the reason they placed restrictions on my account. The agent couldnt provide a timeframe for the investigation. So I went out with the issues not resolved still. 

After some days, I called Capital several times only for them to tell me that they are still investigating. Last Monday, which was the XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX I opened a checking account with another bank, and they didnt have any hard time verifying my social security. Today I called Capital One again, and they still investigating and I asked for details and they couldnt provide any details about the investigation. 

I being this was enough and I decided to file this complaint. Today I told the Capital One agent that I dont want any account with them anymore, I just need my money and close the account. The agent told me that I have to wait until they finish their investigation for that. This is frustrating and I want my money.",None,CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION,NY,11550,None,Consent provided,Web,08/28/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,9948385
04/03/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am sending this correspondence to address significant concerns regarding the accuracy of my credit report Your failure to positively verify these accounts has hurt my ability to obtain credit. Under the FCRA, unverifiable accounts must be removed and if you are unable to provide me a copy of verifiable proof, you must delete immediately the account accounts listed below. 
Pursuant to the FCRA, a consumer report does not include any report containing information solely about transactions or experiences between the consumer and the person making the report. Any reporting of late payments or derogatory statuses is a direct violation of 15 USC 1681a ( d ) ( 1 ) as that information pertains to experiences any continuation of providing negative information required by section FCRA 605B ( 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ) a copy of which is enclosed which states that this information must be removed within four business days of receipt, I am requesting that the adverse information on the items be removed to correct my credit report. 

Please investigate these matters and remove the disputed items as soon as possible.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11694,None,Consent provided,Web,04/03/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8691995
08/28/24,Debt collection,Telecommunications debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt is not yours,"XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Source Receivables Management XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  Subject : Dispute of Debt and Request for Verification under 15 U.S.C. 1692g Dear Source Receivables Management, I am writing to formally dispute the debt referenced in your communications, related to the account ending in XXXX with a balance of {$120.00}, allegedly owed to XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX I do not recognize this debt and believe it to be invalid. Pursuant to 15 U.S.C. 1692g of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ), I request that you provide the following : Verification of the Debt : Detailed information proving that the debt is valid, including a copy of the original contract or agreement that shows I am responsible for this debt.

Account History : A complete accounting of the debt, including the original amount, any payments made, and any fees or interest that have been added. 
Proof of Ownership : Documentation that proves Source Receivables Management has the legal right to collect this debt. 
Creditor Information : The name and address of the original creditor to whom the debt was owed. 
As required by law, I request that this debt be marked as disputed on my credit report until the matter is resolved. Additionally, if you can not verify the debt, I request that you immediately cease any further collection activities and have the debt removed from my credit report. 

Please provide the requested documentation within 30 days of receipt of this letter. If you can not provide sufficient verification, I demand that you remove all information regarding this debt from my credit report and confirm in writing that this has been done. 

Failure to comply with this request will result in me filing complaints with the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ), the Federal Trade Commission ( FTC ), and my states Attorney Generals office, as well as pursuing legal remedies available to me. 

Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX",None,Source Receivables Management LLC,NY,11385,None,Consent provided,Web,08/28/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9950330
