04/03/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"Dear Sir/Madam, I am writing to dispute certain information in my credit file identified during a recent review of my credit report. The details I am disputing are not accurate and reflect inconsistencies that could impact my creditworthiness negatively. Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act, 15 U.S.C. 1681 ( e ) ( b ), I request an investigation into these inaccuracies to ensure my credit report reflects only accurate and verifiable information. 

The specific inaccuracies I am disputing are as follows : Original Lender Name Inconsistency : My credit report lists the original lender as Progressive with XXXX and XXXX but XXXX XXXX with TransUnion. This discrepancy may lead to confusion or the appearance of multiple debts instead of one. I request that this information be corrected to uniformly reflect the accurate original lender name across all three credit reports. 

XXXX XXXX XXXX : The collection agency handling my account is listed differently across the three credit bureausthis inconsistency could imply incorrect reporting of the collection account. The correct name of the collection agency should be uniformly reported by all three bureaus. Please investigate and update this information to accurately reflect the collection agency handling this account. 

Status Descriptions Variability : The status of my debt varies significantly across the reports, from Unpaid to Collection account to an extensive description on XXXX. This variation could mislead credit grantors about the true nature of the debt. I request a review and uniform update of the status description to ensure it accurately represents the status of my account. 

Enclosed are copies of documents supporting my position and highlighting the discrepancies for your review. Please note, I am not requesting the information be deleted if it is accurate, but rather that an investigation be conducted to verify its accuracy. 

I understand under the Fair Credit Reporting Act, you have 30 days to complete an investigation of the items I have disputed and to provide me with the results in writing. If the information is found to be inaccurate, the law requires you to correct it or delete it from my file. 

Thank you for your attention to this matter. I look forward to your prompt response. 

Sincerely,",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,10465,None,Consent provided,Web,04/03/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8677029
