11/04/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Closing your account,Company closed your account,"Subject : Request for 1099-C Form Account Charged Off To Whom It May Concern, I am writing regarding an account that appears on my credit report under your companys name and is marked as a charge off. This indicates that you reported this balance to the IRS as income due to cancellation of debt. Pursuant to this status, I am formally requesting a copy of IRS Form 1099-C ( Cancellation of Debt ) for my records.

On my credit report, it is indicated that this account has been charged off, suggesting that the debt has been canceled and reported as such to the IRS. If this is correct, a Form 1099-C should have been filed and provided to both me and the IRS as required by law. Please provide me with a copy of this 1099-C form, as this is necessary for my tax records. 

If you do not provide this form or can not substantiate that this account was properly reported to the IRS, I will consider taking legal action for statutory damages and potential fraud. Failure to provide accurate documentation may be a violation of both federal tax law and credit reporting standards.

Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter. I look forward to receiving the requested documentation within 15 days.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,XXXXX,None,Consent provided,Web,11/04/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,10682858
