09/05/24,"Payday loan, title loan, personal loan, or advance loan",Installment loan,Problem when making payments,None,"In XXXX I made 2 payments on my RV Loan each for {$530.00}. After I made the second payment in error, I contacted M & T to reverse the 2nd payment and have it sent back to me via check. A couple of weeks went by and I never received the check. I called back and was told that it was still on its way and to call back the following week. The second week of XXXX I contacted M & T again as I still had not received the check. They stated oh it must be lost and we can send the funds back to my bank via ACH. I provided them all of the necessary information. About a week later I still had not received my funds so they said they would submit the request again. Finally on XX/XX/19 I received a credit of {$530.00} back into my checking account. At that point I assumed that everything was all set. Approximately the first week of XXXX i received a call from M & T collections alerting me that my XXXX payment was past due. I said how is that possible as M & T has an autosweep set up to take the payment out of my checking account which i confirmed that the funds were taken from my checking account and applied to the XXXX payment. They explained that the XXXX payment was reversed. I asked why the XXXX payment was reversed and they said it was was to provide the credit back to me. I said the XXXX payment should have NEVER been reversed as the credit should have been made from the payment dated XXXX. After dozens of phone calls trying to explain my situation to each person that answered the phone, I was able to get the XXXX payment credited as expected. Given the issues I wanted to make sure the XXXX payment was made correctly which as of XX/XX/XXXX, I saw that the payment was satisfied and assumed the loan was back to where it should be. The first week of XXXX I received a call from M & T collections stating that i was 32 days past due. I went into my online banking and saw that they reversed my XXXX payment AGAIN. I was confused as 2 payments were made in XXXX one was reversed and the other was made to satisfy my XXXX payment. As this point M & T still owes me one payment of {$530.00} and they reversed additional payments that should have never been reversed. At this point M & T still has {$530.00} of my funds that they should be using to credit my loan payment to bring my payment up to date.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,M&T BANK CORPORATION,NY,14626,None,Consent provided,Web,09/05/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,10029256
