06/01/24,Vehicle loan or lease,Lease,Incorrect information on your report,Account status incorrect,"I recently noticed a negative remark on my credit report indicating that a payment was missed. However, I was never alerted or notified about this late payment before it appeared on my credit report. The SAME day it appeared on my credit report, I called into Kia to inquire about what happened. I then made all alleged late payments owed to make my account current with Kia.

As a diligent and responsible customer, I rely on timely notifications to manage my payments effectively. I never received any indication that the times I logged into the online portal to make my payments like I have been since XX/XX/year> that the payments were not properly applied to my account as expected. The lack of such communication from your end is a significant concern. 

I understand that maintaining accurate and up-to-date records is essential for both parties. Therefore, I trust that you will investigate this matter promptly and make the necessary adjustments to my account and credit report. I am confident that this is an isolated incident and hope to continue our relationship based on mutual trust and timely communication. 

I have NEVER been 30 days late with ANY of my accounts in all my XXXX years being a consumer. This negative reporting to the credit bureaus caused me significant personal harm including an XXXX point DROP to my credit scores, downgrading my credit status from "" XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX '' across all 3 bureaus and most importantly this mistake caused my daughters student loan application to be denied as I am her only qualified cosigner. 

This mistake has cause significant financial harm to my family. The effects of this mistaken negative reporting will cause financial and emotional strain on my family that will be felt for generations if this is not corrected immediately. My daughter wants to attend college. I have ALWAYS been extremely diligent about maintaining exceptional credit as I knew I would need to use my credit to send my children to college one day. 

As you can see from the document attached I had EXCEPTIONAL credit until this was reported to the bureaus on XX/XX/XXXX which is the same date I called into kia to find out what happened and also made payments customer service said were not applied to my account properly. 

Please acknowledge receipt of this letter and inform me of the steps being taken to resolve this issue. I appreciate your prompt attention to this matter and look forward to your response. 

Thank you for your understanding and cooperation.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,HYUNDAI CAPITAL AMERICA,NY,10471,None,Consent provided,Web,06/01/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9155028
