09/13/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"Dispute : XXXX with Chase Bank for British Airways Credit Card ending in XXXX British Airways charged me multiple times for the same trip, and they claimed that the bank did not release the funds and would not allow me to finish my journey unless I repaid the ticket. Chase refused to refund me for the extra cost. I ended up being charged XXXX for XXXX ticket, and I had to pay twice due to Chase Banks neglect. 

On XX/XX/year>, I booked XXXX single round trip flight going from New York to XXXX ( Booking reference XXXX ) for {$890.00}. 

Confirmed by transaction for payment for the ticket : XXXX on XX/XX/XXXX. 

I noticed that Chase Bank/British Airways had charged me twice for {$890.00}, so I called the bank to dispute the charge, and the duplicate charge was refunded back. 

On XXXX XXXX, I paid my credit card bill for {$1000.00}, which paid for the ticket. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, the first leg of the flight was taken without any issues. British Airways did not contact me or alert me of any payment issues, in fact, they sent me emails to wish me a good journey, and the first leg was completed. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, while attempting to take the second leg of the trip from XXXX, I was informed by British Airways that the Bank did not pay for the ticket, and therefore, they would not issue a ticket unless the ticket was repaid in British Pounds of 737.11 which equaled to {$930.00}. This {$930.00} charge is the only payment that British Airways has for this ticket. Where did the original {$890.00} go?

I would like my charge of {$890.00} back, and Chase refuses to acknowledge where this money has gone, and British Airways claims that the only payment they have for my ticket is the {$930.00} which I was charged at the desk. When I asked Chase, they said the time to handle this dispute had in fact expired despite the fact that this whole scenario has taken time between British Airways and Chase both refusing to help, despite this being something they that caused. They charged me twice for {$890.00}, XXXX was cancelled, but I have no idea where the other charge has gone, it's essentially in a XXXX hole, and British Airways do not have the funds either..

British Airways was more helpful than Chase Bank, they just have taken our funds and said too bad because time is expired our funds our lost. There is no accountability from this bank. I don't understand as this was a British Airways Chase Credit Card, yet both institutions are completely neglectful.

They charged me twice for one ticket, refused to pay British Airways for the ticket I used the card for despite making payment, and due to this, I had to repay again to use a ticket in a very stressful situation. 


Thank you, XXXX XXXX",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,105XX,None,Consent provided,Web,09/13/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,10116921
