03/09/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"In my capacity as President of XXXX XXXX XXXX, a New York XXXX entity in good standing, I took out a {$40000.00} business loan from XXXX ( XXXX ). I was removed a few months later from my position at XXXX XXXX. 

XXXX began contacting me via email and phone calls to both myself and family members telling me the loan was not being paid back. I provided XXXX with the best contact info for the person at XXXX XXXX XXXX who could assist them in resolving the issue. 

XXXX claims I signed a personal guarantee and that I am responsible for the business loan. This is false. I would never sign a personal guarantee for a business loan because I would never want to be placed in this exact situation. I asked them to provide me with a copy of the personal guarantee. They failed to provide me a copy because no such copy exists because I never signed a personal guarantee. 

XXXX is now reporting to the credit bureaus that I personally owe {$40000.00}. I have tried contacting the credit bureaus but they intentionally make it impossible to speak or email or contact them electronically. I tried calling the numbers they provide but I receive an automatic recording to file a dispute online. I try creating an account online to file the dispute but I get a message saying I must call them. It's a similar game many other companies play in order to avoid providing customer service. 

Please advise how I can remove this fraudulent debt from my personal credit score.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10023,None,Consent provided,Web,03/09/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8511876
