09/09/24,Checking or savings account,Other banking product or service,Closing an account,Funds not received from closed account,"Dear CFPB, I am writing to reopen my complaint against Clover-Fiserv due to their continuous and unjustified actions against my business over the past nine months. My previous complaint ID was XXXX, which you closed without a resolution. 

The reason for reopening this complaint is that Clover-Fiserv has been repeating the same tactics without providing any resolution. In my previous complaint, Clover-Fiserv requested various documents and data from us, which we already provided eight months ago. After submitting all the required information, we were informed that our funds would be released after 90 days, which ended on XX/XX/year>. 

After the 90-day period, despite numerous attempts to contact Clover-Fiserv via phone and email, we received no meaningful response. When we did get a reply, we were told, "" Your funds will never be released for an infinite time period. '' Upon asking for a reason, they simply stated, "" No further details provided. '' Now, in response to our CFPB complaint, they are again asking for the same data we already submitted and have created a new case number. This is a repeated tactic they have used to delay and avoid fulfilling their obligations. What does this new case number mean? Are we expected to submit all the information again only to receive the same non-response : "" Your funds will never be released ''? 

We started our business, and within just two weeks, Clover-Fiserv ruined our operations by closing our accounts and holding our funds. If they are claiming the funds will never be released, what are they planning to do with our money? They have no right to indefinitely hold or keep our funds. 

We will now take every possible step to expose Clover-Fiserv for their actions. We will publicly share our experience on every platform available and seek legal action to recover our funds and address the financial and mental stress they have caused us.

The data they are asking for now is the same data they requested eight months ago, and I have attached the previous correspondence for your review. Please assess this matter and judge for yourself who is in the right and who is not.

We urgently need your assistance and intervention to resolve this issue and prevent Clover-Fiserv from continuing to abuse their position. 

Thank you for your attention to this matter. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX.",None,FISERV INC.,NY,11590,None,Consent provided,Web,09/09/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,10054841
