07/03/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Other features, terms, or problems",Problem with rewards from credit card,"I have been an Amazon XXXX/Chase credit card customer since XXXX ( maybe prior since the statements only go back that far. When I signed up for this credit card I was promised 5 % cash back on orders from XXXX which was fulfilled until XX/XX/XXXX. At this point the card reverted to earning 3 % back which is what card owners get if they are not an Amazon XXXX member. However, my membership status never changed and neither did the payments for it via this Chase credit card. I recently only noticed this was happening and called Amazon immediately who updated my account on their end so that I can earn the proper rewards points going forward. They saw exactly what I did and confirmed I should have been receiving 5 % the last 5 years. They told me to call Chase who I have now spoken to several times with no resolution or explanation for why they will not honor the terms of the credit card agreement I signed. 

Even on Chase 's end when I call ; the employees can see my XXXX membership payments on my statements each year and acknowledged the same thing Amazon did. However, when I contacted them via their secure message system they just would deny my request and not give an explanation. Furthermore they would just reiterate the terms of the agreement ( all of which I have met ). 

This has cost me hundreds of dollars potentially in cash back I was promised. As far as I am concerned Chase is in breach of the contract I signed.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11758,None,Consent provided,Web,07/03/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9412150
