04/19/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Problem using a debit or ATM card,"On XX/XX/2024, I was at the XXXX outdoor food festival in XXXX when XXXX high schoolers approached me asking for donations for their basketball team. When stating I didn't have any cash but wanted to donate anyway, one of them offered to input the information in my XXXX for the transaction ( I acknowledge that this was a grave mistake, but at the moment I felt no need to be suspicious of these kids ). When returning me phone, everything seemed normal, but days later I saw that they'd transferred {$2500.00} into an account that has since then been closed, so I'm unable to retrieve those funds from the recipient. I opened a case with the XXXX, who state that this is a modality of scam that has had an increase in the past 6 months. My bank disputed my claim because my login history reveals that I was "" responsible '' for the transaction. While I did log into the banking app, this is a transaction that was made criminally and against my will, having been taken advantage of by these scammers. I reached out to the recipient, who claims to have also been a victim of these people, who supposedly hacked her account and used it for this specific crime. The XXXX backs my claims of having been scammed and has filed this case as XXXX XXXX.",None,CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION,NY,11215,None,Consent provided,Web,04/19/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8808903
