04/23/24,Mortgage,FHA mortgage,Trouble during payment process,"Escrow, taxes, or insurance","I closed on my home on XX/XX/XXXX. I closed with my employer at the time who was ( XXXX XXXX XXXX ). Approximately 120 days later they made a significant cut in my salary $ XXXX ). Did they know this would be taking place and didn't inform me prior to closing? 

Then in XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX I was notified that my property was reassessed for property taxes due to the property changing hands. I knew it may increase but i had no idea it could quadruple. 

I recently was notified by my mortgage servicing company ( Pennymac ) that my escrow account had undergone an escrow shortage analysis. My mortgage payment has increased from {$2700.00} to {$3500.00}. I have to cover the shortage AND pay an additional 20 % padding OR I can come out of pocket $ XXXX + by the end of this month. 

Here is my question... how does any of this satisfy the XXXX? 

If the ability to pay a monthly mortgage obligation includes "" expected property taxes "". 

THE KEY WORD BEING "" EXPECTED '' See Below : XXXX. Monthly mortgage-related obligations. These obligations include expected property taxes, fees and special assessments imposed by a condominium, cooperative, or homeowners association, ground rent, certain lease payments, and certain insurance premiums and similar charges that are required by the creditor. See 12 CFR 1026.43 ( b ) ( 8 ) and related commentary.

How many other homebuyers has this happened to?",None,"PENNYMAC LOAN SERVICES, LLC.",NY,117XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/23/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8841850
