03/28/24,"Payday loan, title loan, personal loan, or advance loan",Installment loan,Getting the loan,None,"On XX/XX/XXXX I received financing for a surgical procedure in the amount of {$10000.00}. The receipt I received via email stated your "" XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX is confirmed '' Your contract reference is XXXX. Lender : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. Loan Servicer : Cherry Servicing , LLC XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Phone Number : XXXX. I made my first payment of {$260.00} on XX/XX/24 before I saw the surgeon. Once I saw the surgeon he declined to do the procedure. The surgeon is XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Phone number : XXXX. The procedure did not take place and I notified the servicing company in writing that I would not need the loan and to please cancel it. I did this immediately, the very next day. They responded to me in writing via email and stated "" to request a refund, please contact the practice where you used Cherry to make a purchase. We defer to the refund policies put in place by our partner practices and can not initiate a refund without their approval ''. This is insane to me because I didn't have the surgery. The practice didn't take out the loan, I did. I feel as if they should have verified that the procedure was cancelled and then cancel the loan asap. The next payment is due to come out of my account on XX/XX/XXXX. This means I will be paying for a loan on a surgery that I never had. I want this loan canceled immediately and my money refunded.",None,CHERRY TECHNOLOGIES INC.,NY,10027,None,Consent provided,Web,03/28/24,Closed with explanation,No,N/A,8648863
05/31/24,Credit card,Store credit card,Trouble using your card,Can't use card to make purchases,"On XX/XX/year>, I applied and was approved for a Raymour and Flanigan credit card issued by TD Bank. Though I did not receive the card, I was able to place an initial order for bedroom furniture and a special order for additional bedroom furniture. Once the first order was delivered on XX/XX/year>, I was charged the amount of {$3200.00}. However, with the special order still pending, I realized I never received my actual credit card. On XX/XX/year>, I called TD Bank to inquire as to the status of my new card. I was told it had been shipped on XX/XX/XXXX. The representative asked if I had moved and I said I was about to move into a new home. So I asked if I could change my address so that the card could be sent to the new home. The representative said the would need to send me a text message to verify my identity. When they went to whatever verification software they were using, according to multiple representatives and supervisors, my telephone number came up as unverified. Thus, unbeknownst to me, that caused my account to be suspended. When my special order came in to the local XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, I was contacted by a manager there, XXXX, to say that my account was frozen and that I needed to contact TD Bank to get it resolved. Well, eight phone calls and three supervisors later, it has not been resolved. All I kept being told was I need to contact the credit bureaus to get my phone number added to my credit report. I checked all three credit bureau reports and they contained my telephone number. However, my account remains frozen, with the representatives at TD Bank offering no resolution. I remain in limbo.",None,TD BANK US HOLDING COMPANY,NY,10940,None,Consent provided,Web,05/31/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9145286
04/04/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"I am sending this correspondence to address significant concerns regarding the accuracy of my credit report Your failure to positively verify these accounts has hurt my ability to obtain credit. Under the FCRA, unverifiable accounts must be removed and if you are unable to provide me a copy of verifiable proof, you must delete immediately the account accounts listed below. 
Pursuant to the FCRA, a consumer report does not include any report containing information solely about transactions or experiences between the consumer and the person making the report. Any reporting of late payments or derogatory statuses is a direct violation of 15 USC 1681a ( d ) ( 1 ) as that information pertains to experiences any continuation of providing negative information required by section FCRA 605B ( 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ) a copy of which is enclosed which states that this information must be removed within four business days of receipt, I am requesting that the adverse information on the items be removed to correct my credit report.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,11203,None,Consent provided,Web,04/04/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8686413
