08/09/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Personal information incorrect,"I am writing to express my deep frustration and serious concerns regarding the accuracy of my personal information on file with your esteemed institution. While reviewing my credit report, I was appalled to discover discrepancies that have raised significant doubts about the completeness and accuracy of my records. Specifically, there are inconsistencies in my identification, Social Security number, and proof of address, all of which I have enclosed within this correspondence for your comprehensive examination. I respectfully urge you to thoroughly investigate this issue and promptly take the necessary steps to rectify any inaccuracies and update my personal information accurately and expeditiously. Your cooperation and assistance in this matter are crucial to maintaining my faith and trust in your institution. 

Your agency is in violation of the law! According to 15 U.S.C. 1681 Section 602 ( a ), I have the right to privacy. Additionally, 15 U.S.C. 1681 Section 604 ( a ) ( 2 ) states that a consumer reporting agency can not furnish an account without my written consent. Furthermore, 15 U.S.C. 1681c ( a ) ( 5 ) specifies that no consumer reporting agency may include any adverse information in a consumer report, other than records of convictions of crimes, that is older than seven years. 

Under 15 U.S.C. 1681s-2 ( a ) ( 1 ), it is stated that a person shall not furnish any information related to a consumer to a consumer reporting agency if they know or have reasonable cause to believe that the information is inaccurate. 

Delete this information immediately!",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10023,None,Consent provided,Web,08/09/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,9758795
