03/07/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"Experian report currently shows balance on my credit card account. Balance was already paid but this is not reflected and won't be until following month. Credit score ( calculated each month ) was lowered significantly from score previous month due to relatively large balance versus available credit. Lowered score may affect my ability to secure loans, force me to pay higher interest rates, etc.

I pay credit cards off in full each month and have never had to pay interest. The algorithm and timing of credit score calculation doesn't accurately show my credit history.

The Experian algorithm seems to be focused on being an early warning system rather than reflecting my longstanding, highly responsible and accountable credit history. I think this shows Experian needs to rethink their approach and tailor the report to the individual so it accurately reflects credit history and behavior.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,NY,121XX,Older American,Consent provided,Web,03/07/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8493627
