05/06/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Problem with a lender or other company charging your account,Money was taken from your account on the wrong day or for the wrong amount,"Chase Processors has improperly and perhaps fraudulently removed money from my company 's checking account. XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX XXXX. We make use of a website, XXXX to sell product and provide customers a way to pay for their purchases with credit card. Chase performs the processing of the credit card transactions, for which they charge a base price of XXXX cents per transaction, or attempted transaction ( in the case where a submitted card for purchase has been denied ). On XX/XX/2024 my website was, unbeknownst to me, inundated in the background by a flood of attempted credit card purchases, the vast majority of which were denied, which persisted until XX/XX/2024. A rogue operation were testing a list of stolen credit card numbers on my website without my knowledge to see which were approved and still usable, a well known type of scam that Chase should have been aware of. On XX/XX/2024 Chase Processing deducted {$15000.00} from my account for their services for the month of XXXX. I was shocked. Historically, they have never deducted more than around {$300.00} for any month for their services. I became aware of the {$15000.00} deduction on XX/XX/XXXX when I logged into my checking account to pay bills. I called them immediately for an explanation. They said they were charging XXXX cents per transaction for over XXXX transactions that month. Chase is a huge, sophisticated operation. It is impossible that their tools and systems did not immediately detect a huge spike, amounting to a MULTIPLE OF AT LEAST A THOUSAND TIMES, over what my website customarily, and historically does. Plain common sense should have recognized that there was a bad actor at work. They breached their fiduciary obligation to me in two ways. They have among their tools the means to immediately put an end to the type of fraud that was occurring, but chose to do nothing, allowing charge after charge and fee after fee to continue for almost a full month. Neither did they alert me as to what was going on. I do not think that this, at minimum gross negligence, verging on complicity was without design. It reaped for them a {$15000.00} plus ill-gained windfall at the expense of a customer to whom they have fiduciary responsibility. If as I suspect this conduct of theirs extends across their whole system, there have probably been millions of dollars pillaged by them from small businesses in the most deceitful way. I request that you hold them to account.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11691,None,Consent provided,Web,05/08/24,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8943565
