06/14/24,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",Virtual currency,Other service problem,None,"I transferred money from my bank account to Kraken XXXX app. I was able to convert some currency from USD to XXXX and send it to a friend. Then I transferred another XXXX $ USD to Kraken and send a larger sum. This conversion we allowed but the sending of the XXXX was denied and i was told to contact support. Support escalated my claim ( Request number XXXX ) and i was contacted via email that my account was being closed without explanation. I requested information as to why the account was being closed numerous times and each time i was told that i cant be given the information as to why the account was closed due to "" security reasons ''. They would not clarify further or show any security reasoning why i couldn't be told them. They closed my account but before the account was closed i was permitted to convert all of my money back to USD and send it back to my bank account. There were service/conversion fees involved in the transfers that i was NOT refunded and since i wasnt permitted to use their app/services to send money i feel this was a fraudulent account closes and they profited from the fees being charged. I would like to request an explanation why my account was closed or the exact security reasons why i couldnt be told this information. I would also like the fees refunded as the services were not rendered.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Payward Ventures Inc. dba Kraken,NY,10304,None,Consent provided,Web,06/14/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9264161
06/26/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Trouble using your card,Can't use card to make purchases,"I am filing a complaint against American Express Credit Card Services under unfair practices used on consumer credit card holders. I believe the company unfairly reduced my credit limit after asking for a random fee to be paid to leave the limit at the current level. This left my card basically maxed out instead of having over {$6000.00} in available credit. 

On XX/XX/XXXX I paid off my credit card account balance in full in order to reinstate my spending privileges. Prior to XX/XX/XXXX I was in a payment program to paydown the balance with the agreement that once paid in full I would regain full access to the credit card. 

The credit card was restored to a limit of {$9300.00} and once again I began using the card and making all payments on time. I made a payment of {$200.00} on XX/XX/XXXX for the XXXX invoice which had a minimum payment due of {$65.00}. On XX/XX/XXXX, I received an email from American Express stating that unless I paid an additional of {$950.00} by XX/XX/XXXX they would review the account to reduce my credit limit and that I would have interrupted use of my card until the review was complete. There was a {$0.00} balance due at this point as I had already made my monthly payment and my available balance online still showed the limit of {$9300.00}. 

Then when I went to check into my hotel that day the {$100.00} charge was declined. I messaged American Express and they told me they could make sure the {$100.00} would authorize but could not tell me anything further about the review or why my limit would be reduced and that my account still showed the {$9300.00}. 
On XX/XX/XXXX I received another email from American Express stating that my credit limit had been reduced from {$9300.00} to {$4300.00} which left me with an available credit limit of {$500.00}. Instead of having an available limit of over {$6000.00} now the card is basically maxed out for any other creditor reviewing my report. 

