09/05/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account status incorrect,"In XX/XX/XXXX Affirm reported me as being late to XXXX on a loan I had taken out in XXXX of XXXX. The report simply stated that I was past due XXXX dollars without giving any other account information. This reporting was erroneous, as I had previously paid the past due amount earlier in the month. The account was paid off on XX/XX/XXXX. I promptly submitted a dispute with XXXX in XXXX of XXXX. Within several days the dispute results returned as verified. Between the periods of XXXX XX/XX/XXXX, Affirm continued to report me late to XXXX XXXX despite the account being paid off and closed. During this time period, 13 different disputes were made with XXXX regarding this issue. In each instance, XXXX "" verified '' the information without making any necessary adjustments. In one instance, XXXX "" verified '' the information and sent me the results within 15 minutes. It is unclear how a proper investigation could be conducted in a period of 15 minutes. 
During the period of XXXX XX/XX/XXXX, multiple certified letters were sent to both XXXX and Affirm regarding this account. The letters clearly stated that I was disputing the accuracy of this reporting based on the account being paid off, and it being continually reported as late. Each correspondence was received, as I received a return receipt for each letter sent. Additionally, I spoke to several employees at XXXX who stated to me they were continuing to receive updates from Affirm that the account was late. Also, Affirm sent me several "" escalation '' emails that did not address my issue, but instead, simply stated my requests were denied. After a complaint iwth the CFPB in XXXX of XXXX, XXXX updated the account to paid. However, the account is still showing as past due and paid off at the same time, and remains a "" derrogatory '' item in XXXX reporting system.",None,"Affirm Holdings, Inc",NY,117XX,None,Consent provided,Web,09/05/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,10028875
