09/15/24,Vehicle loan or lease,Loan,Managing the loan or lease,Problem with fees charged,"Subject : Urgent Complaint Regarding Unethical Financial Practices Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, I am writing to formally express my dissatisfaction and concern regarding an experience I had XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX dealership. On XX/XX/year>, I placed an order for a brand-new XXXX  XXXX XXXX XXXX. The dealer quoted me a vehicle price of {$57000.00}, with a subtotal of {$57000.00}, sales tax of {$5000.00} ( 8.875 % ), and a processing fee of {$170.00}. The total amount due on delivery was {$62000.00}. 

On XX/XX/year>, I was informed that my vehicle was ready for pickup and final documentation. The sales representative advised me to provide a down payment of {$8000.00}. However, I indicated that I wished to pay the full amount in cash via a certified check. When I arrived at the dealership, I was advised to finance the purchase. Despite having {$70000.00} available, I was told by Business Manager XXXX XXXX that I could only pay {$50000.00} in cash and would need to finance the remaining balance due to dealership policy. 

XXXX XXXX assured me that financing {$50000.00} would result in a favorable interest rate, and I would only need to make one payment initially. He claimed that the interest rate would not significantly impact me, and I would be able to pay off the remaining balance in XXXX. I was directed to obtain a certified check for {$50000.00} from a nearby XXXX XXXX, which I did. 

When I returned to the dealership, XXXX XXXX presented me with paperwork, congratulated me on the financing terms, and explained that my credit score of XXXX would not result in a substantial financial impact due to the favorable terms. He wrote down that my monthly payment would be {$440.00}, and I signed the documents in good faith. 

Upon reviewing the documents at home, I was shocked to discover that the finance charge fee amounted to {$7900.00}, with an annual percentage rate of 9.70 %. The total amount of credit was listed as {$24000.00}, and the total payment over the term of the loan was {$31000.00}. This resulted in a total sale price of {$81000.00}, when the initial total amount due on delivery was {$62000.00}. 

It appears I have been misled and pressured into taking an unnecessary loan, incurring an excessive finance charge. I feel that I have been a victim of unethical practices by XXXX XXXX and the dealership. 

I request immediate assistance in resolving this matter. I seek a thorough review of my case and a correction of the finance terms to reflect the true cost of the vehicle. I appreciate your prompt attention to this serious issue. 

Thank you, Vehicle XXXX XXXX",None,TOYOTA MOTOR CREDIT CORPORATION,NY,11223,None,Consent provided,Web,09/18/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,10131329
