04/04/24,Checking or savings account,Savings account,Managing an account,Funds not handled or disbursed as instructed,"On XX/XX/2024, a total of {$130000.00} was wired out of my bank accounts with Chase Bank in New York without my authorization. I never send wires for more than a few XXXX dollars. I was not notified or warned by Chase. Usually they send an email advising when a wire transfer is made. This did not happen. I was the victim of a scam. However, I did not disclose any information as the scammers were already inside my account. All I did was provide a verification code. Chase subsequently closed the online access to my account and I had to set up a new username and password. To my immense horror, Chase had no interest in pursuing a serious investigation. Apparently the other banks who received the funds were also not interested in following up. Chase has insurance, they could reimburse me but they won't. I have no recourse. Their only response were some messages uploaded to my bank account online. The indifference and callousness is glaring. Their flimsy security systems allowed this fraud to occur and now they have no liability? Whatever is in the fine print which, let 's face it, you have to sign if you want to open a bank account, should not PROTECT them from liability. They must refund stolen funds to innocent clients and must devise better protection. They failed to alert me. At the age of XXXX, I have lost a huge amount of money. Further, XXXX, with whom I have had an account for years, is not responding to my CLAIM. I HAVE SPENT HOURS TRYING TO GET THROUGH TO SOMEONE HOW CAN HELP ME TO NO AVAIL.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,10025,Older American,Consent provided,Web,04/04/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8700645
