07/31/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I have read my credit report and I see an inaccurate and unlawful account. It has several late payments which are erroneous. The information listed is not aligned whit the other bureaus. This is a big violation of FCRA, please verify these late payments that you claim I did commit. SEND ME documents such as contracts, billing statements, signed agreements and the representatives you spoke whit who verified it WITH AN affidavit. If the requested documents are not met. Please remove these erroneous and unlawful late payments on my payment history like Equifax did.

I DID MY RESEARCH AND HERE ARE THE LAWS YOU ARE VIOLATING : 15 U.S. Code ss 1681e ( b ), it's crucial that consumer reporting agencies take reasonable steps to ensure the highest possible accuracy of the information concerning an individual in their reports.

15 U.S. Code ss 1681 e ( b ), it is stated that when a consumer reporting agency prepares a consumer report, it must follow reasonable procedures to ensure the highest possible accuracy of the information concerning the individual.

I am fully aware the under 15 U.S. Code ss 1681i ( 5 ), it is stipulated that if, after a reinvestigation, any disputed information is found to be inaccurate, incomplete, or unverifiable, the consumer reporting agency must promptly delete or modify that information accordingly and notify the information furnisher of the changes.

15 U.S. Code 1681s-2, specifically, the Responsibilities of furnishers of information to consumer reporting agencies, it is noted that within 30 days, you did not properly indicate that this account was under dispute, thereby resulting in a violation of this provision.

15 U.S. Code 1682n ( b ) civil liability of a natural person I've been violated.

My disputes are detailed and directly related to the accounts in question. A template response WILL NOT BE an acceptable response. If, within 15 days after your investigation, you are unable to provide me with verifiable proof, you are obligated to remove erroneous and unlawful late payments on my payment history. Listed below This account should not reflect as negative : XXXX. XXXX # XXXX YOU ARE NOT reporting 100 % correctly. You are violating FCRA. REMOVE the late payments on my payment history ASAP.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10469,None,Consent provided,Web,07/31/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9674153
