04/05/24,Credit card,Store credit card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Card was charged for something you did not purchase with the card,"I called my credit card company back on XX/XX/24 & asked for a complete payoff amount on my balance & was given one. I immediately paid that stated balance and assumed that was the end of it. A couple of weeks later I received my lien release on the item I had a balance for along with a payoff statement showing a {$0.00} balance. Today ( XX/XX/24 ) I received another mailing from them which turned out to be a billing statement for the amount of {$0.00} ( XXXX cents! ). I of course called the company to find out what was going on as I already had my lien release with the payoff statement & never used the card again. I thought maybe I had to pay just to have the card on my person but that wasn't the case, so I asked them if it was interest ( on a XXXX balance ) & was told that wasn't it, and it also wasn't any fees. They turned around & told me that I owed the XXXX cents ( {$0.00} ) on my account still ; over 1.5 months later! So, I asked them in no uncertain terms how it is I had a lien release with a payoff showing a {$0.00} balance & all they would do is try to pawn it off as what I owed. Totally wrong so I requested to close the account & they again tried to get me to pay the XXXX cents! I declined & told them to close it with the XXXX cents removed & to reflect that it was closed by the customer & not them. I received no explanation as to how that {$0.00} got back on my account & why I would have a lien release if I still owed $ $ $ on the account! I did get threatened to be hung up on if I kept complaining about it too! So, I had to coddled them to get them to do what never should've had to be done in the first place! They claim a mailing will be sent within 3 to 5 business days, but I won't hold my breath on that & fully expect another round of fighting to happen before it's all said & done! I hope not!",None,