07/07/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Public record information inaccurate,"After disputing a bankruptcy on my report with Experian, I sent them court documents proving the inaccuracy. Experian did not provide a reason for the bankruptcy case number XXXX. Experian 's response was that the information on the report is valid. However, they did not explain where they got this information. This is a violation of my consumer protection rights, and they rejected my request to dispute the matter again, which is a serious violation of my consumer law rights. Despite presenting supporting documents from the courthouse, Experian refused to delete the inaccurate information on my personal report.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,NY,10032,None,Consent provided,Web,07/07/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9442879
