08/20/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Problem with personal statement of dispute,"In late XXXX, I noticed late payments from a Capital One account on my credit report. I found, I was an authorized user on a relatives account, so I requested to be removed and for the late payments to be removed as well. Capital One advised me to contact the credit bureaus pertaining to the late payments. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, I reached out to XXXX, explained the situation, and was assured it would be handled. However, a month later, I found that the account was no longer listed when I tried to pay my BJs balance on My Mobile App. I immediately contacted Capital One and learned that XXXX had reported the account as fraud. 

I spoke with a supervisor at Capital One, who instructed me to send a notarized letter with my name, address, Social Security number, and confirmation of ownership of the account. Capital one XXXX assured me the account will be Reopened. 

I followed the Capital One supervisors instructions to send a notarized letter taking ownership of the account. However, when I called back in late XXXX I was told it was being investigated, I then called back the end of XXXX and was told the account would not be reopened and the debt was owed. The representative was rude and unhelpful very solution focus and unprofessional. This has been such a uneasy experience. I do not think this is fair treatment what so ever I simply begged for a further investigation into this matter. 

I contacted XXXX again and spoke with agent named XXXX. He confirmed that a previous agent disputed the XXXX account and other capital one accounts. XXXX confirm the time and date I spoke to agent, although he would not provide a first name he gave me a file number XXXX. XXXX advised no further action could be taken. He mentioned that the dispute was filed as an account not associated with my name, effectively treating it as fraud with the creditor. 

I expressed my frustration and then requested that this issue be reviewed for training purposes to prevent similar problems for other consumers. The BJs account is crucial for my daily needs, and this situation has been extremely stressful for me. 
This situation has caused significant emotional distress, and the agents Ive spoken with have been unresponsive and unsympathetic. I am caught between Capital One and XXXX, with neither taking responsibility for their agents mistakes or providing clear guidance. 


