03/16/24,Student loan,Federal student loan servicing,Dealing with your lender or servicer,Trouble with how payments are being handled,"I have student loans being serviced by MOHELA. I have been paying my loans down every month for many years, even when a payment wasn't due, always on the first of the month, in order to minimize the compounding interest. When I attempted to do so on XXXX XXXX, I was met with a message saying my account was still in transition to a new website. I checked back daily, only to receive the same message. I filed a complaint with the Federal Student Aid website, to which I have never received any response. 

When I was finally able to access my account on the new website roughly a week later, I found that my interest had not been paused. While this was frustrating, and I intended to try and address it, I tried to pay it off, just to slow the accrual. I found that the link to do so wasn't working, so I was unable to pay. The cycle started again, when I logged in every day to try and pay, and was unable to do so. I tried messaging them through their website, and received no response. 

I was finally able to get through to their customer service line on XX/XX/XXXX. When I explained the issue to the customer service agent, she informed me that MOHELA was aware of the issue, and that payment had been down for everyone for over a week, and would likely be down for at least another week while they tried to repair it. I asked if my interest was being compounded during this period. She stated that it was. I asked if those of us affected by their system 's issues would be refunded our interest, given that the fault was not on us. She stated that we would not.",Company believes it acted appropriately as authorized by contract or law,MOHELA,NY,12866,None,Consent provided,Web,03/16/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8562009
