06/27/24,Credit card,Store credit card,Fees or interest,Unexpected increase in interest rate,"I purchased an item with a discount price {$14.00} at Victoria 's Secret and applied for a store credit card, which I never received by mail. On XX/XX/XXXX, much earlier than the due date, I made a {$14.00} payment over the phone and received confirmation that the payment had been processed. Today, XX/XX/XXXX, I received a call from a private number claiming I owe around {$68.00} ( approximate amount ) due to a bank rejection. During the call, the person insisted they had all my information and offered to reduce the amount to around {$38.00} if I agreed immediately. However, I grew suspicious, so I contacted customer service again. They mentioned a different amount owed, around {$71.00}, and asked me to check my bank statement for any record of payment rejection. Yes, I found no record of the {$14.00} payment or any related transactions. But shouldn't I have received any information about this rejection or subsequent charges earlier, not until today? I firmly believe I should only owe the initial {$14.00}. Therefore, I've requested the account be closed to avoid any further interest charges.",None,"Bread Financial Holdings, Inc.",NY,11367,Servicemember,Consent provided,Web,06/27/24,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,9362618
