06/29/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Closing your account,Company closed your account,"On XX/XX/XXXX, I received a push notification on my phone saying that my Apple Card ( Goldman Sachs ) had been closed. When I connected with customer support, they said they had no information but that an email about the closure had been sent. The email cited violation of customer agreement, however after reviewing the customer agreement, I had no indication of what violation I had made - the card had never been used for illicit activity, gambling, or fraudulent activities, and I had always made my payments on time and in full each month since opening the card. The customer support agent said he'd open a case, and that it could take up to XXXX business days to resolve. 

Additionally, the high yield savings account I had opened via the Apple Card was locked, and I am unable to withdraw or transfer the funds. I connected with customer support again on XX/XX/XXXX, who was unable to provide any information outside of "" the account is being closed. '' I was given the option to receive a check, or have them open a case to enable me access to the account for the purposes of transferring the money. I opted for the latter, because I was scared of the check getting lost in the mail. 

No one at XXXX - Goldman Sachs has been able to provide me with the cause of closure of my Apple Card or the restriction of my savings account.",None,GOLDMAN SACHS BANK USA,NY,10016,None,Consent provided,Web,06/29/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9384856
