04/02/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"Despite my continued efforts, I have yet to see any resolution to these issues. Enclosed is a copy of the letter I previously sent to the credit bureaus. Your firm 's response deemed my request for verification of erroneous items on my report as "" frivolous '' or "" irrelevant. '' I want to stress that I consider this matter of utmost importance. Should you disregard my original request, which was sent via certified mail, I will not hesitate to escalate the matter to the Federal Trade Commission. I urge you to conduct a thorough reexamination of the following information and provide evidence supporting the alleged item, such as a contract, note, or any document bearing my signature. If such evidence can not be provided, I demand the immediate removal of these items from my report.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,117XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/02/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8680433
