04/01/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"Subject : Urgent : Dispute of Account Information - Immediate Action RequiredDear Self Bank, I am writing to you with utmost urgency regarding discrepancies in the account information associated with my account. As a consumer, I demand immediate action to rectify these inaccuracies in accordance with Section 609 of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) .Account Details : Account Name : XXXX XXXX Account Number : Credit Card Ending XXXX It has come to my attention that the information reported by XXXX XXXX  may contain errors or inaccuracies. I vehemently dispute the accuracy of this information and insist on a thorough investigation into the matter.Under the FCRA, it is your obligation to ensure the accuracy of the information provided to consumer reporting agencies. Therefore, I demand that you promptly provide me with the original documentation related to this account, including any agreements or contracts that I purportedly signed upon its opening.I expect your immediate attention to this matter and a response within 30 days as mandated by federal law. Failure to address this dispute and provide satisfactory resolution will leave me with no choice but to escalate this matter further.I am not providing my Social Security card or any other personal identification at this time. It is your responsibility to verify the accuracy of the reported information without requiring additional documentation from me.Your prompt action in resolving this matter is imperative. I trust that you will handle this dispute with the urgency and seriousness it deserves.Sincerely XXXX XXXX",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,109XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/01/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8670469
