03/12/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Dear [ Credit Reporting Bureau ], I am writing to dispute a late payment reported on my credit report for the [ Account Name ] account ( XXXX : [ XXXX ] ). 

I have reviewed my credit reports from all three bureaus ( Equifax, XXXX, and XXXX ) and discovered inconsistencies regarding this late payment amount due. While your report reflects a late payment on XXXX, neither Equifax nor XXXX reports this delinquency. Payment was made to the creditor on time and never received a late payment notice Due to this discrepancy, I believe the information on your report is inaccurate. The Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) requires credit reporting agencies to ensure the accuracy of information they provide. In this case, the inconsistency across all three reports raises concerns about the validity of the late payment on your record. 

Therefore, I request that you investigate this matter further and remove the late payment from my report. If the investigation reveals the late payment is truly inaccurate, I also request that you update the information with the other two credit reporting bureaus to ensure consistency across all reports. 

In the event you are unable to verify the accuracy of the late payment, I request that you remove the entire ( XXXX : [ XXXX ] ) account from my report. 

I have enclosed copies of my credit reports from XXXX, Equifax and XXXX highlighting the inconsistency in the late payment amounts for your reference. 

Thank you for your time and attention to this matter. I look forward to your prompt resolution. 

Sincerely, XXXX",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,100XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/12/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8528473
