03/04/24,Debt collection,Other debt,Communication tactics,Frequent or repeated calls,"I called Affirm and asked them to send a statement of the account that they are demanding payment on, and Affirm refused to send me a statement. The first representative simply hung up on me. The second representative refused to provide any information at all. I asked him ( his name was XXXX XXXX to connect me to a supervisor. He connected me to a young woman named XXXX who I could barely understand as she spoke with a heavy accent and spoke very quickly. She explicitly refused to send me a statement in the mail, but said that she could send me the information in email. I asked her to please send that. I held on the line twice while she said she was preparing the email. She sent me an email that said "" Please log in to your account '' and had a button to log in to the account. I told her truthfully that I can not log in to the account, and I told her that I needed a statement that would give me an account number, the original balance, the amounts paid thus far, and the remaining balance. She said that they do not use statements. She did describe a "" loan letter '' and provided verbal information about this, but she refused to send the information in email, as well as refusing to send it in the US mail. I asked her where she was located and she said in XXXX XXXX. I asked her to transfer me to someone in the United States, because they would understand that the law requires them to send a statement. She told me that they do not have people in the United States. I read her a statement from their website that states they are located in the United States. I told her that I needed the phone number for their office in the United States because that person would understand that I am legally entitled to receive a statement from them, and she told me again that they "" do not have anyone in the United States. '' She was willing to give me the information verbally, but not in any way in writing. I told her that I still need the information in writing and will be making a complaint. This conversation ended at XXXX XXXX Eastern Time on XXXX XXXX, 2024.",None,"Affirm Holdings, Inc",NY,13440,Older American,Consent provided,Web,03/04/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8477298
