03/30/24,Credit card,Store credit card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"My PC Richard/Synchrony store credit card was out of my possession ( likely lost or stolen ). A purchase was made at a PC Richard store using this stolen card, however the person making the purchase provided an address, phone number and email address that did not match any of the information on my PC Richard account or my PC Richard/Synchrony bank credit card account. 

I called in XXXX to dispute these transactions and was told that the address on file had recently been changed to the fraudulent address ( XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX, NY XXXX ). The agent indicated that the transaction and account had been flagged as a result of this address change. 

I never received documents indicating the resolution or closing of the case. On XX/XX/XXXX I reviewed my credit report which stated that my PC Richard/Synchrony account has a past due balance. When I called Synchrony bank to inquiry about this, they stated that the dispute was not found in my favor because the purchase was made in person and the card was swiped. 

I reopened the case with Synchrony, however my complaint is 2 fold : 1 - I was never provided with notification that the dispute case was closed.

2 - Synchrony bank noted a potentially fraudulent address when the purchase was made and permitted the transaction to be completed. Further, when I called Synchrony in XXXX, they verified my identity through confirmation of my SSN as well as through a secure link using facial recognition and a photo of my holding government-issued id. The dispute investigator did not take into consideration the contact information difference between what was on my PC Richard/Synchrony account and the invoice that Synchrony stated the merchant provided to them on XX/XX/XXXX. I have requested that the dispute case be reopened and I have provided them with the merchant provided invoice, my address dispute with XXXX to support the fraudulent address and my claim that I did not perform the transaction. 

In the meantime, my credit score has dropped XXXX points and needs this needs to be corrected ASAP. I did not perform these transactions and Synchrony must perform an adequate review of the information provided. A simple review of the address, phone number and email differences from the merchant-provided invoice and my information on file with PC Richard/Synchrony along with my identity verification and dispute is plenty of evidence to find in my favor and remove the past due status on my account.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL,NY,115XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/30/24,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8662400
