04/11/24,Debt collection,Telecommunications debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt was result of identity theft,"On XX/XX/XXXX, I requested a credit report from XXXX as I noticed that my credit score had gone down considerably from last month. On the report there was a debt collection. I called XXXX, also on XX/XX/XXXX and was told that Sunrise Credit Services was collecting a {$2200.00} debt for XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX. The account was opened on XX/XX/XXXX and the phone number issued was a XXXX XXXX XXXX under my maiden name, XXXX XXXX. A phone was purchased for {$1900.00} and the remainder of the debt was in unpaid bills. I disputed the claim once already at XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX is holding me responsible. 
I have put in a fraudulent claim to XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX 
Not only have I not used my maiden name in 25 years, I live in New York, have never lived in Massachusetts and do not have any friends or family in Massachusetts or associated with the mobile number XXXX 
Please advise. 
Thank you. 
