06/17/24,Checking or savings account,Savings account,Managing an account,Deposits and withdrawals,"On or around XX/XX/year>, I was informed by a banker from Chase, whom I was working with on a checking account matter, that he had randomly noticed my savings account had been deactivated due to inactivity. This makes no sense since I have made withdrawals at least monthly from the account for at least the last 5 years. 
I received no notice of the deactivation, no letter, no email, no text, no note or flag on the on- line system, nothing. 
There is nothing in the Deposit Account Agreement about the criteria and/ or procedures for account deactivation. 
After attempting unsuccessfully at least 5 times to reach the banker by phone, I went into the branch on XX/XX/year> and attempted to deposit a check. The teller informed me that the account was deactivated and I couldnt deposit the check. I sat with a different banker, signed some papers, reactivated the account, and deposited the check. All the personnel I spoke to at the branch did not understand why the account had been deactivated. 
I submitted several inquiries on Chases on-line secure messaging system to attempt to understand their unwritten rules about account deactivation and notice procedures. I receive conflicting answers about the unwritten rules, and an apology for not receiving notice.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,10598,Older American,Consent provided,Web,06/17/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9277454
