03/30/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am writing to dispute the inaccuracies present in my credit report concerning the account held by XXXX XXXX XXXX, Account Number XXXX. According to my recent credit report, there are discrepancies that require immediate attention. 

Upon thorough review of the reported information, I have found that XXXX XXXX XXXX has failed to provide adequate documentation validating the existence of a contractual agreement between us. As per the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), consumers are entitled to verification of any debts reported on their credit file. To date, XXXX XXXX XXXX has not furnished any evidence substantiating their claim. 

Furthermore, the inaccurate reporting by XXXX XXXX XXXX is adversely affecting my creditworthiness and causing undue financial strain. I request that XXXX XXXX XXXX promptly cease reporting this disputed account to all credit reporting agencies until such time that sufficient proof of the alleged debt can be provide. 

I also kindly request your immediate investigation into this matter and investigate the inaccuracies and inconsistencies XXXX XXXX XXXX has been reporting different information to the credit bureaus which is illegal. After the investigation I kindly request the removal of any negative reporting associated with the disputed account from my credit report. Additionally, I expect XXXX XXXX XXXX to provide me with the documentation verifying the validity of the debt in question with the legally mandated timeframe. 

Please consider this letter as a formal dispute under the FCRA, and I anticipate your prompt resolution of this matter.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10562,None,Consent provided,Web,03/30/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8660905
