07/20/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Dear XX/XX/XXXXXXXX, DISPUTE AND NOTICE OF INTENT TO ARBITRATE I am writing to respond to your XX/XX/year> letter and to reiterate my dispute regarding the inaccurate information reported to the credit bureaus. I also notify you of my intent to initiate arbitration proceedings pursuant to our agreement. 

ATTEMPTS TO CONTACT Your letter claims attempts were made to contact me by phone and email. However, 15 U.S.C. 1666b explicitly requires mailed disclosures, specifically stating that "" a creditor shall furnish a clear and conspicuous written disclosure '' to the consumer. A phone call or email does not satisfy this requirement. To comply with the law, you must provide evidence of mailed disclosures, including a tracking number for certified mail. 

DAMAGE TO REPUTATION Your company 's inaccurate reporting has damaged my reputation, resulting in credit denials and significant time and money spent disputing this fraudulent account. 

REQUEST FOR PROOF I reiterate my request for proof of proper disclosures and investigation procedures, as mandated by 15 U.S.C. 1681s-2. Your failure to provide such evidence will be held against you. 

VIOLATIONS AND DAMAGES Your company has willfully violated the FCRA, resulting in multiple damages. I will pursue these violations under 15 U.S.C. 1681n and 1681o, with damages of {$1000.00} per violation. I have counted over five violations, totaling {$5000.00} in damages. 

ARBITRATION I will initiate arbitration proceedings if this matter is not resolved within the next 15 days. Your company will be responsible for covering all filing fees and costs associated with arbitration, as per our agreement",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,NY,11207,None,Consent provided,Web,07/20/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9558313
