04/16/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Deposits and withdrawals,"I deposited a XXXX check for my minor child that was given to her as a birthday gift from my uncle. My daughter turned XXXX this year and is not capable of managing XXXX. I have deposited checks to my account for my minor children over the years and it has never been an issue. On Saturday, I lost access to my account. I called on Sunday morning and Citibank stated there was fraudulent activity and I had to call back on Monday when the fraud department was open. I did that. I spoke to XXXX. I verified with him that the check was for my minor child. He said not a problem the hold on my account would be lifted by today ( XX/XX/XXXX ). The hold was not lifted, so I called back. They stated my account was approved for closure! And that they do not accept third party checks. No one would help me. They treated me like a criminal. I explained that I have deposited checks for my daughter several times over the years to which they state I did not. I pulled up My emails with the dates of the deposits and informed them. The lady said okay so we still have to verify from the person who wrote the check. This is absolutely horrible and they treated me so poorly. I am humiliated.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,11209,Servicemember,Consent provided,Web,04/16/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8788093
