03/19/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Statement Regarding Unauthorized Sharing of Transactional History To Whom It May Concern, I, XXXX XXXX, am issuing this statement to address the unauthorized sharing of my transactional history by XXXX XXXX . This egregious violation of my privacy rights has caused me significant concern and distress. I wish to highlight the numerous laws and regulations that have been violated as a result of this unauthorized sharing. 

First and foremost, XXXX XXXX XXXX actions are in direct contravention of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), specifically 15 U.S. Code 1681a, which defines the term "" consumer report '' as any communication of information by a consumer reporting agency that bears on a consumer 's creditworthiness. By sharing my transactional history without my permission, XXXX XXXX is effectively creating a consumer report without adhering to the strict regulations outlined in the FCRA.

Furthermore, XXXX XXXX XXXX actions violate the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act ( GLBA ), particularly 15 U.S. Code 6801, which emphasizes the importance of protecting the privacy and security of customers ' nonpublic personal information. By sharing my transactional history without my consent, XXXX XXXX is failing to uphold its obligation to safeguard my confidential financial information. 

Additionally, XXXX XXXX XXXX unauthorized sharing of my transactional history may constitute a violation of state privacy laws, including [ insert relevant state privacy laws if applicable ], which further reinforces the severity of this breach of privacy.

Moreover, XXXX XXXX XXXX actions demonstrate a lack of
compliance with its own privacy policies and disclosures, as required under the GLBA and other relevant regulations. Failure to obtain explicit consent before sharing sensitive financial information is a clear violation of these policies and disclosures.

In conclusion, I demand that XXXX XXXX  immediately cease and desist from sharing my transactional history without my explicit consent. Furthermore, I expect full compliance with all applicable laws and regulations governing consumer privacy and data protection. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX ---",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,109XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/19/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8567640
