04/06/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Investigation took more than 30 days,"I am writing to file a formal complaint against your agencies for failing to conduct a timely investigation and rectify inaccuracies within my credit report, in violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). 

On XX/XX/XXXX, I submitted a dispute regarding discrepancies observed in my credit report pertaining to XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. Despite being well within the 30-day period mandated by the FCRA, I have yet to receive a response or any indication of an investigation being conducted. 

The discrepancies identified include variations in reported last activity dates across TransUnion, XXXX, and XXXX. Specifically, XXXX lists the last activity date as XX/XX/XXXX, XXXX as XX/XX/XXXX, and TransUnion as XX/XX/XXXX. Additionally, there are inconsistencies in the representation of payment history, with XXXX indicating XXXX instances of 90-day late payments compared to only 1 reported by XXXX. Moreover, discrepancies in on-time payment percentages and specific entries further highlight the lack of accuracy and consistency in my credit report. 

These discrepancies not only violate my federally protected consumer rights to privacy and confidentiality under 15 USC 1681 but also undermine the integrity of the credit reporting system. As per 15 U.S. Code 1681i ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ), it is your obligation to conduct a reasonable reinvestigation within 30 days of receiving notice of dispute from the consumer. Yet, your agencies have failed to fulfill this obligation, thereby disregarding the purpose of the FCRA to ensure fair and equitable treatment of consumers. 

I demand an immediate escalation of this matter and a thorough investigation into the inaccuracies and inconsistencies reported in my credit report. Furthermore, I insist on receiving documented proof of any alleged late payments associated with my account. 

It is imperative that XXXX, XXXX, and TransUnion take swift and decisive action to rectify these violations of the FCRA and restore the accuracy and integrity of my credit report. Failure to do so will result in further escalation of this complaint and pursuit of legal remedies available under the FCRA. 

I expect a prompt response and resolution to this matter. Please do not hesitate to contact me if further information is required.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,10562,None,Consent provided,Web,04/06/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8711164
