03/11/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"Subject : Urgent Notice : Cease Unauthorized Credit Reporting or Face Legal Action Violations of FCRA and New York Identity Theft Laws Dear CAPITAL ONE, I am contacting you to address a grave infringement concerning the unauthorized reporting of information to my credit report, as mandated by the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) under Sections 1681b ( a ) ( 2 ), 1681c ( a ) ( 2 ), and 1681s-2 ( a ), and New York state laws pertaining to identity theft and fraud. 
It has come to my attention that CAPITAL ONE has been engaging in unauthorized reporting to my credit report without first obtaining my explicit consent. According to federal law, as outlined in the FCRA, the consumer 's consent is an absolute prerequisite for such reporting activities under Section 1681b ( a ) ( 2 ).

Moreover, New York state law, particularly the provisions regarding identity theft and fraud, emphasize the critical importance of consumer consent for credit reporting. Any violation of these laws constitutes a serious offense.

I firmly assert that I have not granted CAPITAL ONE permission to report any information to my credit report. This egregious lack of explicit consent represents a flagrant violation of my rights, potentially resulting in harm to my creditworthiness and a blatant disregard for federal and state laws.

I demand, unequivocally, that CAPITAL ONE immediately ceases all further reporting of information to my credit report without obtaining my explicit consent, as mandated by Section 1681b ( a ) ( 2 ) of the FCRA and New York state laws concerning identity theft and fraud. Failure to comply within the allotted 30-day timeframe will be construed as willful noncompliance, subject to severe penalties under applicable laws, including those pertaining to identity theft.

It is imperative to understand that obtaining consent is not discretionary but a legal obligation under these specific sections of the FCRA and New York state laws. This is not a negotiation ; it is a directive for compliance with both federal and state regulations, safeguarding consumers like myself from unauthorized and detrimental credit reporting.

I expect immediate action on this matter and anticipate that CAPITAL ONE will promptly rectify these egregious violations, thereby respecting my rights under federal and state laws.",None,CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION,NY,11542,None,Consent provided,Web,03/11/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8516054
