05/28/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am submitting this dispute due to the blatant violations of the Fair Credit Reporting Act as mentioned below. Congress has found that there is a need to ensure that consumer reporting agencies exercise their grave responsibilities with fairness, impartiality, and a respect for the consumers right to privacy. Correction to the following violations of law needs to be performed to ensure the protection of the consumers rights. 

Violations : 1. The law ( 15 USC 1681 ( 2 ) ( A ) ( i ) ) excludes transactions or experiences between the consumer and the person making the report. 

The law does not permit transactional history to be displayed on the report but every account on my credit report contains transactional history which completely violates my right to privacy. 

THERES NO NEED TO LIST EACH ACCOUNT THAT IS IMPACTED BY THE STATED VIOLATIONS BECAUSE EVERY ACCOUNT IS REPORTING TRANSACTIONAL HISTORY. 

2. The law ( 15 U.S. Code 1681b ) requires permissible purpose in written form from the consumer before adding anything to the consumers report. 

This agency did not receive my consent in any form before adding a collections account to my report nor do I consent to the report of this account. 

Collections : XXXX XXXX XXXX 3. The law ( 15 U.S. Code 1681b ) requires permissible purpose in written form from the consumer before adding anything to the consumers report. 

This agency did not receive my consent in any form before adding inquiries to my report nor do I consent to the report of any inquiries.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10037,None,Consent provided,Web,05/28/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,9108561
