ying information pursuant to 12 CFR 1022.3 ( g ) ( 1 ) which is my name social security number, government identification number date of birth, pursuant to 12 CFR 1022.3 ( g ) 3 ) my account number which is a unique electronic identification number Used To identify me the consumer specifically, in conjunction with information regarding my transactions and experiences, which would be a consumer report pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681a ( d ) ( 1 ) ( A ) making XXXX XXXX XXXX a consumer reporting agency due to the fact such information is bearing on my consumer credit worthiness, credit standing, credit capacity, character, general reputation, collected in whole or in part for the purpose of serving as a factor in establishing the consumers eligibility for credit and has a direct reflection on my credit score pursuant to 15 U.S. Code 1681g ( f ) ( 2 ) ( A ) ( i ) The FCRA is public law and ignorance to the law is no excuse pursuant to "" 619. You are liable for your actions of obtaining information on i the consumer from XXXX XXXX XXXX a consumer reporting agencies under false pretenses and are now indebted XXXX for such violations in accordance with the FRCA, please note i may take action against any related person for the corporation which they can be held liable for the fine directly and face jail time ________________________________________________________________________________ "" Any person who knowingly and willfully obtains information on a consumer from a consumer reporting agency under false pretenses shall be fined not more than {$5000.00} or imprisoned not more than one year, or both.

Transunion as a consumer reporting agency you failed to maintain reasonable procedures to limit the furnishing of consumer reports to the purposes listed under section 604, such action is in violation of the fcra "" 607 ( a ). Compliance procedures '' 617. Transunion You're liable for your actions of negligent noncompliance of the rules set forth under the FCRA your liable to i the consumer as a result of your failure to follow the requirements of the FCRA in a amount of _____ for damages sustained as the result of your failure to follow requirements of the FCRA I am aware in order to be in consumer reporting agency may furnish a consumer report under the following circumstances and no other pursuant to 604 ( 2 ) In accordance with the written instructions of the consumer to whom it relates Permissible purposes of reports and under any other reason under 604 of the Fcra failed to comply with the requirement imposed under the FCRA pursuant 604 "" ( 2 ) as i have not given you any written consent to furnish a report on my behalf, for your actions of creating a consumer report on my behalf without consent617. You're liable for your actions of negligent noncompliance of the rules set forth under the FCRA 604 ( 2 ), your liable to i the consumer as a result of your failure to follow the requirements of the FCRA in a amount of _____ for damages sustained as the result of your failure to follow requirements of the FCRA In addition i aware a financial institution may share my non public information to consumer reporting agencies in accordance with the GLBA, according to the cfpb interpretation of the FCRA quoted as followed __________________________________________________________________________ https : XXXX A person, including a financial institution, may share information strictly related to its own transactions or experiences with a consumer ( such as the consumers payment history, or an account with the institution ) with any third party, without regard to affiliation, without becoming a consumer reporting agency. The Privacy of Consumer Financial Information regulations that implement the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act ( GLBA ) may restrict this type of information sharing because it meets the definition of nonpublic personal information under the Privacy regulations. Therefore, sharing it with nonaffiliated third parties may be subject to an opt-out notice under the privacy regulations. In turn, the FCRA may also restrict activities that the GLBA permits. For example, the GLBA permits a financial institution to share a list of its customers and information such as their credit scores with another financial institution to jointly market or sponsor other financial products or services. This communication may be a consumer report under the FCRA and could potentially cause the sharing financial institution to become a consumer reporting agency.

Even if a financial institution shared non public information of a consumers, customer such information is consider a consumer report according to the FTC interpretation 5. REPORT CONCERNING A CONSUMERS ATTRIBUTES AND HISTORY. Information that does not identify a specific consumer does not constitute a consumer report even if the communication is used in part to determine eligibility.

However, information may constitute a consumer report even if it does not identify the consumer by name if it could otherwise reasonably be linked to the consumer. 
