04/03/24,Mortgage,FHA mortgage,Applying for a mortgage or refinancing an existing mortgage,Changes in loan terms during the application process,"In XXXX of 2021 Dovenmuele acquired my loan from XXXX. My mortgage was acquired while I was actively a part of a COVID-19 forbearance plan ( under the CARES Act ) in which allowed a temporary suspension of my mortgage payment by way of forbearance. 
During this forbearance period, the financial institution can not charge fees, penalties or interest beyond the regular monthly mortgage payment. 
Dovenmuehle has breached my deferral agreement, in which the bank agreed to bring my mortgage current and delay any repayment obligation for missed monthly mortgage payments without my accruing any interest or penalties. I would not be responsible for any past due amounts until the earlier of the maturity date of the mortgage, sale of the mortgaged property, or the payoff or the refinance of the mortgage loan.

Dovenmuele has breached the agreement by adding the total past due payments to the outstanding principal balance on the loan, effectively double- charging and improperly increasing the amount of my mortgage.

There are violations to truth-in- lending, consumer protection act, and to RESPA.

Dovenmuehle has misrepresented the application of the deferred payments as I've requested numerous times for an explanation for the substantial increase to my mortgage. I've requested an explanantion for the "" new '' principal in which inflated my loan from {$100000.00} to nearly {$120000.00}. The forbearance plan was intended to help homeowners and yet I feel deceived. Dovenmuehle offered only a modification in which put me further in debt to Dovenmuehle and only offered reprieve for approximately one year. There representatives are rude, have no regard and have no explanation for the "" new '' principal.",None,"Dovenmuehle Mortgage, Inc.",NY,120XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/04/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8678058
