04/03/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Closing an account,Company closed your account,"I woke up to an email from Chase Bank that they had restricted my account ( Checking & Savings ) with them. I called them immediately to resolve this. They provided no help and just told me that the restriction is permanent and that my account would be closed in 7-10 business days and that I would receive a check with remaining funds. They provided no reason as to why it was being closed for no reason. I went in person to a Chase and asked the same questions and asked for options to receive the funds sooner as Chase is my only bank and this has left me without ANY access to my funds. My direct deposit from my job also went through the day after this so I have no access to that ( I tried to cancel it but it wasnt in enough advance of the direct deposit, it was already scheduled ). I can not buy food, access transportation, buy necessary healthcare products, etc. In person they said the same thing. They said they were ending the relationship without any explanation as to why and that I could not expedite the funds. I followed up today, 6 days after the initial email, to see when the account would be closed or get any sort of update as to when I would receive my funds. Again, they provided me with no information and the representative said it should close within 10 business days. I asked her to clarify if that meant 10 business days from the original email or from today. She was very vague and danced around the question. After researching online, I found that Chase is notorious for closing accounts for no reason and with no notice. They do not care if their long-term, loyal customers are able to eat or pay for their shelter or healthcare products. I need these funds sent to me ASAP.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11103,None,Consent provided,Web,04/03/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8689716
