03/05/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX, PA XXXX Experian XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, TX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, GA XXXX Consumer Financial Protection Bureau XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX, Iowa XXXX Federal Trade Commission XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX Washington XXXX DC XXXX Subject : Dispute of Inaccurate Information on Credit Report Dear XXXX XXXX XXXX, Experian XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX XXXX I am writing to dispute inaccurate information on my credit report. I recently received a response from XXXX and XXXX XXXX regarding an account that has been reported on my credit file. The information provided by XXXX and XXXXXXXX XXXX does not align with the information reported by XXXX, XXXX, and Experian, and has resulted in discrepancies in the reported dates and amounts associated with the account. 

According to the response from XXXX and XXXX XXXX, they reached out to XXXX and confirmed that the account was assigned to a debt collector and settled for {$800.00}. However, the information provided by XXXX, XXXX, and Experian does not reflect the same settlement amount or date. This inconsistency has significantly impacted my creditworthiness and has the potential to harm my financial standing. 

I am requesting a thorough investigation into this matter and urge XXXX, Experian and XXXX to update the information on my credit report to accurately reflect the settlement and any other relevant details regarding the account in question. I also request that XXXX provide me with a copy of my updated credit report once the investigation is complete. 

Additionally, I have filed complaints with the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) and the Federal Trade Commission ( FTC ) regarding this issue, as it violates the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) by reporting inaccurate information. 

Please find enclosed copies of relevant documentation supporting my dispute, including the response from XXXX and XXXXXXXX XXXX and any other pertinent information. 

Thank you for your attention to this matter. I look forward to a prompt resolution and the removal of the inaccurate information from my credit report. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,NY,11234,None,Consent provided,Web,03/05/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8481522
