04/11/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Card was charged for something you did not purchase with the card,"In response to the Companys Response regarding case # XXXX, The response from Discover Credit Card is inaccurate and insufficient. When I initially called Discover Customer Service regarding the fraud charges, I specifically told Discover that there were XXXX transactions by XXXX. from XX/XX/XXXX, to XX/XX/XXXX, not from XX/XX/XXXX, as XXXX XXXX claimed in response. The breakdown of those charges is XXXX transactions for {$39.00}, XXXX for {$4.00}, and XXXX for {$1.00}, totaling {$630.00}. I called XXXX, and the phone number doesnt work, as I told Discover many times. Therefore, I urge Discover to call XXXX, which XXXX claims I had a subscription from. Discover keeps asking to provide documentation from a merchant on the Discover dispute site ; however, as I stressed many times because this is a fraud, I have no documents I can represent other than the detailed record I kept since I realized that I only received a partial refund. XXXX XXXX asserts that some transactions are valid due to the documentation provided by the merchant. I demand to be given documents, Discover claims obtained from XXXX, and transaction details Discover asserts they have received from XXXX to conclude those charges are valid. XXXX XXXX claims she received them based on Discovers investigation. I would like to see the transaction details containing an initial agreement for monthly subscriptions and receipts for each month during the above-mentioned duration. Moreover, The response from Discover concluded that I received the monetary relief amount of {$96.00}. However, as you can see in Table XXXX attached, I havent received any monetary relief. XXXX refunded me {$350.00} out of {$630.00}. The {$270.00} still remains to be refunded to me. I called XXXX today and demanded that they email me that Discover has rejected the refund and its amount, but I havent received an email from them yet. I called XXXX XXXX of Discover around XXXX XXXX, but she hasnt returned my call. The Discover fraud policy said that all Discover card members are protected with our {$0.00} Fraud Liability Guarantee, which means you're never responsible for unauthorized purchases on your Discover Card account. I want Discover to provide me with my authorization to XXXX since Discover concluded that the charges are valid based on the documentation provided by the merchant. Discover failed to detect suspicious transactions. My other credit companies immediately send me notifications and ensure that the charges are valid.",None,DISCOVER BANK,NY,115XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/11/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8740698
