03/15/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"I am deeply concerned and frustrated to discover that despite your confirmation of the deletion of certain inquiries from my consumer report, they have been reinserted. This violates my rights under the FCRA and disregards the authority of the CFPB, to whom I initially reported this issue. 

I filed a complaint with the CFPB regarding unauthorized inquiries. Equifax 's letter dated XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX confirmed their removal, leading me to believe the matter was resolved. However, upon reviewing my updated report, I found the inquiries reinstated. By reinserting inquiries that were previously confirmed as deleted, Equifax is not only breaching its duty to accurately report consumer information but is also misleading consumers and regulatory bodies alike. It is deeply troubling to note that Equifax not only failed to uphold its commitment to rectify the inaccuracies on my consumer report but also provided false information to the CFPB regarding the resolution of this matter. Such actions undermine the integrity of the credit reporting system and erode trust in Equifax 's ability to handle consumer disputes effectively and ethically. Furthermore, I expect a thorough investigation into the circumstances surrounding this incident and accountability for those responsible for providing false information to both me and the CFPB. 

Failure to address this matter promptly and adequately will compel me to escalate my complaint through legal channels and pursue all available remedies under the FCRA and other applicable laws. 

Expecting an urgent response and resolution. 

Here is the list of Inquiries that was deleted and now REINSERTED again : XXXX XXXX - Inquiry Date - XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX - Inquiry Date - XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX  - Inquiry Date - XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX  - Inquiry Date - XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX - Inquiry Date - XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Date - XX/XX/XXXX",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11435,None,Consent provided,Web,03/15/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8553081
