05/02/23,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am writing to request an investigation and removal of certain information from my credit report based on the following provisions of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and other relevant federal regulations : 15 USC 1681A ( d ) ( 2 ) ( A ) ( i ) : This provision excludes from credit reports any information solely related to transactions or experiences between ( I ) the consumer and the person making the report.

15 USC 1801 : This provision establishes the policy of Congress that financial institutions ( person making the report ) have an affirmative and continuing obligation to respect the privacy of their customers and to protect the security and confidentiality of their nonpublic personal information.

15 USC 6801 : This provision reiterates the policy of Congress that financial institutions have an affirmative and continuing obligation to respect the privacy of their customers and to protect the security and confidentiality of their nonpublic personal information. 

15 USC 6802 : This provision prohibits financial institutions from disclosing nonpublic personal information to nonaffiliated third parties unless they provide or have provided a notice that complies with section 6803 of this title.

Based on these provisions, I believe that the following items on my credit report are in violation of the FCRA and should be removed : XXXX XXXX : All information including and/or related to late payments XXXX XXXX  : All information including and/or related to late payments XXXX XXXX : All information including and/or related to late payments XXXX XXXX : All information including and/or related to late payments Inquiries : All I kindly request that you conduct a thorough investigation into these items and, if found to be in violation of the FCRA or other applicable regulations, remove them from my credit report. Please provide me with written confirmation of your investigation and any necessary updates or removals to my credit report. 

Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter. I understand that under the FCRA, credit reporting agencies must complete investigations within 30 days of receiving a dispute. I look forward to your timely response. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10030,None,Consent provided,Web,05/02/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6912691
