03/13/24,Student loan,Private student loan,Dealing with your lender or servicer,Received bad information about your loan,"Hello, last year I was informed that a class action lawsuit ( XXXX v. XXXX XXXX ) I was involved in was finalized. As a result, my federal student loans were canceled. The school was proven to be involved in illegal practices when it comes to student loans. 

A few months ago I contacted Navient about XXXX particular loans that I believe should be canceled under the recent settlement decision. I informed them that these three loans in their possession must have been XXXX loans and as such should be consolidated to Fedloans and then canceled as well. The only loans that I know of were FFLP ( federal loans ) and I have no original documentation on these loans, however they insists that the loans are valid private loans. I then asked for all the documentation on these loans and my signed agreement to them to be sent to me and to freeze the loans until we get to the bottom of this. What they mailed to me was a copy of of some document with no loan details, and an electronic signature. The document they send had no details not even who the lender was, the XXXX, or anything specific. This seems like fraud perpetrated by the school and was being enforced by XXXX and now Navient. 

My credit report is being ruined by these three loans mentioned above and I don't even think they are valid loans. They can't produce any documentation proving they are my loans much less private loans and not XXXX loans. 

Someone needs to investigate this Navient company and situations like this I am sure I am not the only person this is being done to. 

Thanks, XXXX",None,"Navient Solutions, LLC.",NY,11561,None,Consent provided,Web,03/13/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8539105
