03/17/24,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",Mobile or digital wallet,Unauthorized transactions or other transaction problem,None,"My issue involves an unjust ruling by PayPal in a payment dispute that favored a claim by a buyer that he did not receive the goods he paid for, where in fact that he actually did. I have filed my complaint both online in the PayPal Resolution Center and by speaking with two separate customer service agents. I have also taken the matter up by email with two PayPal customer executives : XXXX XXXX, VP of Global Customer Service, and XXXX XXXX, Senior VP of Global Customer Service. I have not heard back from anyone about my complaint. The dispute is PayPal case ID number : XXXX XXXX 
The matter concerns a payment transaction through PayPal by the buyer on XX/XX/XXXX for {$300.00}. This was an in-person sale where the buyer had my home address and cell number in order to pick up my merchandise. It was some 10 months later on XX/XX/XXXX that the buyer filed a claim against me and that I was notified by PayPal that the buyer filed a claim of not receiving his goods. According to PayPal rules, a buyer has up to 180 days after a purchase to file a claim for not receiving goods. Why would a buyer wait 10 months to file a complaint, especially when he had both my home address and cell number. And why would PayPal go along with this unjust ruling in favor of the buyer? Upon my notification of this dispute, I personally called the buyer on his cell phone to find out why he filed the dispute, and was told that upon reviewing his expenses for XXXX, he came across a {$300.00} payment that he couldn't account for. I reminded him of the goods I sold him and he told me he failed at the time of the purchase to notate what it was for. I urged him to contact PayPal and tell them it was a big mistake. After I made several follow up attempts with him, by phone and email, he would not reply. At that point I realized that I was scammed by the buyer. Lastly, please note that I have provided PayPal with hard copy evidence showing cell phone screen shots of texts with the buyer indicating when was coming to my house on a specific date and time to pick up his merchandise. And to make matters worse, I have just received a collection notice from PayPal 's collection agency, XXXX XXXX to make restitution for the {$300.00} ( plus a {$15.00} fee imposed by PayPal, which could now impact on my personal credit rating. PLEASE HELP ME TO RIGHT A WRONG MADE BY BOTH A BUYER SCAM ARTIST AND PAYPAL. I have been a long-time buyer using PayPal for many years and have come to trust their services. Now this one time when I am selling personal goods and accepting PayPal payment from buyer, I get stiffed.",None,"Paypal Holdings, Inc",NY,105XX,Older American,Consent provided,Web,03/17/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8564514
