03/31/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"I am writing to formally dispute XXXX hard inquiries listed on my credit report by XXXX XX/XX/XXXX, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXX/XX/XXXX. According to my records, this inquiry was marked as "" Accurate '' ; however, I have NOT authorized or initiated any such inquiry. XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX was previously removed then placed back on my consumer report. XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX was WITHOUT proof verified as "" accurate ''. 

I hereby request that you provide me with proof that I myself authorized or initiated this inquiry myself. It is imperative that you furnish me with documentation or evidence validating my consent for this inquiry to proceed. 

In the absence of satisfactory proof demonstrating my authorization, I respectfully request that this hard inquiry be promptly removed from my account. Failure to provide evidence of my authorization will prompt me to escalate this matter and pursue appropriate actions under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) regarding fraudulent hard inquires. 

I trust that you will handle this matter with the urgency and seriousness it deserves. Please acknowledge receipt of this dispute in writing within reasonable time as mandated by the FCRA. 

Thank you fro your prompt attention to this matter.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10562,None,Consent provided,Web,03/31/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8664377
