03/24/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Closing an account,Fees charged for closing account,"My account was closed on XX/XX/XXXX of 2023. I had a {$0.00} balance. It was gone from my view in my app after 5 business days just like the bank told me it would be. I deleted the app and that was that. Apparently, On XX/XX/XXXX there were numerous debits. This caused the account to be reopened per the bank and made the account overdrawn {$690.00}. They also charged a {$25.00} overdraft fee in XXXX and XXXX. I had no idea about any of this until I received a notice from XXXX that they were refunding a deposit I made from last XX/XX/year> because they had to cancel a booking I made. They advised that the refund was going back to my bank account that I had at the time which was this citizens account. I called citizens to inquire about how they handle the refund since my account was closed and they advised that they were not returning the funds because they were applying it to the negative charge that occurred after the account was closed. The amount of the refund from XXXX was {$400.00}. 
This account had been closed for almost 2 full months before these debits occurred. How can the reopen the account after that long. And now they are keeping my refund from my XXXX deposit to pay?? This is insane",None,"CITIZENS FINANCIAL GROUP, INC.",NY,14043,None,Consent provided,Web,03/24/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8617772
