03/19/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"I have diligently followed all the necessary steps to dispute this account. I've reached out to the bank regarding this issue, and they assured me it's been resolved. Additionally, I contacted law enforcement and filed a report and affidavit, validating the identity theft report. XXXX has complied with legal requirements and removed the accounts, yet XXXX seems to believe I haven't completed all necessary steps. 

AMEX XXXX. 

Despite my efforts, XXXX continues to deny my claims, citing invalid documents. This marks the several complaint I've filed against them, each time receiving the same inadequate response. It appears there is a failure on their part to fulfill their legal obligation to process the identity theft report properly. 

I have submitted reports to a law enforcement agency, including Identitytheft.gov, a federal law enforcement agency. I urge the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) to thoroughly investigate this matter, as it seems XXXX is neglecting their duty in handling identity theft reports. 

The stress of dealing with identity theft and the resulting lack of access to my credit is taking a significant toll on my emotional and physical well-being. It's affecting both my professional and personal life, and I feel overwhelmed as I have no other recourse. 

I want to emphasize that I am the sole individual submitting this complaint. I have not enlisted the help of any third party. I implore you to address this matter urgently.",None,AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY,NY,11219,None,Consent provided,Web,03/19/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8580946
