03/15/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Personal information incorrect,"Today XX/XX/XXXX I reached out to Experian Credit Reporting Agency to try and get inaccurate addresses, names, phone numbers, and even employment information removed from my report. First let me say how frustrating it was trying to use the automated service to try and get a hold of a customer service representative. All the automated menu allows you to do is to freeze/unfreeze or request your credit report. It AT NO POINT gives you a prompt to request to speak to an agent. To be honest I'm not quite sure how I was able to get one on the line after 20 minutes. I previously sent them a letter in XX/XX/XXXX requesting they do the same which went unanswered. 
When I finally did get someone on the line she refused to remove certain addresses because according to her other companies were reporting inaccurate addresses as my address on file. That is a violation of 15 USC 6801. This code states "" It is the policy of Congress that each financial institution has an affirmative and continuing obligation to respect the privacy of its customers and to protect the security and confidentiality of those customers ' nonpublic personal information. Moreover, they have a mandate to "" insure that consumer reporting agencies exercise their grave responsibilities with fairness, impartiality, and a respect for the consumer 's right to privacy. Furthermore, the Privacy Act of 1974 permits individuals to gain access to their records which are maintained in a system of records and to seek amendment of any incorrect or incomplete information contained in those records. ( 5 U.S.C. 522a, Public Law 93-579 ) In addition EXEPERIAN, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX never offered an annual opt out notice as is required by CFR 313.5. According to CFR 313.7 the notice provided should be "" clear and conspicuous. ''",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,NY,11209,None,Consent provided,Web,03/15/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8557917
