05/01/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"On XX/XX/XXXX, I purchased XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX from XXXX for {$2000.00} each, or {$4000.00} total. In return, I was supposed to receive my investment back plus a 15 % return in one year. So, I was due to receive {$4600.00} after they sold the beef from the cattle within 10 days after XX/XX/XXXX. I put the charge on my Chase XXXX XXXX XXXX card ( XXXX ). Please see attached for the contract and my credit card statement showing the purchase for {$4000.00}. 

XXXX was later found to be operating a fraudulent ponzi scheme. They have disconnected their phone number, and I never received my promised payout. Please see the latest update here : https : XXXX XXXX is now under federal investigation by the SEC with ongoing legal proceedings. 

XXXX XXXX is the attorney handling this case. 
XXXX XXXX I reached out to Chase twice about getting the {$4000.00} charge reversed because I never received the "" goods "" ( {$4600.00} ) I was promised. I am attaching their latest response from XX/XX/XXXX, XXXX. They denied my request saying the charge was valid. But that isn't the basis for my dispute. I am not disputing that I made the purchase. No one stole my credit card and made the purchase. I acknowledge that I made the {$4000.00} purchase. I am simply arguing that I never received anything from XXXX in return. 

The whole point of making a purchase through a credit card rather than paying cash is to receive some layer of protection from fraudulent companies such as XXXX. This ponzi scheme has involved thousands of victims and some of them have already received refunds on their credit cards from other issuers such as XXXX XXXX -- why won't Chase do the same to make their customers whole? 

Thank you for your help! 

XXXX XXXX",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11201,None,Consent provided,Web,05/01/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8903433
