04/10/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Other features, terms, or problems",Problem with rewards from credit card,"I XXXX contacted Chase regarding this issue on XX/XX/2023. 
The issue is not being able to redeem my points via Chase 's XXXX XXXX XXXX portal due to an "" Error with your membership ID ''. 
I have points ammounting to XXXX when redeemed towards XXXX purchases. 

Throughout the last XXXX months, I have been calling Chase and spending XXXX of hours on the phone attempting to solve this issue. 
In the beginning, I was repeatedly passed between Chase XXXX XXXX department and XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX department, both claiming the issue was not on their end. 
Eventually, I got representatives from both departments into a conference call where they spoke and came to the conclusion that Chase has to solve this issue on their end. 
Whether solving it involves them corresponding with an XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX team does not matter to me, as I am unable to get in touch with the correct people and do that work for them. 
Chase is the XXXX responsible for fulfilling their promised card benefit offering. 
After the conference call, I began to be able to get Chase to believe me that they had to deal with this issue and throughout the last XXXX months, I have been promised XXXX times that I would be contacted with a resolution in "" XXXX business days ''. 
After they did not call back the XXXX time, I was told on XX/XX/XXXX that nothing had actually happened and the representative had not contacted their XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. 
It has now been over a XXXX since the second promise of a call back in "" XXXX business days '' and I called again. I have been very busy so I was unable to call them with the frequency of the XXXX XXXXXXXX months lately. 
Today 's call informed me that no progress had been made since I was last promised a call back. 
I wanted details regarding this whole situation but representatives have not been willing to explain to a very granular degree, and I was told I would need to obtain a lawyer and subpoena Chase in order to request my account notes. 

As I had been making Chase aware, you can not redeem points towards purchases older than XXXX days, and my remaining valid purchases are dwindling and soon to be XXXX. 
I have been told a manual compensation will be possible, but I was given the same "" XXXX business days '' estimate XXXX  with no indication of any changes in the strategy for solving this issue. 
I no longer have any faith that I will be contacted back as a pattern of negligence has already been established.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,117XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/10/24,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8738983
