04/08/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"I received notification from XXXX XX/XX/2024 that my credit score dropped drastically, XXXX points. I reveiwed the information on XXXX and it stated that my student loans had increased. I called XXXX the loan carrier, because I am in an IDR until XX/XX/2024. I am not sure why all of a sudden I would have negative information being posted to the credit bureaus. I have not had anything like this happen in the past with my student loans. I spoke with a representative with XXXX and she stated they don't have any control over what the credit bureaus do with my credit score. I tried to explain it was because of the information XXXX provided them. I filed a disupte with XXXX. That did not make a difference, in fact I had to call XXXX a second time because they didn't do anything with my complaint. I called XXXX back XXXX explaining again that the way they are reporting my status is affecting my credit score. Today I received notification from Equifax that my credit score dropped XXXX points due to my student loan has increased. I called XXXX today XXXX and wanted to speak with a supervisor. After spekaing with a representative and being put on hold my call was disconnected. I called XXXX back and spoke with a representative that was going to escalate the issue. I verified with the representaive, being in and IDR should not affect my credit score, my student loans will always be on my credit report, until paid off, but while in IDR that should not affect the score. I was turned down from a local bank for a business loan because of the reporting of my student loan. I have asked over and over that they please check into this issue of incorrect reporting to the credit bureaus. Today is the first time XXXX  representaive has sent my information on to someone who has the ability to see what is going on. This has had a negative impact on my situation on trying to open up my business. I have not been able to get lending due to the recent information being provided to all three credit bureaus.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,149XX,Servicemember,Consent provided,Web,04/08/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8725554
