03/26/24,Vehicle loan or lease,Lease,Problems at the end of the loan or lease,Problem extending the lease,"My lease is with Ally agreement # XXXX this was a 36 month lease and is due to be returned XX/XX/XXXX XXXX due to financial struggles i decided that it would be best for me to extend my lease vs leasing a new car based on the fact that payments have gone up on car from the time that i leased this current car. i am in the mortgage industry which has been struggling a great deal over the past 3 years and my income has suffered greatly. about 6 months or so back or more i contact Ally and they stated very clearly that they could extend my lease for up to 6 months and assured me that it would not be an issue. they stated that i needed to contact them 30 days prior to the lease coming due and that they would XXXX the extension. Per their request i reached out to them, XX/XX/XXXX and they took my request and confirmed that the lease extension should be granted without an issue. they mentioned that i needed to call them in XXXX business days to complete the process and that they would fax information to me to complete. Based on the information that Ally provided me 6 months ago and several times after i decided not to explore other options for a new car since i was assured that they would extend. i had several offers that i rejected based on my decision to extend. i followed up today XX/XX/26 to get the paper work that they said would be fourth coming and when i spoke with them they stated that they NO longer extend leases and that my request had been denied! this has now put me into a huge finical problem. i now only have 15 day to get a new car and i don't have the time or money to accomplish that. I then called back and they stated they changed their policy last week and cant help me. I told them i am going through financial hardship and they then said they would extend for 3 months, put me on hold and came back and said they changed their mind. They are misleading customers and putting people in very difficult situation with zero concern.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,ALLY FINANCIAL INC.,NY,11050,None,Consent provided,Web,03/26/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8631535
