04/05/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"To the CFPB, XXXX XXXX XXXX is filing a complaint against the credit agencies for discrepancies within my credit report of improper documentations.. 
According to Per 15 U.S. Code 1681 Congressional findings and statement of purpose ( a ) Accuracy and fairness of credit reporting The Congress makes the following findings : ( 1 ) The banking system is dependent upon fair and ACCURATE credit reporting. INACCURATE CREDIT REPORTS directly impair the efficiency of the banking system, and unfair credit reporting methods undermine the public confidence which is essential to the continued functioning of the banking system. 

The discrepancies starts with the credit agencies themselves : The Balances are different The Closed accounts are different The Inquiries ( 2yrs ) are different The discrepancies with XXXX  XXXX are : The Original Balance are different The Last payment dates are different The date that it was opened are different The discrepancies with XXXX XXXX XXXX are : The Original Balance is different The Last payment dates are different The dates that the credit was opened are different The status of the account on certain dates are different The discrepancy with XXXX XXXX XXXX  are : The open dates are different I tried reaching out to XXXX XXXX Equifax XXXX & XXXX to clarify these issues but the representatives just kept saying they can only see their reports of my credit with them. These credit agencies SUPPOSE to have the same reports through & through no differences since they are collecting the information from the same exact source which is the companies that are providing the information, if the wavers at any moment how is the information XXXX.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11691,None,Consent provided,Web,04/05/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8693947
