10/03/23,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Investigation took more than 30 days,"I sent a letter regarding inaccurate and unknown things on my credit report. To this day over 30 days later I have not received a response yet. I feel like I'm being taken advantage of and being ignored of my disputes. Section 611 ( a ), it is plainly stated that a failure to investigate these items within 30 days gives a reason to immediately remove those items from my credit report it has been over 30 days so they should be deleted promptly. I demand these accounts be deleted immediately or I will file for litigation due to the stress you caused me. My information was also impacted by the XXXX, XXXX and Transunion data breach and may have got into the hands of the wrong person.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,10001,None,Consent provided,Web,10/03/23,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,7633563
04/23/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Problem with a lender or other company charging your account,Transaction was not authorized,"Made a purchase on XX/XX/23 with XXXX XXXX  for my XXXX birthday dress. Less than XXXX hours after the order was placed I emailed to confirm I would receive the order by XXXX. I was told orders take XXXX to produce so it would not arrive in time. I asked could I cancel the order and was told that I could not cancel because the order was already in production but I could request to change to a ready to ship item. 

I couldn't understand how I could not cancel since it was in production but I could change for a different product and stated that in an email to the merchant. At that point, the merchant stopped responding to me. 

XXXX days later I received a package but it was not the item I ordered nor did it fit. 

I contacted the merchant via phone since they stopped responding to my emails requesting a refund and to return the item I received that I did not purchase and was told someone would get back to me but no one ever did. 

I submitted a dispute claim with Citibank. The merchant responded well after 90 days later and provided shipping information to Citibank and Citibank closed my dispute in favor of the merchant. 

I don't understand how that's possible. The purchase amount was {$280.00} and I did not receive the item I ordered. I had to order a completely different dress overnighted from a different vendor. I want a refund. 

I still have the item snet to me in the packaging it was received in. I will return it happily.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,11432,None,Consent provided,Web,04/23/24,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8840137
08/03/23,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"This letter serves as a formal complaint that you are reporting inaccurate and incomplete information on my credit report notation of the following late payments ( 2 ) is inaccurate. Please investigate and verify that all data for this account is reporting accurately including every notation, date and balance whether reported or not { XXXX XXXX Credit Card with Account # XXXX } I also respectfully request to be provided specific proof that theses alleged late payments ( 2 ) were in fact late. I request to see all statements and payments transaction records from the you as the creditor that would proof that my payment was not submitted on time. It is my understanding that I must verify these items with the reporting creditor ( XXXX XXXX Credit Card ) for accuracy. If they are unable to provided that proof, or if lacking proof of these payments being late, please update my payment history to PAANL status ( Paid As Agreed Never Late ) according to consumer protection laws. 

In addition in accordance to the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) Code 15 USC 1666B A creditor may not treat a payment on a credit card account under an open end consumer credit plan as late for any purpose, unless the creditor has adopted reasonable procedures designed to ensure that each periodic statement including the information required by section 1637 ( b ) of this title is mailed or delivered to the consumer not later than 21 days before the payment due date.

Furthermore as per the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) Code 15 USC 1681 Section 602 states There is a need to insure that consumer reporting agencies exercise their grave responsibilities with fairness, impartiality, and a respect for the consumers right to privacy. Where is my right to privacy, when your reporting to the credit bureaus about alleged late payments?

Over and above that, by means of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) Code 15 USC 1681a ( 2 ) ( B ) report containing information solely as to transactions or experiences between the consumer and the person making the report ;",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11226,None,Consent provided,Web,08/03/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,7346909
