05/28/24,Debt collection,Telecommunications debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt was result of identity theft,I was a victim of Identity theft close to 2 years ago. I got a message that I had an account with XXXX XXXX XXXX. I called them at the time and advised that I made no such account and that my identity was stolen. I had sent them a Dispute letter to the company for XXXX as well as a FTC notice to Furnishers as per the FTC ( reference number available it needed ). I have called multiple times to XXXX XXXX XXXX and got confirmation of no account however I was called by a debt collector ( Sunrise Credit Services ) about a debt. I have not received any paperwork and a single call and as such I thought this was a scam. I went on vacation and came back to find that my credit score has dropped more then XXXX pts due to this collection. I have placed a freeze on all credit accounts. I would like to have this removed and for Sunrise to send by certified mail the identity theft documentation and demand that the collectors retract their reports to credit bureau 's.,Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"SUNRISE CREDIT SERVICES, INC",NY,145XX,None,Consent provided,Web,05/28/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9118818
