03/23/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Funds not handled or disbursed as instructed,"In XXXX of XXXX, my wife was involved in a pig butchering scam. We had a joint account at Bank of America in XXXX, California, outside of XXXX XXXX. On 4 dates, she had made transfers for a total of {$190000.00} to a crypto account, that was then transferred to the criminals who stole the money. They originally contacted her via XXXX. Once I found out the money was stolen, I went with my wife to BOA to address the situation. They stated that she had made the transfers, that I had no right to be contacted about the wire transfers, and that they would look into it. I signed a statement, which reviewing it now, is a complete lie. On that statement, it said that I had made the transfers. I was not the person going to the bank making the wire transfers. That was my wife, and I had no knowledge. The manager there wouldn't give me her name as if she was the manager of a XXXX 's. Mind you, the treasury helped support banks like this to the tune of billions of dollars in 2008, and BOA was able to buy a mortgage company at a fraction of their price. A few months later, I get a statement from BOA saying they couldn't recover the funds. XXXX transfer ( $ XXXX on XXXX XXXX, XXXX ) she made from the Bank of America to XXXX to buy XXXX. XXXX transfer ( XXXX XXXX, XXXX ( $ XXXX ) ) to XXXX to buy XXXX. Third transfer, XXXX XXXX, XXXX ( $ XXXX ) to XXXX to buy XXXX, and fourth transfer, XXXX XXXX, XXXX ( $ XXXX ) to XXXX to buy XXXX. 

When we reported this to the sheriff at XXXX, and provided him with all the information, he never even filed a report because he said there was nothing he could do. 

I would like to know this : Were these transfers, because of their amounts and short time period, ever reported as required of these types of banks by law? I want my money back, and I want my government to shut down all crypto exchanges. Do your job.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION",NY,137XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/23/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8610155
