03/14/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"I made a purchase for a hotel reservation for {$1500.00} in XX/XX/2023. Because of a fraudulent call, I thought this charge was paid to the wrong people and I asked that it be reversed. Discover reversed it. Upon realizing that the call I received was a part of a scam, I asked Discover to send the money back. Discover said that they will withdraw the claim and send the money back. It was reposted onto my account in early XX/XX/2023, but the hotel never received the money. I followed up continuously for a month, and neither party ( Discover or the hotel ) budged on their positions. Around XX/XX/2023, I made other accommodations. My original hotel reservation was canceled because the balance was never met, despite Discover saying they received the money AND it being posted on my account. 

I've called Discover several times to dispute this charge. I've sent in invoices, payment reminders, and balance due statements from the hotel to prove they didn't receive the money. I've also sent in proof that I didn't stay there. They have said it was insufficient evidence and refuse to reverse the charge on my card. Essentially, they are making me pay for something when the money never made it there. I understand the process has been confusing, but I don't see why I should have to pay if the payment was never fulfilled. In the documents below, I will include everything I sent Discover : a payment reminder email, invoice of my bill being unpaid, invoice of my canceled reservation, a website page proving my balance was not met with the exact same amount that discover posted on my account, the payment history on the hotel website showing that they never received the money. Additionally, I can include proof that I stayed somewhere else during the window of the dates entirely, to prove that I can not be in two places at once. 

Thank you for reading and I hope you can help me. I very much would not like to pay {$1500.00} for a reservation that was canceled.",None,DISCOVER BANK,NY,11550,None,Consent provided,Web,03/14/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8536855
