04/03/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"Dear Sir or Madam, I am writing to dispute the accuracy of information reported on my credit file regarding an account with XXXX XXXX. I believe that the information reported by [ Equifax/XXXX ] is inaccurate and does not reflect my payment history accurately. Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), I am requesting a thorough investigation into this matter to ensure that my credit report reflects only accurate and complete information. 

Account Information for Dispute : Creditor Name : XXXX XXXX ( Installment ) Account Number : XXXX ( Please adjust with the last four digits as reported ) Reported by : Equifax and XXXX Issues : Payment Status Inconsistencies : Equifax reports "" Pays account as agreed, '' while XXXX states "" Paid account/was 30 days past due date. '' This discrepancy may unfairly affect my credit score. 
Delinquency Reports : Both Equifax and XXXX list a 30 days late payment in XX/XX/year>. If this is incorrect or if there are extenuating circumstances that led to this mark, such as errors in reporting or miscommunication, it should be investigated and corrected. 
XXXX XXXX : The account closure date is only reported by Equifax, not XXXX. Consistent reporting across all bureaus is essential for accuracy. 
Account XXXX : There is missing information across the bureaus, including the closed date by XXXX and nearly all details by XXXX. This lack of consistency XXXX present an incomplete picture of my credit history. 
I have attached documents that support my position and request that the following actions be taken : Verify all information regarding the XXXX XXXX account with the creditor. 
Correct any inaccuracies found, especially regarding payment history and account statuses. 
Update my credit report to reflect accurate and consistent information across all bureaus. 
Provide me with a written summary of your investigation and the outcome. 
Please complete this investigation within the 30-day period as mandated by the FCRA. I appreciate your attention to this matter and expect your prompt response. 

Sincerely,",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10465,None,Consent provided,Web,04/03/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8676980
