06/20/24,Debt collection,Credit card debt,Communication tactics,"You told them to stop contacting you, but they keep trying","Hi, Earlier today I filed a complaint with the CPFB, # XXXX Today at XXXX XXXX  EST I received a call from XXXX. The person on the phone said her name was XXXX, that she was with the JP Morgan Executive Office, and had to verify some information with regards to the complaint I just filed. 

I told her it was not a good time, my wife was sick and I was watching my son. She insisted and said "" it will only take a minute. '' She then asked me for personally identifiable information like my birth date, address, etc. 

I informed her I do not give out personally identifiable information ( PII ) to random people who call me. Ironically part of my original complaint was that random people were asking me for PII. 

It should be made clear to JPM that no one is under any obligation to provide PII to someone who calls them. Indeed given the number of scammers out there, they should not be requesting this.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,125XX,None,Consent provided,Web,06/20/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9306195
04/14/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"ACCOUNT NAME/NUMBER : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX {$31000.00} Dear TO WHOM IT MAY CONCERN, I am writing to dispute the presence of certain charge offs on my credit report. I believe that these charge offs have been reported in violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and the Metro 2 compliancy requirements.

Specifically, I believe that the information reported by your agency regarding these charge offs is inaccurate, incomplete, and misleading. As a result, my credit score has been unfairly impacted and I have suffered damages as a result.

Under the FCRA, it is your responsibility to ensure that all information reported to credit bureaus is accurate and up-to-date. Additionally, the Metro 2 compliance guidelines outline specific reporting requirements for charged off accounts, including the requirement to report the date of first delinquency and the date of charge off. 
Based on my own records, I believe that the information reported by your agency is incorrect and in violation of these guidelines. I have attached copies of my records to this letter for your review. 
I am requesting that you investigate this matter and correct any inaccurate or incomplete information in my credit report. 
Additionally, I am requesting that you provide me with a copy of the investigation results and any updates made to my credit report as a result of your investigation. 
Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter. 

