03/19/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Statement Regarding Unauthorized Sharing of Personal Information To Whom It May Concern, I am writing to address a concerning issue regarding the unauthorized sharing of my personal information by XXXXXXXX XXXX  on my consumer report. This unauthorized sharing of information has come to my attention and raises serious concerns regarding the protection of my privacy rights and compliance with applicable laws and regulations. 

XXXX XXXX XXXX actions in sharing my personal information on my consumer report without my authorization are in direct violation of several laws and regulations designed to safeguard consumer privacy and ensure fair credit reporting practices. Specifically, these actions may contravene the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act ( GLBA ), Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) regulations, and potentially state privacy laws. 

The FCRA mandates the accuracy, fairness, and privacy of consumer credit reports, including the permissible purposes for accessing and sharing consumer information. The unauthorized sharing of my personal information by XXXXXXXX XXXX  may violate the FCRA 's provisions related to permissible purposes and the accuracy of consumer reports. 

Similarly, the XXXX requires financial institutions to protect the privacy and security of customers ' nonpublic personal information. XXXX XXXX XXXX unauthorized sharing of my information may breach the XXXX 's privacy requirements and regulatory standards set forth by the CFPB. 

Additionally, state privacy laws may provide further protections for consumer privacy rights and impose additional requirements on the collection, use, and sharing of personal information. 

I demand immediate action to address this unauthorized sharing of my personal information by XXXX XXXX and to rectify any inaccuracies or violations of my privacy rights on my consumer report. Furthermore, I expect XXXX XXXX to implement measures to prevent similar unauthorized sharing of personal information in the future and to comply fully with all applicable laws and regulations governing consumer privacy and fair credit reporting practices. 

Please provide confirmation once the necessary actions have been taken to address this matter and ensure the accuracy and privacy of my consumer report. 

Sincerely, XXXX",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,NY,109XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/19/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8578907
