03/13/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Credit inquiries on your report that you don't recognize,"I am writing to formally dispute and bring attention to the inaccuracies present in my consumer credit report. Listed below are fraudulent/inaccurate and or unauthorized hard inquiries on my credit report that I will like to be thoroughly investigated and removed. 

XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  XX/XX/XXXX It has come to my attention, through a thorough review of my Fair Credit Report, that there are hard inquiries listed on my report that I believe to be fraudulent and inaccurately attributed to my credit profile. I demand a comprehensive and rigorous investigation by the credit buries to substantiate the validity of each hard inquiry they have recorded. Furthermore I request that the credit bureaus provide documented proof for any hard inquiry deemed to be accurate. I am committed to maintaining the accuracy and integrity of my credit report, and it is imperative that these discrepancies are rectified promptly. Your cooperation in conducting a thorough investigation and providing a clear documentation will be instrumental in resolving this matter promptly and ensuring the veracity of my credit report. Please investigate and remove these hard inquiries from my credit report.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10562,None,Consent provided,Web,03/13/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8541929
03/13/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"If you persist in apparent disregard, noncompliance, or deficiency of substantial, satisfying, and/or otherwise evident proof of compliant reporting practices, I must warn you that this letter serves as my official notice prior to my likely decision to petition a civil court nearest me for a writ of review related to the aforementioned issues I suspect. Please be advised that I am the injured consumer of your unproven or inadequate reporting practices. As such, I am contesting the assumed, but actually very conditional, reporting privileges for any and all of your claims challenged within this consumer complaint. This declaration calls for your demonstration of authoritative, certifiable, compliant, lawful reporting that assuredly adheres to no less than the mandatory state and federal reporting mandates and statutes. My demand for your fastidious scrutiny shall categorically include, but not be limited to, your adherence to accords cited within the FCBA, FCRA, ECOA, as well as any and all applicable laws within my state, proven to be commodiously ample for illustrating your adequate statutory reporting occurred exactly as related to any claim purported by you in my report ( s ). Particularly concerning to me is if any or all of your claim 's aspects are alleged yet display potential deficiency, having plausible deviations from your obligatory utilized industry standards for legal, fair, and ethical reporting and did so with respect to a comme il faut status. Incontestably, your compulsion should be that of certifiable conformity to the Metro 2 Data-filled Field Formatted Reporting Standards, per CDIA! 

I have recently obtained copies of my personal consumer credit report ( s ) and have discovered questionable and/or inadequately verified data in my file at your company 's office ( s ), as reported on my reviewed files. I am concerned that this information may have been inadvertently or intentionally re-added to my credit report profile by your company 's office ( s ) following its earlier removal from reporting, without issuing the requisite 5- day notice to me as mandated by reporting regulations that you MUST comply with.

As per the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), any item of reporting that has been previously removed can not be reinserted onto any consumer 's credit report profile without written notice from at least the accepting credit reporting agency ( ies ) /repository ( ies ) directly to me, the injured consumer, within five ( 5 ) business days of the alleged date of reinsertion. I want to inform you that I have not yet received any such notice or confirmation of the accuracy and completeness of your reported claim ( s ). 

Listed below are the Accounts and Inquiries that are being challenged : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10452,None,Consent provided,Web,03/13/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8542131
03/13/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"As a vigilant guardian of my own privacy, I invoke the power vested in me by the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ) to address the violations concerning my personal information. The FCRA, under 15 U.S.C. 1681 section 602 ( a ), mandates consumer reporting agencies to handle their significant responsibilities with fairness, impartiality, and respect for my right to privacy. Equifax and XXXX, as consumer reporting agencies, must heed this directive. I assert my right to ensure that my private information remains confidential, a right that is fortified by 15 U.S.C. 6801, which clearly states that financial institutions have an ongoing obligation to honor the privacy of their customers. The entity that furnishes information to credit agencies falls under this definition and thus, is bound by these laws. Furthermore, 15 U.S.C. 1681 section 604 ( a ) ( 2 ) specifies that a consumer reporting agency may furnish a report only with my written consent, which neither Equifax, XXXX, XXXX nor the furnisher of information has obtained from me. I hereby revoke any form of consent previously granted, whether verbal, non-verbal, written, implied, or otherwise. The law is clear in 15 U.S.C. 6802 ( b ) that a financial institution can not disclose my nonpublic personal information to a nonaffiliated third party without informing me of my right to nondisclosure, a right that was never presented to me. Moreover, 15 U.S.C. 1681C ( a ) ( 5 ) prohibits the reporting of any adverse information older than seven years, which includes the account in question. This is a violation of my legal rights, as there is no permission granted on my part for such reporting. The accuracy of information is paramount, as stated in 15 U.S.C. 1681s2 ( A ) ( 1 ) ( A ), which forbids the furnishing of information to consumer reporting agencies if it is known or suspected to be inaccurate. Equifax and XXXX failure to maintain reasonable procedures, as required by 15 U.S.C. 1681e, to prevent such violations further compounds the issue. Lastly, in accordance with 12 CFR 1016.7, I exercise my right to opt out of your reporting services at this time. My privacy is not a commodity for trade, and I demand the respect and confidentiality that is rightfully mine. Please be advised that this notice of my rights has been issued to you multiple times and has been met with disregard. This persistent neglect is not only disrespectful but also a clear breach of the legal obligations outlined above. I insist on immediate compliance with these regulations, and any further inaction will be met with the necessary legal recourse to protect my rights.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10462,None,Consent provided,Web,03/13/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8542138
