04/09/24,Debt collection,Private student loan debt,Written notification about debt,Didn't receive enough information to verify debt,"I have received a letter from Forster & Garbus LLP, a debt collector stating that I have to pay judgement due amount of {$42.00}, XXXX plus interest. They also sent a notice of garnishment from Marshal for total amount of {$63000.00}. They have been contacting my employer also. I do not know how they got judgment against me. I have not got any summon to appear in court. I took a student loan between the year XXXX from a private company to XXXX  XXXX  in XXXX XXXX. The company stopped paying the loan after one year and I could not pursue my study further. Probably, the loan company was closed or bankrupt. Because of incomplete study, I remained unemployed for many years. I do not remember the amount of loan, but it is far less than the debt collector asking for. In past, I received several letters from different debt collectors for asking different amount. I sent letters to few of them asking verification and copy of written agreement. I have not received any reply from them. I suspected inaccuracy and stopped responding the other debt collector afterward. I was afraid of scam. 
I would like the following information : 1. The name, address, amount, and account number used by the original creditor. The creditor contact address and phone number.

2. Provide verification and documentation. Provide copy of written agreement created my original requirement to pay. Provide promissory note with my signature.

3. State when the creditor claims this debt became due and when it became delinquent.

4. Have you made a determination that debt is within the statue of limitations and applicable to it? When the statute of limitations expires for this debt, and how you determined that?

5. Send me proof of summon with signature of the receiver. Proof of registered post by court.

6. A copy of the last billing statement sent to me by the original creditor.

The court judgement in favor of creditor is biased or based on misleading information supplied to court. The judgement is one sided favoring the creditor. You have all legal tools and access ; it does not mean that you suppress the weak and take advantage.

After receiving the above-mentioned information, I would like to make an informed decision about your claim. I would like involve regulatory authority and appeal in the court in this matter.

I shall be grateful for your favorable and helpful response.

Thank you. 
Sincerely, XXXX XXXX",None,Abrahamsen Gindin LLC,NY,10314,Older American,Consent provided,Web,04/11/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8721623
04/08/24,Debt collection,Private student loan debt,Written notification about debt,Didn't receive enough information to verify debt,"I have received a letter from XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, a debt collector stating that I have to pay judgement due amount of {$42.00}, XXXX plus interest. They also sent a notice of garnishment from XXXX for total amount of {$63000.00}. They have been contacting my employer also. I do not know how they got judgment against me. I took a student loan between the year XXXX from a private company to study medicine in XXXX XXXX. The company stopped paying the loan after one year and I could not pursue my study further. Probably, the loan company was closed or bankrupt. Because of incomplete study, I remained unemployed for many years. I do not remember the amount of loan, but it is less than the debt collector asking for. In past, I received several letters from different debt collectors for asking different amount. I sent letters to few of them asking verification and copy of written agreement. I have not received any reply. I suspected inaccuracy and stopped responding. I was afraid of scam. 
I have also received another debt collector, Portnoy Schenck, LLC. letter in same week mentioning the judgement against me for {$16000.00} for the same above-mentioned loan. I got confused and suspected irregularities. Now this debt collector blocked my bank account. I have not received any registered post summon from the court for this case. 
The debt collector has to determine that debt is within the statue of limitations. They should provide copies of agreement and signed promissory note. How I will know the debt collector is authorized and not misleading. How Court can deliver one sided decision? How come two debt collectors can ask for the amount for the same loan?

Later, I took Federal loan and paying the amount in installments regularly. 
I am mentally very disturbed and does not know what to do. My bank amount is blocked. I, therefore, request please help me. I am enclosing the letters from debt collectors and copy of my letter to one of them. 
Thank you. 

XXXX XXXX",None,"Portnoy Schneck, L.L.C.",NY,10314,Older American,Consent provided,Web,04/08/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8716706
