03/18/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"RE : You Violated the United States Code Law ( TILA 15 U.S. Code 1666 ( b ) billing error ) Recently I checked my credit report and noticed multiple billing errors under 15 U.S.

Code 1666 ( b ) billing error -The creditor 's mistake in not accurately showing a payment or credit that the consumer made on their account statement.

-A billing error under the Fair Credit Billing Act ( FCRA ) that is caused by a creditor 's computational or accounting mistake. 
Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), creditors are required to provide consumers with at least 21 days ' notice before reporting a late payment. Since I did not receive this notice, I am demanding to see hard evidence from the creditor 's bank account that I did not make the required payment and that the late payment was in error. 
I request that the following items on my credit report be updated to reflect that they were paid as agreed. 
1. This late payment status is irrelevant XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX This account is fully satisfied. Please update this account immediately 2. This late payment status is irrelevant XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  The late payment in the past was settled. I'm currently on time with my payments. Please update this account immediately 3. This late payment status is irrelevant XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX This account is inaccurate. Please update this account immediately PLEASE SEE THE PROOF ATTACHED TO THIS LETTER Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), I am entitled to have these accounts on this letter updated immediately. If you do not comply, I will file a lawsuit in small claims court in my city and state seeking monetary damages for your violation of my rights. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX XXXX",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11235,None,Consent provided,Web,03/18/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8568766
