03/05/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Public record information inaccurate,"XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, NY XXXX XXXX XX/XX/year> Consumer Financial Protection Bureau XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Washington, DC XXXX Subject : Complaint Against Experian and XXXX for Unauthorized Reporting of Bankruptcy Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, I am writing to file a formal complaint against Experian and XXXX violation of my consumer rights under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). Specifically, my complaint is regarding the unauthorized reporting of bankruptcy on my consumer credit report and/or credit file, which I did not consent to nor was I properly notified about. 

Violation Details : It came to my attention that both Experian and XXXX have listed a bankruptcy on my consumer credit reports. This information is not only wrongful but was also reported without my explicit consent or prior notification. This action has significantly and negatively affected my credit score, making it difficult for me to obtain credit, and it has caused me undue stress and financial hardship. 

Previous Attempts to Resolve : I have previously attempted to resolve this matter directly with Experian and XXXX, but to no avail the issue was not resolved Despite my efforts, the issue remains unresolved, and this information is still present on my credit reports. 

Requested Resolution : I respectfully request the CFPB to intervene and facilitate the removal of the bankruptcy information from my credit reports maintained by Experian and XXXX. Additionally, I seek assurance that such errors will not recur in the future and request to be informed of the steps taken by these credit reporting agencies to correct this issue. 

I trust that the CFPB will take my complaint seriously and assist me in rectifying this situation as swiftly as possible. I look forward to your response and am hopeful for a favorable resolution. 

Thank you for your attention to this matter. 

