03/07/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, NY XXXX XXXX XX/XX/2024 Consumer Financial Protection Bureau 1700 G Street NW Washington, DC 20552 Subject : Formal Complaint Against Experian, XXXX, XXXX, and XXXX for Unauthorized Reporting of Bankruptcy Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, I am reaching out to file a formal complaint against Experian, XXXX, XXXX, and XXXX for severe violations of my consumer rights as protected under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and any other relevant consumer protection laws. Specifically, the unauthorized reporting of bankruptcies on my consumer credit reports and/or credit file by these agencies. 

Detailed Complaint : Without my consent and without any prior notification, these credit reporting agencies have listed bankruptcy information on my consumer credit reports. This erroneous information has not only damaged my creditworthiness but has also led to substantial personal and financial distress. The inaccuracies reported by these agencies have resulted in denials of credit, severely impacting my ability to purchase a car and a house. Moreover, the public reporting of such sensitive personal financial information without my consent constitutes a significant violation of my privacy. 

Attempts to Resolve the Issue : Despite my efforts to contact Experian, XXXX, XXXX, and XXXX to correct this misinformation, my attempts have been unsuccessful, and the bankruptcy information remains on my reports. The lack of response and resolution from these agencies has only compounded my stress and mental anguish. 

Sought Resolution : Immediate removal of the bankruptcy information from my credit reports and credit file across all mentioned credit reporting agencies. 
A formal investigation into how this breach of my consumer rights occurred and steps taken to prevent future occurrences. 
Compensation for the undue stress, mental anguish, and financial losses incurred due to the wrongful reporting of bankruptcy information and the resulting denials of credit. 
A written apology from each of the credit reporting agencies for the mishandling of my personal information and the distress it has caused. 

I implore the CFPB to take immediate action on my behalf to address these violations of my consumer rights. Your assistance in this matter is not only crucial for rectifying my personal credit history but also serves as a deterrent against the careless handling of consumer information by credit reporting agencies. 

Thank you for your attention to this urgent matter. I look forward to a swift and favorable resolution. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,NY,11434,None,Consent provided,Web,03/22/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8494565
