04/16/24,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",Domestic (US) money transfer,Money was not available when promised,None,"My name is XXXX XXXX. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, XXXX initiated a {$22000.00} wire transfer from my XXXX account under my full name, XXXX XXXX, with my address XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX, NY XXXX, to my Chase account under my name. 

During the wire mistakenly, we missed a number, and the wire ended up in another person 's account who is deceased. 

On XX/XX/XXXX as I still hadn't received the transfer the Chase representative had already promised on the recorded line that the wire would return to the source within a couple of days. 

When I followed up on this matter, Chase then alerted me that I should call a XXXX attorney without any explanation of what the attorney should do or what the issue was that I couldn't retrieve my {$22000.00}. 

In the meantime, I'm missing the {$22000.00}, which I was depending on to cover my XXXX XXXX XXXX 's medical expenses after her Stage XXXX XXXX diagnosis. 

It has come to my attention that I'm protected by the Electronic Fund Transfer Act of 1978 ( EFTA ) ( 15 U.S.C. 1693 et seq. ), which was enacted to protect account holders for these situations. It is my understanding that the bank has a responsibility as a financial service to assist in resolving problems for their customers.

I hope you can assist me in rectifying this issue.

Thank you in advance for your assistance.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,XXXXX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/16/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8780992
