04/15/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I have recently obtained copies of my personal consumer credit report ( s ) and have discovered questionable and/or inadequately verified data in my file at your company 's office ( s ), as reported on my reviewed files. I am concerned that this information may have been inadvertently or intentionally re-added to my credit report profile by your company 's office ( s ) following its earlier removal from reporting, without issuing the requisite 5-day notice to me as mandated by reporting regulations that you MUST comply with.

As per the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), any item of reporting that has been previously removed can not be reinserted onto any consumer 's credit report profile without written notice from at least the accepting credit reporting agency ( ies ) /repository ( ies ) directly to me, the injured consumer, within five ( 5 ) business days of the alleged date of reinsertion. I want to inform you that I have not yet received any such notice or confirmation of the accuracy and completeness of your reported claim ( s ). 

Listed below are the Personal Information that are being challenged Incorrect Name : - XXXX XXXX XXXX Incorrect Name : - XXXX XXXX XXXX Employer - XXXX XXXX  Incorrect Previous Address : - XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX Listed below are the Accounts/Collections that are being challenged XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX Listed below are the Collections that are being challenged XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Listed below are the Inquiries that are being challenged XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Your agency is in breach of the law! 
Under 15 U.S.C. 1681 Section 602 A, I am entitled to privacy. According to 15 U.S.C. 1681 Section 604 A ( 2 ), a consumer reporting agency is prohibited from providing an account without my explicit written permission. Additionally, 15 U.S.C. 1681c ( a ) ( 5 ) stipulates that no consumer reporting agency may include in a consumer report any negative information, other than criminal convictions, that predates the report by more than seven years. Finally, 15 U.S.C. 1681s-2 ( A ) ( 1 ) mandates that no person should provide information about a consumer to a consumer reporting agency if they know or should reasonably suspect that the information is inaccurate.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10456,None,Consent provided,Web,04/15/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8777815
