04/14/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"ACCOUNT NAME/NUMBER : XXXX XXXX AMOUNT XXXX {$31000.00} Dear TO WHOM IT MAY CONCERN, I am writing to dispute the presence of certain charge offs on my credit report. I believe that these charge offs have been reported in violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and the XXXX XXXX compliancy requirements. 
Specifically, I believe that the information reported by your agency regarding these charge offs is inaccurate, incomplete, and misleading. As a result, my credit score has been unfairly impacted and I have suffered damages as a result. 
Under the FCRA, it is your responsibility to ensure that all information reported to credit bureaus is accurate and up-to-date. Additionally, the XXXX XXXX compliance guidelines outline specific reporting requirements for charged off accounts, including the requirement to report the date of first delinquency and the date of charge off. 
Based on my own records, I believe that the information reported by your agency is incorrect and in violation of these guidelines. I have attached copies of my records to this letter for your review. 
I am requesting that you investigate this matter and correct any inaccurate or incomplete information in my credit report. 
Additionally, I am requesting that you provide me with a copy of the investigation results and any updates made to my credit report as a result of your investigation. 
Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX XXXX",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11435,None,Consent provided,Web,04/14/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8770072
