09/12/24,Student loan,Federal student loan servicing,Dealing with your lender or servicer,Received bad information about your loan,"I have called and emailed to formally express my dissatisfaction with the lack of accurate and timely responses and literal disregard from NelNet and XXXX regarding my student loan account. Despite multiple attempts to resolve my concerns, including several phone calls and emails, I have not received the correct information or the assistance I have been seeking. 

I have reached out several times to request clarification on the status of the court-ordered discharge of my loans. Each time, I have either received incorrect information or no follow-up at all. Many times when I follow the prompts when calling in the call just drops my call. This has caused unnecessary confusion and frustration, delaying my ability to manage my account effectively.",None,"Nelnet, Inc.",NY,142XX,None,Consent provided,Web,09/12/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,10105901
04/15/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"I am reminding you once again that you must remove any claims listed above or below that have not met the minimum criteria required for you to assume the privilege of reporting. If you fail to prove the undeniable facts of each allegation and adhere to the necessary reporting practices mandated by the XXXX 's Metro 2 Compliance standards, then I contest the reportability of any such claim. The XXXX 's XXXX stipulates that "" ANY DEVIATION FROM THESE STANDARDS JEOPARDIZES THE INTEGRITY OF THE DATA. '' Therefore, it is imperative that you accept my challenge to prove the accuracy and compliance of each claim. I demand that you remove any such claim immediately from reporting as I have requested. 

Below listed is the currently reported not yet proven valid nor demonstrated as being certifiably compliant reported allegation ( s ) of information that I mark as being in question. 

Listed below are the Personal Information that are being challenged Incorrect DOB : - XXXX Listed below are the Collections that are being challenged XXXX - XXXX Listed below are the Inquiries that are being challenged XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Your agency is in breach of the law! 
Under 15 U.S.C. 1681 Section 602 A, I am entitled to privacy. According to 15 U.S.C. 1681 Section 604 A ( 2 ), a consumer reporting agency is prohibited from providing an account without my explicit written permission. Additionally, 15 U.S.C. 1681c ( a ) ( 5 ) stipulates that no consumer reporting agency may include in a consumer report any negative information, other than criminal convictions, that predates the report by more than seven years. Finally, 15 U.S.C. 1681s-2 ( A ) ( 1 ) mandates that no person should provide information about a consumer to a consumer reporting agency if they know or should reasonably suspect that the information is inaccurate.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,117XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/15/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8778908
