04/11/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"I contacted XXXX about my loan. My credit report ( XXXX and Equifax ) indicated that I have a balance. I was told it was not updated in my credit report due to a suppression placed on my account. XXXX advice me that the Suppression on my account would be lifted in XXXX. I filed a Dispute XX/XX/XXXX with the credit bureaus that my account from XXXX was reported incorrectly. 

I contacted XXXX again after I didnt see any change and the results of my Dispute XX/XX/XXXX came back stating account was accurate. I spoke a XXXX representative who noted that I called previously. I was told that they are unable to remove the suppression until they get the okay to do so. When that will happen, I was told it will take a long time. They told me to contact the Department of Education. 

I contacted the Department of Education about my account with XXXX being in Suppression. I was told there must be a misunderstanding on XXXX part because my account was transferred to XXXX ( paid in full ). I went back into my credit reports and filed a new dispute XX/XX/XXXX. As of XX/XX/XXXX, it is still under investigation. 

Here is the timeline. My loans were transferred XX/XX/XXXX from XXXX to XXXX. XXXX reported on my credit report : XXXX, Equifax, XXXX Paid, Closed : was paid as agreed Balance {$0.00} Date closed XX/XX/XXXX Next, loan was transferred from XXXX to XXXX. XXXX reported on my credit report : XXXX and Equifax state Open/Never late, Balance of {$100000.00}, last reported XX/XX/XXXX. Last, XXXX was transferred from XXXX to XXXX. XXXX reported on my credit report : XXXX, Equifax, XXXX Paid, Closed : was paid as agreed Balance {$0.00} Date closed XX/XX/XXXX Loans forgiven XX/XX/XXXX XXXX I logged into the XXXX account. On my account it stated {$0.00} and closed. I provided screenshots of all my reports.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10552,None,Consent provided,Web,04/11/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8753752
