11/14/23,Student loan,Federal student loan servicing,Dealing with your lender or servicer,Trouble with how payments are being handled,"Ed Finacial Services continues to reject and return student loan payments. The company only accepts my loan payments once they are "" past due. '' Prior to the federal loan repayment period going into effect, I submitted a payment of {$1200.00} on XX/XX/2023 which was reversed by the company. I assumed this was due to the loan repayment period not going into effect so I ignored it. 

In XXXX, I made two attempts to pay back my student loans for the month of XXXX, and both attempts were rejected. 

I made an additional attempt to pay my loan on XX/XX/2023, which was also rejected. 

The company only accepted my payment once my loan was marked "" past due '' in XXXX. 

As shown in the attachment below, I am facing similar challenges in the month of XXXX. I should also note that while the company retroactively indicates the loans were reversed on the same day, I continued to monitor the payment status and each time the company indicated my payment was "" processing '' for several days after my payment attempt, leading me to believe the payment was en route. Additionally, following each attempt to pay my loans, the company sent me a "" payment confirmation notice '' via email. 

