03/26/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"On the XXXX XXXX XXXX the below/ attached letter was sent to all credit reporting agencies. 

I am writing as my final notice to XXXX TRANSUNION/ XXXX to remove the XXXX XXXX XXXX  Account XXXX from my Credit Report as the account has been closed and I am officially opting out of reporting the said account.

Per the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), I XXXX, a Federally Protected Consumer and natural person hereby revoke Any and Every Authorization, I the consumer may have given you knowingly or unknowingly, written or unwrtten, verbal or non- verbal per 15 USC 6802.

This act is in violation of the Privacy Act of 1974 and an invasion and intrusion to my privacy.

It is a fact that no account can be reported without my consent pursuant to 16 CFR 313. 

XXXX XXXX XXXX  has affirmed their position in reporting the account closed and have reportedly opened a request with the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) for a removal from my credit report with all Credit Agencies.

In addition to violationg 15 USC 6802, this act further violates 15 USC 1681b for permissible purposes under the law and will be reported to the appropriate authorities. 

If no action is taken within XXXX banking days, this letter will be uploaded to the CFPB website as communication evidence for further investigation. 

I look forward to a positive resolution on this matter.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,11003,None,Consent provided,Web,03/26/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8632129
