04/07/24,Debt collection,Other debt,Written notification about debt,Didn't receive notice of right to dispute,"XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX PXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX : Dispute of Debt and Request for Deletion from Consumer Report Dear Sir/Madam, I am writing to dispute the validity of a debt that has recently appeared on my consumer report, as well as to assert my rights under the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ) and the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). 

Upon reviewing my consumer report, I was surprised to find an entry regarding a debt that I have no knowledge of. I have not received any prior notification or communication regarding this alleged debt, nor did I have the opportunity to dispute it before it appeared on my consumer report. 

I want to emphasize that if you believe that proper notification was indeed provided to me, I kindly request that you furnish me with the CERTIFIED mail receipt that includes my signature, demonstrating that I received notification of this debt at least XXXX days prior to its appearance on my consumer report. As a consumer, I am aware of my rights under the FDCPA and FCRA, which include the right to be notified of any debt collection activity and the right to dispute any inaccuracies on my consumer report. 

If you are unable to provide a certified copy of my signature confirming receipt of proper notification within the specified timeframe, I demand the immediate deletion of this collection/charged off account from my consumer report. Failure to comply with this request will prompt me to take further action to rectify this matter. 

I expect a prompt response to this dispute and request within XXXX days, as stipulated by the FCRA. Please provide all correspondence to the email address listed XXXX. 

Thank you for your attention to this matter. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX",None,PORTFOLIO RECOVERY ASSOCIATES INC,NY,11210,None,Consent provided,Web,04/07/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8716014
