05/14/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Unable to get your credit report or credit score,Other problem getting your report or credit score,"My EQUIFAX XXXX score is not showing on XXXX correctly. 

Despite my actual credit score being XXXX, Equifax consistently reports it as XXXX, using the same XXXX XXXX model they claim to utilize. This discrepancy is not only concerning but also damaging to my financial well-being and opportunities. 

According to the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), consumers have the right to accurate credit reporting. Section 1681e of the FCRA mandates that consumer reporting agencies must follow reasonable procedures to ensure maximum possible accuracy of the information they report. Equifax 's failure to accurately reflect my creditworthiness violates this fundamental provision. 
Furthermore, Equifax 's actions may constitute a violation of other relevant credit codes and laws, including but not limited to : The Equal Credit Opportunity Act ( ECOA ), which prohibits discrimination in credit transactions based on factors such as race, color, religion, national origin, sex, marital status, age, or receipt of public assistance.

The Consumer Credit Reporting Reform Act of 1996, which requires consumer reporting agencies to provide consumers with free annual credit reports and to investigate and correct inaccurate information in a timely manner.

It is evident that Equifax 's persistent reporting of an incorrect credit score is not only negligent but also potentially discriminatory. By artificially deflating my credit score, Equifax is impeding my ability to access credit on fair terms, thus undermining my financial opportunities and potentially perpetuating cycles of economic disadvantage.

Despite assurances from Equifax agents that the issue would be resolved, no corrective action has been taken. This lack of accountability is unacceptable and necessitates intervention from regulatory authorities such as the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau.

I urge the Bureau to investigate this matter thoroughly and take appropriate enforcement action against Equifax to ensure compliance with the FCRA and other relevant credit laws. Additionally, I request that Equifax be compelled to promptly correct my credit report to reflect my true creditworthiness and provide appropriate compensation for any damages incurred as a result of their inaccurate reporting.

Thank you for your attention to this matter. I look forward to a swift and satisfactory resolution to this issue.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11554,Servicemember,Consent provided,Web,05/14/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8993464
