10/13/22,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Deposits and withdrawals,"In late on the afternoon of XX/XX/2022 I deposited a check ( via mobile app ) into my Chase account in the amount of {$89000.00}. 

The following morning on XX/XX/XXXX at approximately XXXX XXXX  I logged into my account and the entire check amount was made available immediately for use in my account. 

At that time I proceeded to make several transfers to other business accounts held with chase and a single wire transfer to another party in the amount of XXXX. 

At XXXX XXXX, after having made the funds available to me, Chase put a hold onto my account after the fact, This made the account in which I made the deposit to have a negative balance of XXXX and change. The accounts into which I transferred the funds, all owned by different legal entities however did show that the funds were still available. 

On or after XX/XX/XXXX, Chase proceeded to withdraw without authorization the funds from 3 other accounts, the original transfers were completely deleted as if they never occurred. The wire transfer is the only of the 4 transfers made on XX/XX/XXXX that remained in my transaction history. 


On the morning of XX/XX/XXXX I went into the chase branch, I told them that I was upset, and that nobody forced them to make the funds immediately available, but that once it was made available and the funds were transferred they couldnt take these funds out without authorization unrelated entities accounts, the banker asked if I had contact info from XXXX XXXX, the bank from where the check was issued, I shared it, the banker called XXXX XXXX and XXXX  confirmed that the check was paid from their end on XX/XX/XXXX. The banker said that he was lifting the hold and that it would hit my account in 2 hours. 

Today XX/XX/XXXX the funds are still not available. The issues are as follows : 1 ) the bank can not continue to hold the funds unless there is reasonable concerns that the funds wont be paid, in this case Chase had direct communication with XXXX XXXX and no such concern exists, they have chosen to hold the funds in violation of Federal Regulation CC. 

2 ) once the bank made the funds available, they had no right to remove funds from unrelated entities, although they were not forced to make the funds available in XX/XX/XXXX Chase on their own chose to do so, there is no provision in Federal regulation CC that allows a deposit to be reversed once its made available when there has not been any information indicating any fraud whatsoever. Regardless of the above, the other entities are not a party to the funds availability, once transfers were made these entities must be able to rely that funds deposited and made available in their accounts are actually there to stay, they have not made any check deposits and can not be made a party to the hold policy of another account holder.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11204,None,Consent provided,Web,10/13/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6084314
