04/13/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Problem using a debit or ATM card,"On XX/XX/2024 I made multiple ATM withdrawals from the XXXX located at XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX NY XXXX XXXX When I tried to make my fourth withdrawal of {$400.00} the machine did not disperse any money, nor was there any error code on the screen. I immediately let the cashier know about the issue and he assured me it's an issue they have been having and the ATM company was just there that morning working on it. He told me there's nothing he could do and my bank would know to return the funds since I didn't receive any money. After waiting quite some time for the money to be returned I contacted Chime bank to dispute the charge. It's already quite an inconvenience that you can only speak with them over the phone, no email or chat option available. I have a toddler and I'm currently XXXX XXXX XXXX so it's not so easy for me to get on the phone for long periods of time to speak with a bank. I filed a dispute with Chime and they assured me that they would take care of the issue and I'd receive a temporary credit by the XXXX of XXXX. On XXXX  XX/XX/XXXX I received an email stating my dispute was denied and that I'd have to call them for more information or to fight the denied dispute. Again more of an inconvenience for me. I can not spend all day long on the phone with these people just to get my money back that I never received. I submitted a copy of the atm receipt along with my dispute so there's no reason they shouldn't be able to see that the ATM had {$400.00} unaccounted for from that day.",None,Chime Financial Inc,NY,11967,None,Consent provided,Web,04/13/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8766846
