04/12/24,Checking or savings account,Savings account,Managing an account,Problem using a debit or ATM card,"On XX/XX/, 2024, from XXXX XXXX  to XXXX XXXX  ET, my husband and I went to the Chase ATM at XXXX XXXX in New York to deposit a total of {$2500.00} USD into our joint savings account. After inserting the money, we confirmed the amount is showing correctly on the ATM screen and opted to receive an email receipt before leaving the bank. Upon arriving home, we noticed that both the email receipt and our bank account reflected an incorrect amount showing only {$1500.00}, with {$1000.00} missing. We promptly contacted Chase Bank on the morning of Monday, XX/XX/ 2024, to report the discrepancy, and again on XX/XX/2024, but both attempts were declined. Chase 's Claims Department mentions they check and found no technical issue around the time when we arrived the ATM and also did not find extra {$1000.00}! We requested a recording of the ATM screen, but the support mentioned she did not guarantee a recording is available and that it's only shared with authorities. 

