09/18/23,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"In XXXX I cosigned two XXXX student loans for my granddaughter ONLY on the condition that the loan but deferred until her graduation year. which would have been XXXX. Which we both agreed would be the best option as she and I are low-income. Unfortunately, she had to drop out due to unprecedented circumstances during covid therefore the full amount she was approved for was not disbursed to the college. However, we did not receive an updated approval disclosure for either the loan of the adjusted amount owed or the adjusted Estimated Repayment Schedule and terms. Only notice stating that XXXX 's loans would go into repayment that same year. Nevertheless, from what I read from the Promissory note and Application I read, I ONLY gave the company ( XXXX XXXX Loans ) my permission to pull my credit to check my credibility and financial credit history. However, recently it has come to my attention that all XXXX credit bureaus ( XXXX, Equifax, and XXXX ) have been entering lots of inaccurate and false information including late payments pertaining to those loans on my credit report with my written consent. This violates USC Code 15 U.S.C 1682 a.1.a AND 15 U.S.C 1681 ( B ).",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10469,None,Consent provided,Web,09/18/23,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,7561602
