03/27/23,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",Mobile or digital wallet,Fraud or scam,None,"Albert.com  Alber the app in the XXXX  store is a scam app. They take money claiming to help you save money for rainy day funds claiming to help you with financial support. I have tried to contact Albert there is no phone number only email. In XXXX Albert  was taking money from my account without my full knowledge in XXXX when I saw an email about my account I re-downloaded the app and tried to withdraw my money from my account in the app. I no longer have the same bank account but I updated all my details as well as bank information. I was unsuccessful in withdrawing my money. I contacted Albert support with over 50+ emails of me sending proof from the previous bank, my current bank, my ID, and a picture of me holding my ID I sent all of this with videos showing that I was unsuccessful with every way to withdraw funds. I was told to contact them back when I have proof from my bank that I was the owner of the account. I sent them that proof. I waited 10 business days for the letter to get to me. Only to be told that I'm supposed to send my current bank statement not my old one like they ask few emails ago. I have sent them proof of my identity 3 times. The latest hoop I had to jump through was them saying it was because of my name on the account. I am unable to update to government name as they asked. No matter what it's another hoop or waiting for customer service to come up with a way to stall in giving my money. If you check the app store the first XXXX review warns people about the apps as well as XXXX XXXX search Albert scam and I'm not the only one. They take a rainy day fund sometimes without your full knowledge and make it impossible for you to take back your own funds.",Company believes complaint is the result of an isolated error,Albert Corporation,NY,11221,None,Consent provided,Web,03/27/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6755330
