04/04/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"I am writing to formally dispute the presence of a fraudulent account on my credit report, which is currently being reported by Equifax. Despite my earlier submission of a dispute letter and the required documentation to the Federal Trade Commission ( FTC ), as per your protocol, this account remains on my Equifax credit report. Upon discovering this fraudulent account, I contacted the associated bank, which has confirmed the fraudulent nature of the account and assured me of its removal from their records. Subsequently, the other major credit bureaus, namely XXXX and XXXX, have removed this account from their records after recognizing its fraudulent nature. 

