05/31/22,Vehicle loan or lease,Lease,Managing the loan or lease,Billing problem,"HYUNDAI MOTOR FINANCE FORMER ACCOUNT NO. XXXX I am charging HYUNDAI MOTOR FINANCE with LARCENY in the amount of {$2600.00}. This complaint relates to two payments I made one on XX/XX/2019 in the amount of {$950.00} and the second payment of {$1700.00}. I made these two payments in GOOD FAITH and, I thought each of these payments had been applied. 

At the end of the lease in XXXX, I requested a print out of my lease history agreement with HYUNDAI MOTOR Finance to review. I discovered these two payments were never applied to my lease agreement. I believe these two payments should have covered nine payments at {$340.00} per month. Because these two payments were never applied to my former lease account, I incurred further interest charges that, also, should be returned to me over the nine payments I made to get ahead on my car payments. 

When I complained to The Hyundai Customer Care Center, the customer service represent gave me a difficult time in stating if I had sent these two large payments in ; then, these payments were applied. I responded by stating to her these payments were on reflected and/or credited to my lease payment account. 

I, further, spoke to a dispute customer representative who stated to me that I should mailed the front and back of these two checks. I had given him all the required information : date, check number, amount. He could not find either payments doing a payment search on his computer. I mailed them OVERNIGHT to HYUNDAI MOTOR FINANCE CORPORATION/THE PROCESSING CENTER. 

I was informed by HYUNDAI MOTOR FINANCE/PROCESSING CENTER that both of these payments would be re-debited to my checking account. This information was stated to me in XXXX. As a follow up, I kept calling HYUNDAI MOTOR FINANCE to state I had not seen these two payments re-debited to my checking account. 

Now, HYUNDAI MOTOR FINANCEXXXXPROCESSING CENTER is stating that it had re-debited the two payments to my checking account in XXXX. As of this date, I continue to wait for my overpayments that were never applied to my former account and have never been re-debited to my checking account. 

UNDER THE PAINS AND PENALTIES OF PERJURY, my bank, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, can confirm these two payments were never, ever re-debited to my checking account with them.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,HYUNDAI CAPITAL AMERICA,NY,128XX,Older American,Consent provided,Web,06/14/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5616990
