05/19/22,Credit card or prepaid card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem when making payments,Problem during payment process,"Hello- For the last XXXX years, I have tried to update the checking account on file that my Chase Credit Card charges in automatic billing. I no longer store funds in the checking account on file so each time Chase processes a credit card charge, the checking account on file becomes overdrawn and I'm hit with an overdraw fee of {$35.00} by the bank with which I have checking account ( not Chase. ) I am also assessed fees of varying degrees by Chase for being late on my monthly payment. I have tried to call several times over the past XXXX years to resolve this, and have tried to resolve it online. Chase support agents have not been able to update the checking account on file, claiming only I can do that on my online XXXX account. I have explained to them that I try to do so but the "" Manage '' button for automatic billing does not work on my account, and therefore I am unable to make the update. I have asked to disenroll in automatic billing instead which they have failed to complete and which I am unable to do within the XXXX  application. They further claim that I do not have any other checking accounts connected to my Chase account, even though I pay from another valid checking account every single month. I don't enter the info for that account from scratch each time I pay. The account is in fact stored as my default manual payment option when I manually pay my credit card on the XXXX application. Despite that, they claim the account is not connected. This dilemma has cost me hundreds in overdraft and late payment fees and may have impacted my credit. I am at my whits end for resolving this as each time I call, I'm cycled through a circle of agents, none of whom believes a solution to my problem exists.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,10002,Servicemember,Consent provided,Web,05/19/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5582945
