08/09/23,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Problem with a credit reporting company's investigation into an existing problem,Investigation took more than 30 days,"On XX/XX/2023, Experian fraudulently reported that a vehicle, which I did not own, was repossessed. The facts are completely in error, and the credit reporting companies have used my name and information for commercial purposes without my consent. 

I have attempted to resolve this matter, and as of this date, the credit bureaus have either not responded, or they have intentionally refused to provide any documentation to refute my claim, or show proof that my claim is without merit. 

I am prejudiced by this entry, as it is fraudulent, and no company or credit bureaus seems willing to correct their errors of fact. This matter is now more than seven years old and they are still reporting misleading and erroneous fraudulent information. As a result, my car loan interest rate is at an exuberant rate which I need in order to continue to earn a living. I am close to homelessness where I have to choose to find a closer job. 
In accordance with the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( Experian ), Acct No. ( XXXX ), has violated my rights. 15 U.S. Code 1681 Section 602 A. States I have the right to privacy. 15 U.S. Code 1681 Section 604 A Section 2. States a consumer reporting agency can not furnish an account without my written instructions.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,NY,11692,None,Consent provided,Web,08/09/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,7377915
