10/13/22,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Problem with a credit reporting company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"This is not a duplicate nor is this complaint filed by a third party. I am filing this complaint myself. Please see this complaint is processed to the letter of the law. I am dismayed by the capability of the Credit Reporting Agencies to retain disregard a consumer 's appeal for the alteration of the disputed accounts on my Credit Report. Under the FCRA sections 609 and 611, the Credit Bureaus are obliged to confirm the information and status of the accounts being reported on my Credit Report. But in my case, Equifax has kept reporting the disputed accounts saying that the information they gave is precise, with which I seriously disagree. I am submitting this complaint to you today to request that Equifax run me copies of documents bearing my signature to prove the status of the disputed accounts. If they are unsuccessful to comply with the condition and continue the reporting of the disputed accounts, please realize I will pursue legal action. I need the accounts corrected XXXX : XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11230,None,Consent provided,Web,10/13/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6079399
