03/31/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"MY COMPLAINT WITH XXXX ( PDFS ATTACHED ) : In a XX/XX/XXXX letter, I formally requested verification for 6 disputed accounts listed on my credit report. I observed inconsistencies and consequent inaccuracies across all credit bureaus regarding dates such as date opened, date last reported, and date last active ( refer to orange highlights on pages 2 through 7 ). 

Additionally, in a letter sent to XXXX via certified mail on XX/XX/XXXX, I noted the presence of 5 unauthorized hard inquiries [ out of 13 ] on my XXXX report ( see pages 8, 9, & 10 ). As of XX/XX/XXXX, I have not received a response from XXXX regarding this matter. 

XXXX responded by confirming that all accounts are verified as mine ( see pages 1 through 20 ), yet inconsistencies ( and thus inaccuracies ) persist across all 6 accounts among the credit bureaus, as indicated in a XX/XX/XXXX credit report ( see orange highlights on pages 21 through 26 ). 

MY COMPLAINT WITH XXXX ( PDFS ATTACHED ) In a XX/XX/XXXX letter, I requested verification for 6 disputed accounts on my credit report. I noted inconsistencies and therefore inaccuracies among all the credit bureaus regarding date opened, date last reported, and date last active ( see orange highlights on pages 2 through 7 ). 

XXXX replied by stating that all the accounts are verified as mine ( see XXXX Reply PDF ), but inconsistencies ( and therefore inaccuracies ) remain on all 6 accounts among the credit bureaus on a XX/XX/XXXX credit report ( see orange highlights on pages 1 through 6 of PDF XXXX Credit Report Outcome ). 

MY COMPLAINT WITH EQUIFAX ( PDFS ATTACHED ) In a XX/XX/XXXX letter, I formally requested verification for 6 disputed accounts listed on my credit report. I highlighted inconsistencies and resulting inaccuracies across all credit bureaus regarding dates such as date opened, date last reported, and date last active ( refer to orange highlights on pages 2 through 7 ). 

In response, Equifax sent a XX/XX/XXXX dated letter stating they were unable to locate my credit file and requested additional verification to be sent to two of their addresses ( see pages 1 & 2 ). I promptly provided the requested verification ( see pages 3, 4, & 5 ). However, Equifax replied again on XX/XX/XXXX and XX/XX/XXXX, indicating that the information provided did not match what they had on file ( see pages 6 through 9 ). 

Despite Equifax claiming to be unable to locate my credit file, Equifax took the unusual step of reporting my disputed accounts with XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX, XXXX, and XXXX as "" new accounts '' ( see circled items on pages 1, 2, 3, & 5 of Equifax Credit Report Outcome PDF ). Additionally, they changed the status of my XXXX account from "" open '' to derogatory ( see pages 3 from 2-9 dispute PDF & page 3 of Equifax Credit Report Outcome PDF ). Since filing my dispute, my credit score with Equifax has dropped by approximately XXXX points ( see page 7 of Equifax Credit Report Outcome PDF ). 

It is very evident that Equifax has mishandled my dispute, and inaccuracies persist, if not worsened. 

LAST AND MOST IMPORTANTLY : In accordance with the Fair Credit Reporting Act, the 6 disputed accounts ( on XXXX, Equifax, and XXXX ) and the 5 unauthorized hard inquiries ( on XXXX ) violate my rights. 

15 USC 1681 section 602 a states that I have a rightto privacy ( and that credit reports must be accurate and fair ).

15 USC 1681 section 604a, section 2 states that a consumer reporting agency can not furnish an account without my written instructions.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,134XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/31/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8664443
