09/30/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Closing an account,Company closed your account,"I am writing to file a formal complaint against Citibank regarding the urgent mishandling of my account, lack of communication, and the unjustified pending closure of my account. 

On XX/XX/year>, I attempted to purchase a necklace at the XXXX XXXX store in New York using my Citibank card. Despite having sufficient funds in my checking account, the transaction failed. Immediately afterward, my account was placed under review. I immediately contacted Citibank 's customer service to confirm that I started the transaction and was assured that the issue would be resolved. 

Over the past month, I have made numerous attempts to contact Citibank, reaching out at least 20 times to get clarity on the status of my account. Every time I reached out, I was told that someone would contact me within 24 to 48 hours, but to this day, I am still waiting for a meaningful response. My account has remained under review during this period, causing significant inconvenience. 

What escalates the situation further is that I recently received an email from Citibank stating that my account will be closed. Citibanks reasoning behind the closure appears to be linked to the initial transaction attempt at XXXX XXXX, which I confirmed with the bank was authorized by me. Despite repeated confirmations, the Fraud Department 's decision to categorize this as suspicious activity is unfounded and outrageous. To make matters worse, Citibank had previously assured me that the issue was resolved, only to now use it as grounds for account closure. 

I HAVE REPEATEDLY OFFERED TO PROVIDE SUPPORTING DOCUMENTS TO VALIDATE THE LEGITIMACY OF ALL TRANSACTIONS AND FUNDS IN MY ACCOUNT WITHIN THE FIRST MONTH OF OPENING IT. YET, CITIBANK HAS MADE NO EFFORT TO REACH ME FOR THESE DOCUMENTS. I am appalled by the bank 's decision to close my account, which holds over {$15000.00} of my funds, rendering me unable to access my money and causing severe financial hardship. 

Citibank 's inaction, failure to provide any substantive resolution, and now the closure of my account due to an issue I was told had been resolved leave me with no choice but to escalate this matter through CFPB. I want immediate assistance in resolving this matter and ensuring Citibank restores access to my funds.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,11101,None,Consent provided,Web,09/30/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,10298324
