The problem comes up when on XX/XX/27 I send a dispute on my profile information in order to get my ITIN number updated and replaced with my SSN that I recently got from the Social Security Administration. After almost a month, the response that I receive is that "" THE WORKER ID DOCUMENT ( S ) PROVIDED CAN NOT BE USED TO UPDATE YOUR SOCIAL SECURITY NUMBER. THE WORKER ID NUMBER IS ISSUED BY THE SOCIAL SECURITY ADMINISTRATION FOR WORK PURPOSES ONLY. THIS NUMBER IS NOT ISSUED BY THE SOCIAL SECURITY ADMINISTRATION AS A SOCIAL SECURITY NUMBER. THE WORKER ID NUMBER IS NOT ISSUED BY THE SOCIAL SECURITY ADMINISTRATION AS A SOCIAL SECURITY NUMBER AND CAN NOT BE ADDED TO YOUR EQUIFAX CREDIT FILE. '' How come can my SOCIAL SECURITY NUMBER that has been issued by the SOCIAL SECURITY ADMINISTRATION be as per them a "" Worker ID Number Only '' what is this nonsense?. Now, just because my SSN has restrictions due to my immigration status does that means that I will be denied access to MY OWN credit report? I don't think that is any fair, and just like me there's plenty of individuals in the same situation that should be fixed and addresses by EQUIFAX, there's no excuses to say that my SSN is not valid as I can perfectly see my credit score and credit report with the other credit bureaus, I didn't have any problem updating my SSN on my bank account nor on my credit union.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11722,None,Consent provided,Web,04/25/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8854060
05/05/24,Vehicle loan or lease,Loan,Repossession,Voluntary repossession,"Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, I am writing to bring to your immediate attention a distressing situation regarding an ongoing dispute over a repossession ( LEADERS FINANCIAL COMP ). Despite my repeated attempts over the past five months to resolve this matter, I have not received any response. This lack of action has adversely affected my family 's ability to move out of a dangerous neighborhood due to credit bureaus ignoring my disputes and sending stallment letters. 

