03/19/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I trust this message finds you well. I am reaching out to address a matter concerning my rights as a federally protected consumer under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). 

Recently, I became aware that a charge off on my credit report is considered a certificate of indebtedness, which in turn is regarded as income and must be removed from my credit report. This issue pertains to the reporting of transaction history, and I believe it violates the FCRA, specifically outlined in 15 USC 6802 through 15 USC 6805. 

Given this circumstance, I am formally exercising my right to opt out of any and all authorizations, whether written, unwritten verbal, or nonverbal, that I may have previously given. It is imperative that my personal information is handled in accordance with my preferences and in adherence to federal guidelines, as mandated by the FCRA. 

Additionally, I kindly request clarification or a summary of the provisions detailed in 15 USC 6805 for my reference and understanding. Your assistance in providing this information would be greatly appreciated. 

Furthermore, I kindly request acknowledgment of receipt of this opt-out request and prompt action to rectify the reporting discrepancy on my credit report. 

Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter.",None,TD BANK US HOLDING COMPANY,NY,12020,None,Consent provided,Web,03/19/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8580914
