03/19/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Card was charged for something you did not purchase with the card,"I have a line of credit, XXXXcredit card with M & T Bank . I lost my credit card on XX/XX/2024. I called to speak to a customer service representative to report the card lost. I spoke with a representative to review a list of charges before sending me a new card. I lost my card on XX/XX/XXXX. When the representative went to review the summary of charges, they found a transaction for {$5700.00} from XXXX XXXX was charged on my card which I did not authorize on XX/XX/2024. ( XXXX days after it was noted that my card was lost which was XX/XX/2024. I did not receive a fraud alert notification for the transaction of {$5700.00} from XXXX XXXX. I did not receive any fraud alert via email or text about this transaction. Because of this, this fraudulent transaction was allowed to go through without my knowledge. I was not able to reject and deny the transaction because of the lack of alerts. M & T Bank initially went through with my fraud claim. A customer service representative I spoke with over the phone told me that the charge would be reversed and credit would be granted. The fraud claim was later rejected. This was different and opposed to what was originally assured to me. This is my 1st fraud claim with M & T Bank. Transactions like these should have fraud alerts to notify the cardholder. Unfortunately, M & T Bank never gave me one. The charge is unusual and uncharacteristic with the history of charges made on my M & T Bank credit card. I have not ever made CC charges with the XXXX XXXX merchant in the past. The unauthorized fraud charge of {$5700.00} from XXXX XXXX is back and still on my M & T Bank CC account. This unfortunate circumstance is a huge inconvenience to me. If this situation isnt, handled properly I will never bank or do business with M & T Bank again.",Company has responded to