06/03/24,Checking or savings account,CD (Certificate of Deposit),Managing an account,Problem with renewal,"I have been banking with Citibank close to 28 years. I have basic needs as a consumer and Citibank met my needs. Last year, I opened a few Certificates of Deposit for $ XXXX each with different maturities, yielding close to 5 % interest per annum, with no penalty for early redemption. This year in XXXX, XXXX of those CDs were renewed at half the interest rate and the new terms have penalty for early redemption. After contacting my Citibank advisor that I do not wish to keep these CDs at the revised terms. She told me that there is nothing she can do about the renewal ; there will be penalty if I were to terminate the account prior to maturity as these terms were in the fine print. 

