03/18/24,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",Domestic (US) money transfer,Fraud or scam,None,"On Monday, XXXX XXXX, 2024, someone who XXXX Citibank 's securit, or a Citibank employee , called me from Citibank 's XXXX department , using the official phone line and Citibank 's official 2 step verification sms line apparently, broke into my business account and made three wires from my business checking totally nearly {$14000.00}. Despite that I have informed Citibank that I did not make any wires, and that someone had clearly broken in their system, and also had use of their phone lines, Citibank has as yet to return the money stolen from me due to their own security breach.The amounts and reference numbers for the illicit wire transfers are Wire # 1. {$4800.00} + {$17.00} wire fee totaling {$4800.00} ref # XXXX ; Wire # 2 {$4900.00} + {$17.00} wire fee totaling {$4900.00} ref # XXXX, and Wire # 3. {$4000.00} + {$17.00} wire fee totaling {$4000.00} ref # XXXX ). I filed claims with both the FBI Internet crime and XXXX State Police for the same theft. At first Citibank 's agents acknowledged it was a fraud/theft and told me that they would put the money back as provisional credit no later than XX/XX/XXXX. When the money did not go into my account, I called them, they then indicated it would not be going back to my account but would be pending an investigation, changing their story. I complained and explained to a supervisor and told them that I had not made any wires nor given anyone nor any third party my information. The supervisor then assured me it would go to the XXXX department as it was originally and I should be getting the provisional credit shortly. Then, week 's later, after calling repeatedly, I got a message from Citibank denying my claim, incorrectly stating that I somehow had a role in the wire transfers, which is not true at all. I complained again and the last supervisor said they would appeal the decision. In the meantime 2 months have already gone by and the costs and additional damages to me and my family, damage to our credit rating, financial hardship have been mounting. It is unacceptable. Citibank 's system was hacked/hijacked and they are not taking responsibility and instead forcing me to suffer a major loss that is the result of their own negligence/system failure. Worst is it was I who even caught this happening in the act and informed Citibank, doing their own fraud department 's work for them. When I did so, their agent XXXX they saw someone was in my account making wires as we spoke. I later found out that Citibank had already at that moment the names, bank and account numbers of the recipients AS the money was being transferred. This means that it would only have take a phone call to those banks at the same instant to stop or freeze the money. This, too, was Citibank 's failure alone.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,124XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/18/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8568777
