03/06/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Notice to Agent is notice to principal notice to principal is a notice to agent. I am contacting you because I have found this account furnishing inaccurate and incomplete information on my credit report. I noticed this account on my credit report has turned into a charge-off. The account in question, "" XXXXXXXX XXXX  XXXX XXXX XXXX a "" Past Due '' balance of {$700.00}, however, this {$700.00} has been "" written off ''. I am referencing relevant sections of the FCRA, and IRS guidelines about reporting canceled debt. As per the law, those who provide information to Credit Reporting Agencies are obligated to ensure the information is accurate. I am cognizant of the requirement for you to report this canceled debt to the IRS. 15 U.S Code 1681 s-2 ( a ) Duty of furnishers of information to provide accurate information ( 1 ) Prohibition ( A ) Reporting information with actual knowledge of errors. A person shall not furnish any information relating to a consumer to any consumer reporting agency if the person knows or has reasonable cause to believe that the information is inaccurate. You have reported to the credit reporting agencies that this is a written-off debt. A 1099-C, being non-debt in nature, should not be reflected on my consumer report. By law, the IRS demands you to include the 1099-C in your gross income for tax purposes. Additionally, I have not yet received my required copy of Form 1099-C for the canceled debt, and am now requesting it. The IRS states, "" After a debt is canceled, a creditor will send you a Form 1099-C, Cancellation of Debt showing the amount canceled and date of cancellation ''. This omission has led to inaccurate reporting of this income on my consumer report. I believe it is important to rectify this matter to ensure proper documentation and reporting. Furthermore, you have substantially damaged my way of life, as Ive been denied credit. As of now, you are now notified about the harmful inaccurate information. It is imperative that you Delete and Block this illicit charge from my consumer report. I must emphasize that you are now aware of the importance I place on the proper handling of my consumer report in accordance with the Fair Credit Reporting Act. I trust that you will fulfill your obligations under the law ( 15 U.S.C 1681s-2 ) and ensure the accuracy and integrity of my private credit information. Also, this account is inaccurate, from XXXX to XXXX the account should have been updated to "" CLOSED '' and then charged off. This account is no longer open and the debt has been written off. I thank you consumer reporting agencies for fulfilling your jobs and following the FCRA regulations. I have provided proof of inaccurate payment history and inaccuracies below, in case evidence is needed in court or otherwise. I've counted XXXX periods that report the status of "" Charged off '' but the account wasn't listed as closed. THIS ACCOUNT IS ABSOLUTELY INCOMPLETE AND VIOLATES THE FCRA due to a lack of accuracy. Therefore I am requesting this account be removed and blocked from my consumer report due to FCRA and IRS guidelines and goodwill. Thank you for your attention to this matter.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,10472,None,Consent provided,Web,03/06/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8492758
09/05/23,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"In accordance with the Fair Credit Reporting Act. The List of accounts below has violated my federally protected consumer rights to privacy and confidentiality under 15 USC 1681. 

Account name : XXXX XXXXXXXX Account # XXXX, Account name : XXXX XXXX Account # XXXX, Account name : XXXX Account # XXXX, Account name : XXXX XXXX Account # XXXX, Account name : XXXX XXXX  Account # XXXX has violated my rights. 

15 U.S.C 1681 section 602 A. States I have the right to privacy. ( Therefore I would like my privacy to be respected. ) 15 U.S.C 1681 Section 604 A Section 2 also states a consumer reporting agency can not furnish an account without my written instructions. ( At no time at all did I give ANY type of instructions, written or verbal.

15 U.S.C 1681c. ( a ) ( 5 ) Section States : no consumer reporting agency may make any consumer report containing any of the following items of information Any other adverse item of information, other than records of convictions of crimes which antedates the report by more than seven years.

15 U.S.C. 1681s-2 ( A ) ( 1 ) states A person shall not furnish any information relating to a consumer to any consumer reporting agency if the person knows or has reasonable cause to believe that the information is inaccurate. I went ahead and highlighted the inaccuracies in the attached documents from the three consumer reporting agencies. 
Examples of these inaccuracies are, ( 1 ) In XXXX XXXX XXXX history XXXX XXXX payment history is showing as Unknown, and in Equifax the payment history is showing as 44 potentially negative months. ( 2 ) Equifax is showing XXXX and XX/XX/2023 payments for XXXX XXXX as being on time even though it should have been documented as CO for that period. These are just some inconsistencies, please see the attached documents for a full comparison. 

