03/25/24,"Payday loan, title loan, personal loan, or advance loan",Installment loan,Getting the loan,None,"A sales rep by the name of XXXX XXXX ( XXXX ) came to my home he explained what was supposed to happen if I decided to get the solar panels. The sales rep broke down every thing that was going to be done. He looked at my roof and told me that the roof is sinking and I told him that the beams were splitting and he said that they were going to replace the beams and redo the roof so it can support the panels if I decided to go with them. I video taped the sales rep while he was in my home explaining what they were going to do to the roof if I decided to sign the contract. He then asked for my social security number stating that he was going to see if I pre-qualified for the financing and give me an idea of roughly how much my monthly bill would be, which he stated was going to be about {$160.00} a month. Keep in mind I video taped the conversation and my son was also on the phone while the sales rep was explaining the process. About 2 weeks later I woke up to noise on my roof and when I went outside to see what was going on I noticed that they were working on the roof. I asked what they were doing and they said they were replacing the roof and putting up the solar panels. I immediately called the company to complain because I didn't sign a contract. I also went into the attic to see what they were doing and I noticed that not only were they putting on the solar panels while replacing the roof but that they didn't even change the beams like the sales rep said they were going to do. I kicked them off of my roof. While on the phone with the company they said they were cancelling the contact and I asked "" what contract? I didn't sign a contract I was only supposed to know the cost if I qualified for the financing. '' I received an email stating that the contract was cancelled soon after. A week or so later I received a bill for {$7800.00} and a monthly bill for almost {$600.00} a month. 
I am a XXXX  citizen and am on a fixed income and by no means can afford a monthly bill of {$600.00} for anything. The whole reason for me inquiring about the solar panels was to reduce my bill not increase it by over {$400.00}. I feel that they scammed me and signed me up for something I absolutely didn't sign up for. I am prepared to go to court and fight this as I have all of the emails stating that the supposed contract was cancelled. What type of solar panels cost XXXX dollars?!?! My roof is now sinking in because of this due to the weight of the solar panels because my beams would have needed to be replace before anything went on my roof.",None,Solar Mosaic LLC,NY,11691,Older American,Consent provided,Web,03/27/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8624059
