03/19/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Closing an account,Funds not received from closed account,"Let me start by saying that my business is a Tax Preparation Office. On XX/XX/XXXX, I got an email out of nowhere from Chase that my business account was closed due to suspected fraud. As far as I can tell, the offending transaction was a refund from the IRS sent to one of my clients under his name for his tax return XXXX and this type of transactions is very common in the tax preparation business, specially when the client request a cash advance from our office .Upon closure, I immediately call the bank and they can not provide any information, just that they will be conducting a review and that I should receive an explanation in the mail, as well as a check with my funds. I went into a physical branch and they say the same. 

It's been almost 30 days later, I still haven't received the check in the mail. So I went back into the physical branch, this time together with my client that I mentioned above to see if someone at the branch can actually verify my client 's identity in person with his passport, social security card, and driver license, but unfortunatley they said no. The only way to verify my client 's identity is providing a telephone number under his name. We even provided a telephone number that we are 100 % sure it was bought by my client under his name, but still the rep on the phone kept saying that the number we provided can not be verified by his system. 

