08/27/22,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",International money transfer,Money was not available when promised,None,"I initiated an international wire transfer on the XXXX of XXXX from my Chase business checking account for XXXX dollars that has not been received by the recipient branch. The wire was sent to my father 's bank account in XXXX. It has been 16 days since I made this transfer. An international wire transfer is supposed to take 1-5 business days. My first phone call to customer service at Chase was on the XXXX of XXXX inquiring why the wire had not been received by the recipient yet - since my account had been debited days ago.I was informed to wait until the end of the week to start an investigation. I called back Monday the XXXX and was issued a case number XXXX but I have been unable to get anyone in Client service to actually track or follow up with what is going on with the transaction. After a week of waiting, on the XXXX of XXXX I had to harass customer service for a helpful answer and was finally directed by an agent to something called the "" secure messages center '' which is a service that exists within the Chase online banking app - a service I did not know existed, nor was informed of by Customer service until I threatened to escalate the situation. To summarise it is like a private inbox within the app itself and the messages sent or received here are not reflected in my regular email inbox that is linked to my bank account. Therefore, unknown to me, this entire time, there had been a message in the Secure Message Center inbox from their "" XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX '' sent on the XXXX of XXXX stating that the wire could not be completed because the XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX required more information regarding the purpose of the wire and that if I did not provide this information within 5 days of the receipt of that message, a recall would automatically be initiated and i would be charged the fees to process the same. Since not a single Customer service agent I had spoken to directed me to this service until the XXXX of XXXX, or even informed me that such a service existed and that I had probably overlooked a message regarding my wire in this specific part of the online banking dashboard, I did not end up being able to provide the relatively simple information that could have allowed the wire to go through within the required time window. The message also mentioned that the recall would take 3-5 business days and that I could contact the XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX for any further information. When I attempted to call this number on the XXXX of XXXX I received an automated response stating that this department was unavailable. In my last conversation with a customer care specialist with Chase I was informed it would take 3 months to recall my money back.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11222,None,Consent provided,Web,08/27/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5923561
