04/12/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"I was in XXXX and XXXX XXXX from XX/XX/2024 to XX/XX/2024. Attached is a flight receipt and screenshot of my flight ticket. I called to file a dispute for this transaction ( {$100.00} - transaction name XXXX XXXX during a layover from XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX I was on leisure vacation in XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX, XXXX, a lovely city that is known for credit cardfraud where I did not haveconsistent cell phone service. I admittedly didn't pay close attention to my transactions, the majority of which occurredon card terminal. 

When I was on layover from XXXX XXXX XXXX, I did a reconciliation of all charges and noticed this unrecognized charge. At this point of realization, I immediately called Chase fraud. The Chase dispute team noted that other charges were flagged on my account that they blocked from clearing. We walked through these transactions, one of which included another P2P payment and a hotel transaction for a hotel I did not stay at ( XXXX XXXX ). Following this call, the fraud representative noted that they'd immediately have my credit card ending in XXXX cancelled and would send a replacement ending in XXXX to my New York address. Because I was in transit to XXXX when the card was closed, I asked if I was allowed to continue using my Chase Sapphire card ( both physical card and wallet ) in the meantime. The Chase employee said yes for digital wallet payments, because my XXXX XXXX digital wallet would automatically update with my new card information. I then proceeded to use XXXX XXXX in the States and in XXXX XXXX. Chase did not send a replacement card until XX/XX/XXXX. When I returned to the United States on XX/XX/XXXX, I activated the new card. 

Two months later on XX/XX/2024, I was told that Chase determined that it "" did not seem like fraud '' because I continued to use my card. I hope the detail above clarifies ( 1 ) that there were clearly other questionable transactions that the Chase team effectively caught, ( 2 ) it look me a few days to notice the erroneous charge ( and I'm shocked Chase didn't ), and ( 3 ) I was instructed that I could continue to use my card until it closed upon successful delivery of the replacement card.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11201,None,Consent provided,Web,04/12/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8761688
