09/09/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers",Didn't receive advertised or promotional terms,"Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, I am writing to formally file a complaint regarding my Chase Ink Unlimited Card ending in XXXX. I applied for the card under an offer that provided XXXX points after spending {$6000.00} within 90 days. After meeting the spending requirement, I received the XXXX points as promised. 

However, I later discovered that Chase was offering a concurrent promotion for the same card, which provided XXXX points for the identical spending requirement. Given the overlap in timing, I reached out to Chase to request that my account be adjusted to match the higher points offer, especially as I had already fulfilled the spending threshold. 

Unfortunately, despite my reasonable request, Chase declined to match the XXXX points offer. I believe this decision is unfair, as both offers were active during the same period, and I had already met the required spending terms. This experience has been frustrating and disappointing, and I feel that my request for the additional XXXX points was entirely reasonable. 

I respectfully ask the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau to review my case and assist in resolving this matter, as I believe Chase 's refusal to match the offer undermines fair business practices and customer satisfaction. 

Thank you for your attention to this issue. I look forward to your assistance in helping to resolve this matter. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11365,None,Consent provided,Web,09/09/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,10051609
