03/11/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Opening an account,Confusing or missing disclosures,"My Bank of America check and saving account was closed in XX/XX/XXXX because others tried to steal my account. After that, I defended my rights for 4 months and provided my bank account as required by Bank of America. handwriting signature comparison information, until I received a call from Bank of America on XX/XX/XXXX. They considered my request again and assisted me online to reset the user information over the phone. I am very happy to be able to use BOA again, I tried to deposit money into my account, but it failed, I went to the nearby financial center, they asked me to wait until XX/XX/XXXX, but when I logged in again, the system showed my checking And the saving account has been closed and I am not allowed to open another account, they did not give me the reason. I called and could not get any help, they just said that they could not verify my information and asked me to go to the nearest financial center, which I did in the nearest I went to the financial center with my documents countless times for several days, but in the end I still found out that it was a waste of time. They were playing tricks on me, constantly wasting my time, and constantly transferring calls to different departments. No one really helped me. The department that helped me recover my account was deemed by the risk department to have made the wrong decision. They did something wrong, why should I bear the consequences, wasted four months of my life constantly toying with me.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION",NY,115XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/11/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8523476
