09/16/22,Student loan,Federal student loan servicing,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am demanding that Nelnet remove the student loan from my consumer report immediately. According to these loans being obtained 10 to 20 years ago, I was uninformed and coerced, as per 15 usc 6802, no one sat down with me and made things clear and conspicuous about the private policy and that I had the right to opt out to sharing my non-public personal information with non-affiliated third parties. Right there is a breach in the consumer credit transaction. This make this whole transaction null and void. By law that was suppose to be disclose to me and it wasn't. When I began studying consumer laws in XXXX of 2022, I notice that Nelnet/department of education been in violation for reporting to the credit bureaus my non public personal information, and according to the FTC this is what they define as non-public personal information XXXX NPI  is XXXX any information an individual gives you to get a financial product or service ( for example, name, address, income, Social Security number, or other information on an application ) ; any information you get about an individual from a transaction involving your financial product ( s ) or service ( s ) ( for example, the fact that an individual is your consumer or customer, account numbers, payment history, loan or deposit balances, and credit or debit card purchases ) ; or any information you get about an individual in connection with providing a financial product or service ( for example, information from court records or from a consumer report ). 
NPI does not include information that you have a reasonable basis to believe is lawfully made "" publicly available. '' In other words, information is not NPI when you have taken steps to determine : that the information is generally made lawfully available to the public ; and that the individual can direct that it not be made public and has not done so. 

Consumer credit transaction by law shall be private, and I have the right to privacy as per 15 usc 1681 ( a ) ( 4 ) I demanded an election form from Nelnet that should have been given to me the first day I established a relationship with them while obtaining these loans and every year after that as long as I am a customer. I opted out on the form demanding that they stop sharing, reporting my information to non-affiliated third parties that offers educational and financial services. The consumer reporting agencies had no affiliation to Nelnet. when you look at Nelnet website you see all their affiliated companies but not the credit bureaus. The credit bureaus are also considered to be a company that offers financial services and products according to ftc and the bank holding company act. They engage in activities of financial nature for profit. According to 12 CFR 225.28 ( a ) ( b ) ( 5 ) the credit bureaus are so closely related to banks because of the financial activities they engage in. credit bureaus are known to be a financial institution and I demanding that they remove these students loans off my consumer file. my next step is arbitration. I have the right to privacy and I have opted out for my information with Nelnet not to be reported or shared with the credit bureaus or anyone else. And again Nelnet violated my rights for not letting me know about the privacy act and sharing my information that's fraud and breach the whole transaction. null and voided",None,"Nelnet, Inc.",NY,10459,None,Consent provided,Web,09/16/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5984218
04/06/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Problem using a debit or ATM card,"On XX/XX/XXXX, I attempted to purchase 2 money orders, one for {$1000.00} and another for {$100.00} at a United States Post Office at XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX, NY. There was a fee of {$5.00} for money orders for a total of {$1100.00}. The total amount was put in for payment by the clerk for both money orders and the fees. I put in my Chase debit card and added my pin. An "" Exceed Limit '' error occurred and No money orders were given. I contacted Chase customer service to investigate source of error being there were sufficient funds in my account. I was informed that the charge of {$1100.00} had been charged and was pending. I informed her at that time that no money order was given. She indicated, if nothing was given, it will not go through. After a couple days, the {$1100.00} was indicated as paid to the Post Office on my bank statement. Called Chase again, spoke to Claims department, they indicated, it was paid and I had to go back to Post Office to get money order ( Chase closed complaint ). At Post Office, I spoke with XXXX XXXX at XXXX, she checked the transactions for ( XXXX, the clerk ), XX/XX/XXXX for the clerk I went to. She indicated there were no transactions for that amount on their system for that day. I again, notified Chase, they indicated the money was paid and to go back to the Post Office to reconcile ( yet another compliant was closed at Chase, yet again ). The Post Office escalated my complaint to the USPS Consumer and Industry Contact Office, Bhanu Chemmangaattuma ( XXXX ) confirmed an error prevented money orders from being dispensed andthat no transaction in the amount of {$1100.00} was received by the post office. I contacted the Corporate office of Chase and provided proof from Post Office no money order was disbursed and no money was received. They indicated they would investigate and get back to me ( Chase gave another complaint number ). When they failed to get back to me, I contacted them. Chase Corporate indicated that their records reflect the payment was made on XX/XX/XXXX, which is shown on my banking statement. At that time, they indicated, I would have to address my concerns with the Post Office ( Again complaint was closed by Chase ). On Sunday, XX/XX/XXXX, we went to the city of XXXX police department and made a complaint with XXXX XXXX, XXXXe # XXXX. A report was made ( 24-7239 ) where they indicated, it appeared the problem was within Chase and a possible glitch in the system. I attempted to contact Chase again, they would not help me. I tried to get legal services to assist, but they were several XXXX dollars. As it stands now, after 3 complaints with Post Office, 4 dispute claims with Chase, proof provided to both parties, I was not given a money order from the Post Office, they denied receiving any money. Chase took the money out of my account indicating it was paid to Post Office. Hence, I have no money order and {$1100.00} was taken from me. It has been over a month, with several attempts to resolve the issue, with no resolution and I am seeking justice.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,12603,Older American,Consent provided,Web,04/06/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8713537
