04/25/24,Debt collection,Other debt,Written notification about debt,Didn't receive notice of right to dispute,"I am writing to file a formal complaint regarding a troubling experience with XXXX XXXX XXXX, which has resulted in erroneous credit reporting and unfair billing practices. I received a notice in the mail from CCS collecting for XXXX XXXX XXXX stating that I owed them a certain amount. The notice provided an option to make a payment online, which I promptly did to ensure timely payment of any outstanding obligations and to avoid any negative impact on my XXXX XXXX. 

However, upon logging into the online portal, I discovered that the amount displayed was lower than what was indicated in the notice. Despite this discrepancy, I proceeded with the payment on the same day I received the notice, as I am diligent about paying my bills on time and did not want any adverse effects on my XXXX XXXX. 

I consulted with my accountant, who confirmed that I did not owe any funds to XXXX XXXX XXXX. With this information in hand, I initiated a dispute with the XXXX XXXX agency. Additionally, I reached out to XXXX XXXX XXXX directly and provided them with a declaration page of my insurance coverage, proving that I had the necessary coverage they were attempting to collect from me. They acknowledged their error and promptly issued refunds to me. 

XXXX XXXX XXXX assured me on multiple occasionsover XXXX timesthat they had contacted the XXXX XXXX agency to request the removal of the erroneous entry from my credit report. Despite their assurances and my provision of evidence demonstrating that I never owed the debt, the incorrect information continues to be reported on my credit profile. I started trying to resolve this in XXXX and we are now at the end of XXXX. 

I find it unacceptable that despite XXXX XXXX XXXX acknowledging their mistake, issuing refunds, and providing documentation to rectify the situation, they have failed to follow through on their commitment to remove the erroneous entry from my credit report. This has had a detrimental impact on my XXXX XXXX and financial well-being. I also sent in the mail and faxed the agency all of my disputes, proof of refunds and insurance paperwork. 

I am deeply troubled by CCS collecting practices, which involve sending notices that direct individuals to pay online before allowing any period for disputing the issue. This practice is unfair and undermines consumers ' rights to dispute erroneous charges. 

In light of the above circumstances, I am formally requesting the following actions : Immediate removal of the erroneous entry from my credit report CCS. 

I appreciate your attention to this matter and trust that you will take appropriate action to address these concerns. Please provide me with updates regarding the resolution of this issue. 

Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter.",Company believes it acted appropriately as authorized by contract or law,"CCS Financial Services, Inc.",NY,11105,None,Consent provided,Web,04/25/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8859060
