04/13/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Banking errors,"On XX/XX/2024 I made a call to Citizens bank to make a XXXX time payment towards to my Citizens mortgage using my Citizens XXXX  account. My monthly mortgage payment is paid via XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX checking account. The representative was only provided my Citizens XXXX  account number for the XXXX time payment. But since both bank XXXX  accounts are listed, the representative ( XXXX ) wasnt paying attention and used my XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX checking account for the XXXX time payment. This caused a $ XXXX overdraft in my XXXX XXXX XXXX  XXXX  account. By the time the transaction from XX/XX/XXXX had actually processed it was XX/XX/XXXX. I use my XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  account as my primary account to pay my monthly bills, all of which are on autopay. It was the first week of the month and I had no money in my account. I thankfully had some money in my XXXX  XXXX XXXX XXXX account and was quickly able to transfer money to my XXXX  account to pay all my bills. I knew it would take time to investigate what happened and I couldnt wait for nor rely on Citizens to fix the issue. I spoke to a few people at Citizens ( XXXX, XXXX and XXXX XXXX. They didnt seem to understand the severity of the issue. They kept saying dont worry you have a few more weeks until your Citizen monthly mortgage payment is due. My Citizens monthly mortgage payment was the least of my concerns. I kept asking if Citizens would have paid my other bills ( HOA, internet, cable, cell ) if they werent able to fix the issue immediately and no one had a response. In the end, the transfer of money from my XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX account to XXXX  account fixed the issue. I didnt trust Citizens to reverse everything correctly to process it from the Citizens XXXX account. It was also going to force me to provide additional documentation and the level of stress and time I spent fixing the issue myself was already too much.",None,"CITIZENS FINANCIAL GROUP, INC.",NY,10023,None,Consent provided,Web,04/13/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8760056
