05/16/22,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"Upon reviewing my updates, the incorrect information was still found in my reports which I believe has been taken care of due to the written appeals I sent. The last letter sent to the 3 Credit Bureaus was XX/XX/2022, but no response was ever received from them to date. Thus, their action has violated the Fair Credit Reporting Act, 15 USC Sections 1681i, which states that continued reports of the unverified information without any proof provided, within the time allowed by law, is not authorized. The account listed below is still reporting on my Credit Reports and need to delete immediately : XXXX XXXX  XXXX",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10950,None,Consent provided,Web,05/16/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5564478
09/03/23,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Trans Union failed to provide an opt-out notice, as is required by all financial institutions, in which I, the consumer, have the option to opt-out of having my information shared with unaffiliated third-parties. Thus, any unlawful use of my nonpublic personal information without full disclosure and consent constitutes identity theft. 

On XX/XX/23, Trans Union received my Notice of Identity Theft, affidavit, and other required personal identification information per 15 USC 1681c-2, requesting that Trans Union remove one ( 1 ) unauthorized adverse transaction from my consumer credit report. Neither Trans Union nor the company identified in the transaction have provided me with an opt-out notice allowing me to exercise my right to privacy. Trans Union failed to comply with the statute and with my requests by failing to block the reporting of unauthorized information identified by me, the consumer, no later than 4 business days after receipt of notice. 

Trans Union continues to unlawfully use my personal and financial information which included the sharing of information to unaffiliated third-parties that adversely affected my creditworthiness ( i.e. denial for credit of {$90000.00} and {$85000.00} from two separate financial institutions ) and resulted in defamation of my character and general reputation.

Despite three ( 3 ) written notices sent via certified mail, Trans Union continues to report damaging unauthorized personal and financial information on my consumer credit report.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,109XX,None,Consent provided,Web,09/03/23,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,7495207
