05/25/24,Debt collection,Other debt,Written notification about debt,Didn't receive notice of right to dispute,"Security Credit Services Subject : Dispute of Collection Account and Request for Removal from Credit Report To Whom It May Concern, I am writing to formally dispute the collection account placed on my consumer report. The collection agency has not provided the necessary validation information required under 12 CFR 1006.34 ( b ) ( 5 ), and yet, the account has been reported to the credit reporting agencies. 
Additionally, I have not been given the opportunity to dispute this account in accordance with 12 CFR 1006.34 ( c ) ( 4 ) ( i ). As such, I believe my consumer rights have been violated.

The collection agency is using false, misleading, misrepresentation, and deceptive means in its efforts to collect this debt, which is a clear violation of my consumer rights. Moreover, the agency has no authority to furnish any account information to consumer reporting agencies without providing all required disclosures, as mandated by 12 CFR 1006.34 ( d ) and 15 USC 1681s-2 ( a ) ( 7 ) ( A ). 

Given these violations, I am requesting the immediate removal of this collection account from my consumer report. Failure to comply with this request will leave me no choice but to pursue further legal action to enforce my rights under the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ) and the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). 



Date Opened XX/XX/year> Balance {$3000.00} Please acknowledge receipt of this letter and confirm, in writing, that you will remove the collection account from my consumer report. I expect a response within 30 days from the date of this letter. 


Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX",None,"Security Credit Services, LLC",NY,11230,None,Consent provided,Web,05/25/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9095498
