03/28/24,Mortgage,FHA mortgage,Trouble during payment process,Trying to communicate with the company to fix an issue while managing or servicing your loan,"( M & T bank insurance case # XXXX ) On XX/XX/XXXX myself and my wife & child were the victims of a flood and storm in XXXX XXXX XXXX that left damages to our home. The process of getting the funds from our insurance company has been absolutely horrendous and to add insult to injury, My mortgage company M & T Bank has made the process even harder for us. We were originally serviced by XXXX XXXX  when we first purchased our home in XXXX, but was later notified that our mortgage was sold to M & T Bank after hurricane sandy. I realize that banks have different procedures regarding insurance claims but XXXX XXXX  has never made the insurance claims process this difficult and hard. We were blindsided to the M & T bank regulations regarding insurance claim funds because we were never given new loan documents that would have explained the differences in regulations regarding insurance claims made on our property. As a result M & T Bank has denied our request to endorse our insurance check for our storm repairs even tho we meet the criteria of the check being under {$20000.00} ( after our private adjusters fee is taken out as per the M & T Bank claim loss representative XXXX XXXX ). We were denied and as a result have been given a hard time to receive our funds despite being a loyal customer and having our mortgage account in good standing. We have been suffering since the date of loss in XX/XX/XXXX and it is now days away from being XXXX which would be a total of 80 + days and we are still dealing with this terrible financial hardship with no resolution in sight. I have incurred numerous out of pocket financial expenses since this unexpected weather event has occured and have only received information by bank associates that lack empathy regarding my situation. We've been getting different explanations every time that we call the loss department for help in regards to our insurance claim and it is unfair. My wife is a XXXX XXXX surviving XXXX XXXX and i am a decorated retired XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX that worked faithfully in the XXXX XXXX XXXX. We have both worked very hard to stay out of foreclosure within this terrible economy, and this situation has been absolutely terrible to our family. We are being treated like criminals on our own insurance claim. We pay our mortgage, taxes, and insurance faithfully and for M & T Bank to treat us like this is absolutely horrible. I pray no other home owner will ever have to experience what we've experienced.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,M&T BANK CORPORATION,NY,11520,None,Consent provided,Web,03/28/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8649362
