05/03/24,Vehicle loan or lease,Lease,Managing the loan or lease,Problem with fees charged,"I have leased a XXXX Tesla XXXX XXXX through Tesla Finance since XX/XX/XXXX. Accordingly, XXXX XXXX has my XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX checking account information and my authorization to deduct my monthly lease payments, which has been working without issue since XX/XX/XXXX. Notably for purposes of this complaint, however, I DO NOT subscribe to Teslas Full Self Driving ( Supervised ) service ( FSD ). Recently, in an effort to increase customer use of FSD ( and likely use the data generated by its use to improve the system and assist in XXXX attempts to release a robotaxi service ), Tesla has extended owners a free trial of FSD. I did not activate the trial or sign up for FSD during the trial period. However, on XX/XX/XXXX, Tesla Motors, apparently using my BofA checking account information on file with Tesla Finance, performed an unauthorized transaction for {$99.00} alongside my normal, authorized lease payment transaction. Upon information gleaned from an internet search, a similar {$99.00} unauthorized charge was applied to many additional Tesla owners and is ostensibly for FSD subscriptions.

I reached out to Tesla Finance to inquire about the charge, but no one was available to answer my call. I was instead advised to email Tesla Finance, which I have done, but have not received an answer at the time of this writing. I have also disputed the {$99.00} unauthorized charge with XXXX and they are very responsively investigating. However, the investigation will understandably take several weeks. Given the facts that ( 1 ) Tesla has recently experienced sales and revenue slowdowns and is undergoing large layoffs, and ( 2 ) that many Tesla customers are apparently experiencing similar unauthorized charges, I recommend CFPB investigate how serious and widespread this issue is. Whether through error during layoff chaos or something more nefarious ( such as trying to make up for revenue slowdowns ), Tesla maXXXX be collecting unauthorized charges from customers on a large scale.",Company believes the complaint is the result of a misunderstanding,"Tesla, Inc.",NY,146XX,None,Consent provided,Web,05/03/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8922069
