03/20/23,Mortgage,Conventional home mortgage,Trouble during payment process,None,"XXXX XXXX and XXXX XXXX authorized their agent to make a formal Notice of Error with respect to the federally related mortgage transaction which alleged account is presently serviced by Select Portfolio Servicing , Inc. on behalf of XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, Successor in Interest to XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX, as XXXX for XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. 

A foreclosure sale is scheduled for Tuesday, XX/XX/XXXX to auction our primary residence at XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX, NY XXXX. 

The Notice of Error was sent to SPS on XX/XX/XXXX by Certified Mail # XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX and by e-mail to the SPS Ombudsman 's Office. 

Our agent provided a detailed analysis of the initial transaction, whereby the a filed lost note affidavit failed to establish who owned the Note when it was lost and other requirements under UCC 3-804. In addition, the analysis shows that the subject consolidated note was never in the physical possession of XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, the lender. Accordingly, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX could not assign to Plaintiff XXXX XXXX, as Trustee what it did not have. 

Our agent supplied a complete review of the transaction and the fatal defects therein, and also two graphic illustrations that tracked the note and mortgage, illustrating that Plaintiff in NY foreclosure action Index # XXXX had no authority or Constitutional standing to commence the action on XX/XX/XXXX.",Company believes it acted appropriately as authorized by contract or law,"SELECT PORTFOLIO SERVICING, INC.",NY,XXXXX,Older American,Consent provided,Web,03/20/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6720496
03/20/23,Mortgage,Conventional home mortgage,Struggling to pay mortgage,None,"I have attempted vigorously to settle my foreclosure with Rushmore bank for several years after my loss of employment, due to a permanent XXXX. Ive hired real estate brokers and attorneys to settle all the debt associated with the property through loss mitigation. However, Rushmore has acted in a disingenuous and deceptive manner by not truly evaluating a fair and reasonable offer to settle the debt through a short sale. They have violated loss mitigation procedural safeguards for me as a homeowner by consistently not evaluating the proper settlement of the property. In exchange, I have made every attempt and given numerous documents to validate the current condition and value of the home. This complaint is served as an appeal to the erroneously and fictitious property values that Rushmore is utilizing to reject my short sale. 

In the year XXXX, XXXX XXXX, a portfolio resolution specialist, arbitrarily suggested the property was worth low $ XXXX without ever inspecting the property. When he was told the home was a rehab, he than suggested I sign over my home in a Deed in XXXX and they would do the construction on the home. He never considered the other encumbrances that would remain after a Deed in XXXX. I rejected the Deed in XXXX. After begging Rushmore to do an inspection to assess a more accurate value, they hired a real estate agent that is untrained and unlicensed to efficiently evaluate the property. In XXXX the agent stated the home was worth XXXX ( although much less than XXXX XXXX made up number ) but it still had serious errors. The agent reflected a renovation cost of about $ XXXX. A licensed HUD inspector report stated a complete construction cost for the renovation at $ XXXX, more than double the estimated cost from this broker opinion who was neither a construction professional nor experienced in renovation estimates. The as is value of $ XXXX didnt include accurate repair costs, which would have placed the property at a valuation of around $ XXXX. 

The application was resubmitted in XX/XX/XXXX and most recently in XXXX. All with the same outcome, Rushmores lack of proper evaluation and never using a trained expert to resolve our dispute. Rushmore believes this property value has increased over XXXX in less than 3 years. They are using drive-by inspections that are gross inflations of the value of the property that rely on market fluctuations. This does not represent the current condition and damage to my house. Even their own internal inspection done once in XXXX negated their initial arbitrary number by over $ XXXX. They have stated the property was worth $ XXXX in XXXX, $ XXXX in XXXX and $ XXXX in XXXX, none of which were licensed appraisal reports. 

I recently hired a certified licensed appraiser to conduct an accurate valuation and submitted it to Rushmore who said their investor will not consider any expert evaluation only the opinions of unlicensed untrained real estate agents. 

The costs on this property continue to rise and the condition continues to deteriorate. I am entitled to a fair resolution.",None,RUSHMORE LOAN MANAGEMENT SERVICES LLC,NY,11203,None,Consent provided,Web,03/20/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6721026
05/30/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"To whom it may concern, I am writing with respect to several ongoing fraudulent charges that I have been working to resolve since XXXX, XXXX in good faith. 

After speaking with a XXXX, a Representative ( I called into XXXX XXXX XXXX ) I was urged to send in any documentation re XXXX efforts Ive made to resolve said issues. 

Furthermore at approximately XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  on XXXX XXXX, XXXX confirmed Goldman Sachs ( XXXX ) does not have any merchant proof to substantiate that I should be paying the amounts listed below. XXXX stated I cant give you what I dont have Thus, it is my firm brief that XXXX should close this matter and the charges listed below. For the avoidance of doubt, I should not owe these monies. 

Below, please find the Charges in Question, Efforts and Additional Context. 

I am happy to send exhibits and a copy of the full formal letter. 

