04/05/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Closing your account,Company closed your account,"I have two credit cards with AspireCredit Card issued by XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. I always paid them on time especially one that I have had for a while. Back in XXXX, XXXX, my brother passed and I lost my job. I was able to make payments on XX/XX/XXXX to both cards. I was denied unemployment and could not make payments due in XX/XX/XXXX. I received one call only about what I owed and explained the situation I was in and why I was not paying but had a great history with paying. The last payment was made in XX/XX/XXXX. It was not the full amount but I tried my best. Today, I tried to go to Aspire 's website and it stated this email/password could not be found. I called and was informed that both accounts are closed. I was told by XXXX that I was sent emails informing of such action being made. I searched my email and there were no notices at all. I requested to speak to a supervisor. The supervisor stated as the accounts are closed there is nothing she can do. I will have to pay the full amount on both cards and then reapply. I told her I couldn't pay before and that I was going to start today and if I couldn't pay the minimum that has accumulated late fees, how am I to pay {$1400.00} plus now, knowing that I will be denied as well when I reapply for missing payments now and accounts being closed. She stated that they sent me a letter through the mail when I told her I never received an email regarding the potential closure. I informed her that the only thing I did receive was a statement to pay, as I get every month, and that there was a notice on the front of the statement my account was closed to new transactions and the terms of your cardholder agreement still apply and to see the agreement for more details. I explained to her that I do not have the agreement as I don't have it as I have been with them for so long and never had issues with payment before. 