05/25/24,Debt collection,Credit card debt,Written notification about debt,Didn't receive notice of right to dispute,"CFPB Law Dispute Letter Name : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX RE : Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) Dispute under 12 CFR 1006.34 & 15 U.S.C. 1681s-2 ( 7 ) ( A ) Dear CFPB, This letter is to formally dispute inaccurate information on my credit report in accordance with the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). 

Identification of Inaccurate Information I am writing to dispute the following information on my credit report : Account Type : COLLECTION Creditor Name : I C SYSTEM Account Number ( Last XXXX Digits ) : UNKNOWN Specific Information in Dispute : Basis for Dispute I believe the information listed above is inaccurate. I also have revoked all rights of them communicating with me through email, text and calls. I am requesting validation of such debts. I am requesting the purchase agreement between them and the original creditor. I'm also requesting that they furnish proof that they are licensed and bonded and would like all collections to be removed immediately. 

Violation of FCRA I believe this inaccurate information is a violation of my rights under the FCRA, specifically 12 CFR 1006.34 ( b ) ( 5 ) which guarantees the reported information is accurate and verifiable, 12 CFR 1006.34 ( c ) ( 4 ) ( i ) which requires furnishers to investigate disputes, 12 CFR 1006.34 ( d ) which outlines the timeframes for dispute investigations, and 15 USC 1681s-2 ( 7 ) ( A ) which prohibits credit reporting agencies from including inaccurate information.

Request for Action I request that the CFPB investigate this dispute with the credit reporting agency and the information furnisher ( creditor ) named above. I further request that the inaccurate information be removed from my credit report and that I be informed of the results of the investigation within the timeframes mandated by the FCRA. 

Supporting Documents Attached are copies of documents supporting my claim ( e.g., cancelled checks, account closure confirmation, police report for identity theft ). 

Thank you for your time and attention to this matter. I look forward to your prompt resolution. 

Sincerely. 


Printed Name : XXXX XXXX",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"I.C. System, Inc.",NY,11743,None,Consent provided,Web,05/25/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9099752
