04/17/24,Debt collection,I do not know,Written notification about debt,Notification didn't disclose it was an attempt to collect a debt,"I have been receiving robocalls from "" XXXX from FFR '' since XX/XX/XXXX. The calls usually come from XXXX, and have recently also been coming from XXXX. I typically receive multiple calls per week from these numbers, since they first started calling me. If the call goes to voicemail, a recorded message instructs me to call back at XXXX, without explaining the purpose of the call. The recorded message is exactly the same every time. If I answer the call, hold music plays. I searched the phone numbers online, and one of them ( XXXX ) is associated with a debt collection agency called FFR, Inc. Searching the phone number online is the only way I have been able to determine what the calls might be about. The calls have never identified the company as a debt collection agency, informed me that they are trying to collect payment from me, informed me of any creditor to whom I owe debt, informed me of any amount of money I owe, provided verification of my personal information or validation information regarding the debt, or informed me of my rights to dispute the debt. I have not received any written communications from a company called "" FFR, '' or any other written communications notifying me of any debts. I have never been told by the caller what "" FFR '' stands for, or what type of company it is. Since I have not been connected to a person any time I have answered these calls, and I only hear hold music, and I have not been told why I am being contacted, I have avoided these calls, because they appear to be a scam and/or illegal unwanted calls. My phone number has been on the Do Not Call Registry since XXXX. I need to know whether these calls are legitimate, so that I can resolve any concerns, but I have been cautioned against speaking to unknown spam callers. From information I have read on the CFPB and FTC websites, it appears that if these calls were about a legitimate debt I owe, I would have been informed of the debt through written communication, and failure to do so is a violation of fair debt collection laws.",None,"First Financial Resources, Inc.",NY,12203,None,Consent provided,Web,04/17/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8791583
