08/12/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account status incorrect,"My accounts was never late! I have had exceptional payment history with XXXX  XXXX and all payments were placed on Autopay. This late payment that is reporting is a result on a systematic error on their end processing my payment. 

This was clearly a billing error made my the company and is not a reflection of my payment experience which violates USC Code 1681eb. This error has caused severe hard to my reputation, my character, my mode of living and to my family! 

I demand the late payment reported to be removed/updated. 

They are not in compliance with the following law. 15 USC 1666b and its requirements set the standards and the guidance for a creditor to treat a payment as late, yet they are reporting a payment as late and they did not comply with the law! 

15 USC 1666b ( a ) Time to make payments A creditor may not treat a payment on a credit card account under an open end consumer credit plan as late for any purpose, unless the creditor has adopted reasonable procedures designed to ensure that each periodic statement including the information required by section 1637 ( b ) of this title is mailed or delivered to the consumer not later than 21 days before the payment due date. 

I have requested proof that this information was mailed or delivered 21 days before the payment due date and this information was requested in good faith pursuant rule 1002 and It was never provided. 

This is unfair, illegal, fraudulent, and not equitable to me as a consumer!",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,11542,None,Consent provided,Web,08/12/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,9772351
03/12/24,Debt collection,I do not know,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt is not yours,"Over the last year and a half, I have been receiving strange calls to my landline from Portfolio Recovery. There is never a message left, so after several of these calls, I did a XXXX check on their information and found that they are a debt collection company. Since I have never had any outstanding debts and have not received any official letters or other documentation from "" creditors '' demanding payment for an "" unpaid '' debt, I found it odd that I would be receiving calls from a debt collection agency. After a year of no-message calls from Portfolio Recovery , I finally answered one of their calls and told them to stop contacting my number -- that no one in my household had any outstanding debts. I went on to point out that I was aware the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau had fined them {$24.00} XXXX for illegal debt collection practices and made it clear that I knew their repeated calls to me were a scam. Unfortunately, the calls have continued. 

Absent any written demand or documentation from a creditor, bank, or lender sent to me via certified mail, I can only conclude that Portfolio Recovery is, once again, engaged in the same illegal activities which earned them a {$24.00} XXXX fine from the CFPB. Were they leaving threatening messages, their calls would be more disturbing and disrupting ; however, given the dodgy history of this company, the large fine they have had to pay for illegal practices, and their persistence in calling my number tells me that they are looking for naive consumers to scam. I just wanted to pass this on. You may want to launch another investigation into Portfolio Recovery.",None,PORTFOLIO RECOVERY ASSOCIATES INC,NY,10001,None,Consent provided,Web,03/12/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8532047
