05/16/24,Debt collection,Other debt,Communication tactics,"Used obscene, profane, or other abusive language","I received a phone call from a debt collector claiming to be calling about a debt owed. I let the collector know that I was at work and that it was not a great time to speak. The collector did not ask me when was a better time to talk and continued the conversation. I told the collector that I would like to have everything in writing, and he responded with someone else 's address and that they have sent letters to an address where I do not reside. I told him again that I would like to have everything in writing and it's not a debt I owe. He told me to give him an updated address to which I responded that that is his problem to fix and not the consumers '. He answered that it was my debt, that I will be paying for it and I will tell him a new address for the company to send it. The collector promised me that I will pay this or it would go on my credit report. I told him that I wouldn't be doing any of the sort and to please continue the conversation in writing. The debt collector then hung up on me mid-sentence without an explanation or a callback. I felt very humiliated, angered, and confused after the call. 

The debt was placed on my credit report the next day, and to this day, I still receive phone calls and emails referencing the debt asking when I want to pay the debt BEFORE it's placed on my report. The debt is already placed on my report and this is becoming harassing for something that they have messed up. 
On a later date, I was also told by another XXXX of their debt collectors that the credit file has not been placed on my report yet although I was viewing it on my report as she was speaking.",None,"Aldous & Associates, PLLC",NY,119XX,None,Consent provided,Web,05/16/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9027769
