03/13/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"I hope this letter finds you well. I am writing to express my deep concern and frustration regarding the unresolved issue of fraudulent items on my account. This marks my multiple attempts to rectify this issue, and it is essential to address this matter promptly and effectively. 

I want to stress that the persistence of these fraudulent items is causing me significant distress and financial hardship. It has also eroded my trust in Credit Bureaus, which I had previously regarded highly. As a loyal customer, I expected a higher level of service and security, which has been lacking in this situation. 

I kindly request that you take immediate and comprehensive action to investigate and rectify this matter. I expect a prompt response, detailing the specific steps your company will take to address the issue, as well as a clear timeline for the resolution process. Additionally, I urge you to strengthen your security measures to prevent such incidents from happening in the future. 

If my concerns are not addressed satisfactorily and promptly, I may have no choice but to escalate this matter further, which may involve seeking legal remedies and notifying relevant authorities about the fraudulent activities associated with my account. With this, I am asking for your assistance to remove these fraud items in my credit file : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, NY XXXX XXXX XXXX  XXXX Balance : {$3300.00} XXXX XXXX XXXX Balance : {$3300.00}.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,11236,None,Consent provided,Web,03/13/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8527073
