03/12/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"A few months ago, I was trying to change travel plans with XXXX XXXX due to illness. I XXXX  for a customer service number for XXXX XXXX and called the number XXXX provided. 

The person I spoke to claimed to be a XXXX representative and charged me nearly {$700.00} for the option to cancel my flight and receive the remainder of the cost back. As this was way less than the total cost of the flight, I agreed, despite my misgivings. I immediately realized something didn't feel right, and asked them to cancel the transaction, but they refused. 

I later found a different number for XXXX on the official website, and found out that cancelations are free, and that I had been scammed. The representative worked for some kind of travel agency pretending to be XXXX ; I received absolutely nothing in exchange for my ~ {$700.00}. 

I immediately called Citi, my credit card company, to dispute the charge and let them know I had been defrauded. Weeks later I received a notification that they would not reimburse me for the fraudulent charge. I spoke to a Citi representative who understood the situation and told me she would take care of it and secure my reiumbursement. Again, several weeks later, I received a notification that they are still refusing to reiumburse what is quite clearly fraud. I challenged it yet again, provided proof that I had received nothing in exchange for the {$700.00}, no good or service, and was denied a third time despite the merchant not providing anything that refuted my claims. 

I have provided Citi detailed documentation of this fraud, including copies of an email the company sent me with a XXXX logo in their signature, as well as my immediate request to cancel the transaction. At this point, my only recourse is to continue submitting my claim through the same process that has now denied me three times. 

Furthermore, I am not the only one who has suffered this exact scam there are news articles ( which I also provided to Citi ) about this exact phenomenon.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,10028,None,Consent provided,Web,03/12/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8532138
05/18/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Fees or interest,Problem with fees,"CareCredit has determined that, unless I opt in to electronic statements, I will be charged {$1.00} every month for paper statements. This is a JUNK FEE and simply unacceptable. To ensure that I am forced into accepting electronic statements, they will not make electronic statements available to anyone who prefers paper statements. In other words, because I choose paper statements, I can not see my statements online. This is fine and should be enough. Now, to ensure that I am forced to accept only electronic statements, they have decided to rip me off. This is particularly problematic because CareCredit offers 0 % financing for XXXX months on purchases over {$200.00} - a feature I use regularly. I can avoid interest charges because I get my paper statement and can easily see when any balance needs to be paid off. This gambit of theirs will surely cause more of their customers to miss the deadline for payments without interest as statement notices get buried among the hundreds of emails their customers get every day- which means they will benefit not only from the fee but from all the deferred interest they will now be sure to gather. CareCredit should not be permitted to manipulate and gouge their customers in this way. I'm sure these fees will also hit the underprivileged and elderly hardest.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL,NY,10028,None,Consent provided,Web,05/18/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9039726
