03/05/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"I am writing this letter to demand the immediate removal of accounts that have been unlawfully placed on my credit report as a means to extort me. These accounts are as follows : A pass due bill of {$870.00} that was placed by XXXX XXXX XXXX ; to this account I am enforcing all of the codes of the Fair Credit Reporting Act, but especially code 15 { 681 }. Due to the fact that XXXX XXXX XXXX is a Telecommunications corporation and not a bank or a lending institution that extended a loan or line of credit. Therefore they are barred by from putting a closed account on my reports. 

The second account is an American Express Business Credit card debt of {$1300.00} that was assigned to my limited liability Corporation. I am protected by various federal and state financial laws due to the fact that this debt is assigned to the L.L.C. that protects me from creditors coming after my personal assets ; the debt belongs to the L.L.C. as an entity not myself. The F.C.R.A. declares that my credit score is a personal asset. 

Please contact the credit reporting agencies and as a federal bureau enforce them to remove these accounts. 

