04/22/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Problem with a lender or other company charging your account,Transaction was not authorized,"XX/XX/year> Dear Sir or Madam, I would like to make a formal complaint on the handling of my Bank of America account, number XXXX. The bank did not protect my money : On XX/XX/year>, I was the victim of a fraudulent and terrifying scam. My life and my family 's life was threatened by texts and by graphic photos. It was the scariest day of my life. 
I was in my XXXX  dorm alone when the scammers did this terrible crime. Scammers deposited bogus checks into my account totaling XXXX, and I believed that I owed them the money. My life was threatened if I didnt return it at once. I have sent pictures of these texts to Bank of America. I have yet to hear back. This is the first time I was a victim of a crime. 

Im extremely disappointed with Bank of Americas response that it was a self scam. 
I have had this account with Bank of America since I was XXXX XXXX XXXX, its a XXXX   account, and I feel as though it should have been more protected. Because of this scam, I am now overdrawn XXXX dollars. I dont work and my mom puts in a few XXXX a month so that I can have spending money. I dont have any recurring deposit from work coming into my account and do not have the money to bring the balance to XXXX. I didnt even know Bank of America would overdraw for hundreds of dollars like this, leaving me responsible. My acct is frozen now ( XXXX ). I dont want to ruin my credit in the future with this debt. I was the victim of a horrific crime as evident by all of these text messages. 

There are so many banks, my mom trusted Bank of America to protect my money and my brothers money who has an account there too.This is both of our first banking experiences, if that counts at all. 

Im XXXX, and would like to continue with Bank of America, but I want to know if profit is more important than relationships with customers. Im asking for you to please help with this matter, I was traumatized by the scammer and now a second time by Bank of America. 

I would like to make a formal complaint about the customer service from Bank of America and how a youth debit account does not have adequate protection against predators. 

Thank you very much, XXXX XXXX",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION",NY,105XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/22/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8821220
