04/13/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"I am filing a complaint regarding the handling of a dispute with my bank concerning a transaction with XXXX. 

I purchased a laptop from XXXX in XX/XX/XXXX, order number. Upon discovering the laptop was faulty, I returned it via XXXX drop-off. XXXX initially confirmed receipt of the returned item. However, after several months, they claimed to have received the wrong item and refused to issue a refund. 

Despite providing the tracking number for my return, my bank has failed to resolve the dispute, asserting that the charge from XXXX is valid as of XX/XX/XXXX. 

I request your assistance in resolving this matter and ensuring a fair resolution. 

Thank you for your attention to this complaint.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,10598,None,Consent provided,Web,04/13/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8759930
03/31/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am writing to file a formal complaint against XXXX XXXX  and Portfolio Recovery Associates regarding the misuse of my credit report, which violates federal laws and my consumer rights. 

I want to emphasize that I have already opted out previously from having my information reported, yet XXXX XXXX  and Portfolio Recovery Associates disregarded this opt-out and unlawfully reported information on my credit report, which is a clear violation of federal law and my rights. 

Furthermore, pursuant to 15 USC 1681 ( b ), which outlines permissible purposes for obtaining a consumer 's credit report, XXXX XXXX  and Portfolio Recovery Associates did not obtain my written consent to furnish any information on my credit report, nor did they provide me with the option to opt out. This is a direct violation of my rights under this federal law. 

Their actions also violate the Privacy Act of 1974, which mandates the protection of individuals ' personal information held by federal agencies and certain other organizations. By unlawfully reporting my information without my consent and ignoring my opt-out request, XXXX XXXX  and Portfolio Recovery Associates have infringed upon my privacy rights. 

Moreover, it is unlawful to report transaction history on a credit report without proper authorization, as stated in 16 CFR 313.7. This regulation prohibits the disclosure of sensitive personal information without the consumer 's consent, further highlighting the severity of these violations. 

Additionally, 16 CFR 433.2, which addresses the preservation of consumer claims and defenses, is relevant in this context. This regulation ensures that consumers have the ability to assert their rights and defenses, including the right to dispute inaccurate or unauthorized information on their credit reports. 

I demand that XXXX XXXX  and Portfolio Recovery Associates immediately remove the inaccurate reporting from my credit report and update it to reflect that the debt is paid in full. Furthermore, I demand that they provide the following documents : the account XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX, and XXXX XXXX XXXX. Failure to provide these documents would indicate that they can not prove that anything is owed at all. 

Moreover, I want to highlight that XXXX XXXX  and Portfolio Recovery Associates have committed identity theft by mishandling my social security number, which is a serious violation of my privacy and security. 

Neither XXXX XXXX  nor Portfolio Recovery Associates has the right to use the non-mailable addresses they have on file, and all communication must only be through the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ). 

Failure to comply with these demands may result in further legal action. I expect immediate action to rectify these violations and ensure that my consumer rights are upheld in the future.",None,PORTFOLIO RECOVERY ASSOCIATES INC,NY,11233,None,Consent provided,Web,03/31/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8660373
