03/18/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Fees or interest,Charged too much interest,"In XXXX XXXX XXXX I took out a loan to install some heat pumps in my house. The total was approximately {$2200.00}. I was informed that the loan was to be interest-free for XXXX months, at which time I would be charged the typical exorbitant rate. I was never informed that this interest would be retroactive to loan origination date and was led to believe I would be charged interest on loan balance, as I have on every other loan or credit card I have ever used with a promotional rate. After XXXX  months my loan balance was down to {$7700.00}. On my next statement I was assessed and interest payment of {$8300.00}! I have contacted the bank and was told I should have read my statement more carefully. In hindsight I should have but I never would have believed that this practice and I had never encountered this type of loan in my life and still can not believe that this practice is legal and it is certainly not ethical. I made every payment on time and never expected the astronomical fee.I feel violated.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL,NY,120XX,Older American,Consent provided,Web,03/18/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8574846
