05/16/24,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",Domestic (US) money transfer,Money was not available when promised,None,"My bank is Citibank. On XX/XX/2024, I had {$39000.00} on my checking account. My first payment, on that day, was a Direct Debit ( ACH ) to the IRS for {$14000.00}. Then, a payment to my credit card for {$21000.00} - which my bank called a "" transfer '' because they issued my credit card. My 3rd payment was actually a transfer to my saving account for {$10000.00}. At that point, I didn't pay attention that I was overdraft because I have the overdraft protection between my checking and my savings. Finally, my XXXX payment was done thru XXXX for {$3000.00}. During the whole day, no where on the application it showed the overdraft, all my payments looked that they were processed. The day after, the payment for the IRS was rejected but all other payments were processed. I got penalties, interests and fees to pay to the IRS. I filed a complaint to my bank for not processing my payments in the order that I sent them. I was told that the payments that go first are the transfers from account to account and then the biggest amounts. I asked also when these rules where communicated to me because I was not aware of these. They didn't reply. I asked in which documentation these rules are shown but they told me that they did not have the documentation.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,10128,None,Consent provided,Web,05/16/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,9024942
