06/09/23,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",Domestic (US) money transfer,Fraud or scam,None,"Two years ago, XX/XX/2021, I was victim to financial fraud for a sublease apartment that was a false advertisement/ scam. 

I applied for the apartment, as is common practice, giving them my personal information and also sent them four rent deposit payments through Chase BankXXXX for the sum of {$4800.00}. 

I was persuaded and sent the payment under false pretenses. Once the payments were sent, the apartment lender stopped contact and never fulfilled the apartment agreement. 

I contacted Chase Bank immediately to stop or intercept the payments, however, Chase said they would not be able to help me ( Claim Number : XXXX ). I also immediately contacted XXXX however they said I would need to contact my financial institution ( Chase ) to dispute the charges. No action was taken to help me and I was caught in the gap between the two financial services.

Because of the seriousness of the issue, I opened a case with the Police Department and reported it to the IC3 ( internet crime complaint center ) run by the FBI. The police department detective never resolved the case/ discovered who the perpetrator was, saying that because the bank facilitated the transaction, they should have the information on the perpetrator. However, the bank did not or said they could not disclose that information to me. 

At the time, due to covid, I did not have resources beyond this to investigate the issue. 

I looked up that while other money transfer options like XXXX are not FDIC-Insured, XXXX is directly affiliated with my bank and account. 

I am filing a claim with CFPB because I also looked up that under 12 CFR Part 1005 - Electronic Fund Transfers ( Regulation E ) by the Federal Reserve Board consumers should be protected from accidental transfers and forms of fraud when they use electronic fund and remittance transfers.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11375,None,Consent provided,Web,06/09/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,7095454
03/13/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Closing an account,Funds not received from closed account,"Ive been paying my rent through an app called XXXX since XXXX using my chime card so they can see several transactions to XXXX from my account on XX/XX/XXXX. XXXX had a nationwide glitch and they double charged. Everybody so then returned the second charge so they put the deposit back into my account And chime is saying its suspicious activity. You can clearly see on my statements that Ive been dealing with ZRent several times so Im not understanding what the issue is they wont give me my money back they wont help me. I have sent proof who I am I have sent proof showing them that you had a glitch. I have sent text messages between me and my landlord that verified that there was an issue. They double charged him too. I dont understand how and why they can get away with this, its outrageous",None,Chime Financial Inc,NY,137XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/13/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8541399
04/07/23,Mortgage,Conventional home mortgage,Trouble during payment process,None,"My mortgage was in an agreed eighteen month abeyance under the Covid program ( see attached letter ) Before it was due to expire I got in touch with Wells Fargo to commence repayment and to find out how the payments not made in the abeyance period were to be made good I got no clear answer with Wells Fargo suddenly talking about having to requalify for reinstating the mortgage and sending me documents about foreclosure and mortgage assistance, which I did not request. ( see enclosed ) Very alarmed at the turn this has taken which bears no connection with anything said or agreed at the start of during the process of abeyance. 

I called monthly to update Wells Fargo. I was expressly told that payments in abeyance could be tacked on to the end of the mortgage to pay at that time or if sold. 
