04/29/23,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"XXXX is reporting my late payments to third parties agencies which in this matter are the three credit agencies which are TransUnion, XXXX and XXXX. Pursuant 15 U.S. Code 1666b - Timing of payments ( a ) A creditor may not treat a payment on a credit card account under an open end consumer credit plan as late for any purpose, unless the creditor has adopted reasonable procedures designed to ensure that each periodic statement including the information required by section 1637 ( b ) of this title is mailed or delivered to the consumer not later than 21 days before the payment due date. XXXX is in clear violation of this law. XXXX is also reporting my transactions or experiences which is another violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act 15 USC 1681 ( 2 ) ( a ) ( i ) Exclusions from a consumer report clearly states ( 2 ) EXCLUSIONS- Except as provided in paragraph ( 3 ), the term "" consumer report '' does not include ( a ) subject to section 1681s-3 of this title, any- ( i ) report containing information solely as to transactions or experiences between the consumer and the person making the report ; which in this matter is my Utilization. XXXX has been my causing my family and I huge distress by reporting these items on my consumer report with its negative impact.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,10310,None,Consent provided,Web,04/29/23,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,6906087
