04/29/23,Mortgage,Other type of mortgage,Struggling to pay mortgage,None,"Our mortgage lender NBT Bank has denied us access to government programs to help struggling homeowners and we are now in the first stages of foreclosure. My husband and I bought our home with a USDA loan and live here with our XXXX boys, ages XXXX, XXXX and XXXX. We had financial struggles during Covid and contacted our lender NBT Bank to see if they could offer any type of help. The agent was rude and condescending and said there were no programs except for find a way to pay us or we will take your house. I was not able to work due to Covid shutting down my position and we did not know about the CARES act forbearance and did not know that there were any loan modification programs for distressed homeowners and NBT Bank did not want to tell us about any options. We were very frightened and had to apply for a loan from my husband 's 401K to get caught up, a loan we are still having to make payments on from my husbands check. After getting caught up and going back to work we had no problems with payments for about a year until I got XXXX and it was a XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX and the doctor told me I needed to stay off my feet and again we lost my income and the good news now we have a healthy XXXX XXXX XXXX son but it was hard to keep up with the mortgage payments. We contacted NBT Bank to see if they would work with us on the payments or if they could help us, and they said we would have to pay 100 % of missed payments and late fees and legal fees or they would put us into foreclosure. We just got letter from Attorney last week and we are now in foreclosure. My husband has a good job, he has worked as a XXXX  and is now the XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXXXXXX at the local XXXX XXXX. I had been working as a XXXX XXXX but when Covid came they shut down my district for XXXX. A few months after I went back to work I became pregnant and we lost my income again. At this time my husband has taken a second job working as a XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. We no longer have a problem with the mortgage payment, the only issue is that NBT Bank is telling us we need to pay them {$15000.00} in one payment or we are going to lose our house. We now know that NBT Bank is required as a servicer of a USDA loan to consider us for several different distressed homeowner options which they have told us did not exist in the past.",None,NBT BANCORP INC.,NY,XXXXX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/29/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6907815
