03/19/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"I am sending this complaint to address a concerning issue regarding late payments reported on my credit report. Upon careful review of my credit report, I have discovered discrepancies in the reported late payments and am seeking your assistance in promptly correcting or removing these inaccuracies. 

Regarding the account with XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX ), I wish to clarify that this account has never been late. The reported late payment is erroneous, as all payments were made on time. Data Furnisher said they were going to update it to open/never late. Please fix ASAP. 

Similarly, concerning the XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX ) account, I want to emphasize that this account has never experienced late payments. The reported late payment is inaccurate, as payments were consistently made on time. I kindly request that the late payment markings be updated to accurately reflect my payment history, and the bank said they were going to update it to open/never late. Please update ASAP. 

Recognizing the importance of maintaining accurate credit information, I am committed to resolving this matter promptly. I kindly request your assistance in investigating and correcting these inaccuracies at your earliest convenience. Enclosed, please find supporting documentation validating my claim and providing evidence of the incorrect reporting. With your expertise, I am confident that we can rectify these discrepancies efficiently. 

I kindly request that you initiate an investigation into this matter and promptly inform me of the results. If the late payments are found to be accurate, I request an explanation of the findings. However, if they are determined to be inaccurately reported, I request immediate correction or removal from my credit report.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11570,None,Consent provided,Web,03/19/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8580188
03/19/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"I am writing to bring to your urgent attention a critical issue concerning my credit report. Upon reviewing it, I have discovered fraudulent accounts that do not belong to me. I formally dispute the presence of these unauthorized accounts and request their immediate and aggressive removal from my credit report. As a victim of identity theft, I am perplexed as to why the CRA is not complying with the law, especially when the other bureaus have done so. I have provided supporting documentation, including a copy of my identity document, police reports, and any other relevant materials, to substantiate the claim that these accounts are a result of identity theft or fraudulent activity. The fraudulent accounts in question are as follows : XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX XXXX. 

Recognizing the importance of your role in maintaining accurate and reliable credit information, I urge you to swiftly and aggressively investigate and remove these fraudulent accounts from my credit report. It is crucial that these unauthorized entries be deleted as soon as possible to prevent further damage to my credit score and financial standing. I appreciate your understanding of the urgency surrounding this matter and request your prompt attention in resolving this dispute. I hereby request that you initiate an immediate investigation into these fraudulent accounts and provide me with the results as soon as possible. I expect that you will take all necessary actions to promptly delete these entries, ensuring the accuracy and integrity of my credit report. Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter. I eagerly anticipate a swift resolution and the removal of the fraudulent accounts from my credit report.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11570,None,Consent provided,Web,03/19/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8580615
