03/26/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Closing an account,Company closed your account,"I got an email from my bank warning me that my accounts were going to be restricted and closed soon because they suspected fraud activity, therefore they are protecting me and their bank, and I have to call them soon. My phone service wasn't paid for at the moment, therefore, I couldn't call them, so I went and messaged them on the XXXX app explaining all the above mentioned. I asked them why my account was getting restricted, I opted for XXXX or the XXXX XXXX because they don't have live chat support with a real person. They told me I had to call them, and that I could use a calling app, I had never heard of these calling apps before, but I searched for one the following days and later was able to call them. Upon calling, I asked them why my accounts were getting restricted and closed soon, the customer service representative told me my accounts were not just going to be restricted or closed, but they had already been flagged with notes as closed, and that I couldn't and will never be able to work with their bank any more in my life. 

I told her that made no sense, they did not even let me explain myself because I don't do fraud, and have no direct deposit currently, therefore, no one might have deposited a fake check or money. Unless I was hacked which clearly can not be my fault. She told me that the decision was final, I asked if she could tell me which kind of fraud they suspected, and she told me that the exact fraud/ reason was not disclosed to her. So I called other numbers they sent me to see if maybe they knew the reason, and their suspicions were a mistake, I could explain to them and my accounts don't get closed. All the numbers I called had the same response, "" The decision is final and can not be changed, and I don't think that if you contact the hire ups anything is going to change. '' So now here I am, my accounts are getting closed, I don't know which fraud they suspected, and neither do all their representatives. Mind you my accounts were overdrawn by monthly fees and I was trying to make payments and they were denied.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,13208,None,Consent provided,Web,03/26/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8618176
