09/06/24,Mortgage,Conventional home mortgage,Trouble during payment process,Trying to communicate with the company to fix an issue while managing or servicing your loan,"After my mother passed away in XXXX, I established an estate, which was formalized in XXXX. At that time, I sent all the estate information to XXXX XXXX XXXX. The loan was transferred to Fay Servicing in XXXX, and I provided them with the same documents. I have owned the home with my mother for XXXX years, and up until now, I was able to communicate effectively with the mortgage company. However, I have repeatedly tried to communicate with Fay Servicing, and they refuse to provide me with any information about the mortgage. I have sent the death certificate several times, but each time I call, I receive the same response. On XX/XX/XXXX, I mailed a certified letter with return receipt, including a payment of {$260000.00} to Fay Servicing to settle the account. In my letter of instruction, I requested that if my payment was not going to be applied to the account, it should be returned to me. Fay Servicing neither returned my payment nor applied it to the account as instructed. In XX/XX/XXXX, I hired a title company to conduct a title audit of the documents associated with my mother 's mortgage. The examiner discovered title fraud, forgery, and theft. I will be reporting them to all the proper agencies.",None,"Fay Servicing, LLC",NY,115XX,Older American,Consent provided,Web,09/06/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,10042978
