03/22/24,Debt collection,Credit card debt,Took or threatened to take negative or legal action,Threatened to arrest you or take you to jail if you do not pay,"I constantly have been receiving phone calls from different numbers but associated with the same company, which at first they called XXXX XXXX, saying they want to collect a debt I had with Paypal. They usually call early morning or in very inconvenient times when i'm at work and can not talk. I never received any official information from them, other than those very suspecting phone calls. Today at XXXXXXXX XXXX when i was running late to work in the cold weather of XXXX, they called me again, from another phone number I never saw. Without even identifying themselves, they asked to confirm my name and my address. I said i could not talk at that moment and that I did not feel comfortable to confirm personal information by phone not knowing exactly who i was talking to, and if for some reason they were an official company, to please mail me some letter or documents and information I could trust more. This lady was trying to settle an agreement to pay my Paypal credit card debt, even though i told her I wasn't feeling trust, and I lost my access to my credit card information on my paypal account, for a long time. She was very misterious and refusing to answer my questions about the company, but threatening me and trying to give me an ultimate chance to no get into a legal action, accepting an agreement immediately. Then she transferred the phone to a man who identified himself as the "" manager '', without giving me his name either. He was speaking in a very agressive tone and forcing me to accept an agreement asking how much could I pay by-weekly. When I asked more information about the company, he refused to give me and said I should accept the agreement first, before he could give me any information about my debt or the company, and threatening to send me to court, have the money taken from my bank account and be charged all the legal fees to myself, if I didnt accept this blind agreement by phone, with people I dont know, phone number I don't know, and company I don't even know if its official. I asked what was he could offer me and he said he would not charge anymore interest, from the date I started my payment plan. After a lot of disrespect and harrassment he decided to give me more information and provided me with their webpage, surprisingly the name was different now "" Midlandcredit.com '', and an account number they created for my case. He did not give me too much time to look, and was always pressuring me about the by-weekly payment deal. I asked if I would need to see at least my late statements, to have an idea of what was going on, and then he showed me some he got after Paypal assigned the debt for his collection. I started look into those statements and notice Paypal had already accumulated a lot of interest and late fees from all this time since they closed my card, asking him to clarify, but heis answers were always very aggressive and intimidating. And I told him I could agree to pay my original balance in full, from the day of the last payment if he avoided all those fees and interests after that. He agreed but only if I payed immediately. I asked more time to check the company and the rules, and he said Monday. He immediately asked for me to tell him by phone my routing and checking account number, for him to charge me almost XXXX dollars. I felt super invaded, insecure and told that to him. That I would prefer to pay on the website, after I checked the accuracy of all that. He them started being aggressive again and threatened to snd me to court, "" if that was my choice '', and hung up the phone, in a very unpolite disrespectful and violent way. This man did not seem like a manager or a lawyer, he really seemed like a scammer that was anxious and frustrated to have almost touched my big money and being caught.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL,NY,11235,None,Consent provided,Web,04/05/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8603838
03/07/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"Dear XXXX : I hope this message finds you well. I am writing to bring several incidents of identity theft to your attention, which have significantly impacted my credit report. The incidents are documented as follows : 1. On XX/XX/XXXX, I filed a police report ( Complaint Number : XXXX ) regarding the unauthorized opening of accounts. Despite my efforts, these accounts were not opened or authorized by me. 

2. On XX/XX/XXXX, I filed another police report ( Complaint Number : XXXX ) concerning identity theft issues related to my personal information. 
Accounts listed on credit report : XXXX  XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX I kindly request that you conduct a thorough investigation into these matters and take the necessary steps to rectify the inaccuracies in my credit file resulting from these fraudulent activities. The false information has significantly affected my personal life, causing stress, XXXX, frustration, and loss of sleep. 
I was planning to buy a house and was never able to do that because of this wrong reporting .Additionally, I afraid that Department of education will start garnishing my salary .I was contacting them on a numerous of occasions but without any success .I truly believe that you are the only one who can help Once your investigation is complete, I would appreciate receiving a copy of my credit report reflecting the accurate and updated information. Additionally, I request that you share this letter with your customers when conveying my disputes, or provide me with the contact details of the relevant individuals at the implicated companies. 

Should you require any further information to support these disputes, please do not hesitate to contact me at my daytime phone number : ( XXXX ) XXXX, you can also communicate with me through my email address at XXXX. 

Thank you for your prompt attention to this matter, and I look forward to a swift resolution. 
I attach my Driver License with my current address, Permanent Resident Card.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,11230,None,Consent provided,Web,03/07/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8499641
