10/28/22,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Problem with a credit reporting company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"I am a victim of Identity Theft, on XXXX and XX/XX/2022 ive disputed this fraudulent id theft account on my report ( XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX # XXXX ). 
experian and equifax have not responded and they haven't removed this fraudulent account. i filled out a ftc report for this account and they still ignore me. 
pursuant to FCRA 605B ( 15 U.S.C. & 1681 c-2 ) which states that these accounts must be removed within 4 Business Days of receipt of my last letter and they failed to do anything for two months in a row. 
thats against the law and its been more than 30 days since my last letter on XX/XX/2022 Also the XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX # XXXX is a charge off and has a balance of {$16000.00}, XXXX is a charge off account with a balance, how can it have a balance if XXXX has been paid n written it off on there books, and i also received a tax form for it. 

XXXX and equifax are breaking a number of consumer laws FCRA 605B ( 15 U.S.C. & 1681 c-2 ) 15 U.S. Code 1681b- Section 609 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ) of FCRA 605 B 15 U.S. Code 1681 C-1 15 U.S. Code 1681i ( 5 ) and needs to be removed and deleted for violations of all these laws",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,11050,None,Consent provided,Web,10/28/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6141584
