04/15/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Problem with a lender or other company charging your account,Transaction was not authorized,"A transaction ( amount : {$2500.00} ) was made with a Bank of America debit card I never received in the mail on XX/XX/2024. Upon receiving the bank 's app alert asking whether I had authorized the activity, I promptly responded no and declined it. Then I called the bank to report the fraud, during which the associate confirmed that she saw my response indicating the decline of the transaction. There were more fraudulent transactions after that call, and I have disputed them all with another call. XXXX, on XX/XX/2024, I found the transaction ( amount : {$2500.00} ) I declined still went through, so I called the bank again to file a claim. The bank hastily closed the claim on XX/XX/2024 saying it was unable to pay back the amount. 

My complaint is that the bank did not research well and it has the responsibility to protect consumers. I have compelling evidence that the transaction was not made by me : XXXX ) The non-delivery of the plastic card made it impossible for me to have authorized it. Prior to the fraudulent transaction, I could only make withdrawals from ATMs using a temporary virtual card. This was necessitated by the fact that the physical card, which I was expecting to receive in the mail since XX/XX/2024, never arrived. 

XXXX ) My XXXX 's location services have always been active so I have evidence from the data showing I was at home when the transaction occurred. The data clearly show that I had been at home until XXXX pm on XX/XX/2024. In the afternoon I went to see a XXXX show and the data precisely show I was in the XXXX XXXX area between XXXX pm and XXXX pm on XX/XX/2024. I can provide screenshots of the location services data records. 

XXXX ) As the phone was on me, I immediately saw the bank 's app alert asking whether I had authorized the activity on XX/XX/2024, and I promptly responded no and declined it. I can provide the screenshot of the alert and my response of declining it. This can also be corroborated by reviewing the initial phone call I made on XX/XX/2024 to the bank, during which the associate confirmed that she saw my decline response of the transaction. 

To summarize, the fraudulent transaction was made using the plastic card that I had been anticipating but never received in the mail. The location data records show that I was at home when the transaction happened. I immediately declined the transaction upon seeing the alert message in the bank app. 

If the card was not delivered safely into my hands, shouldn't the responsibility for covering the charge fall upon the bank? Moreover, despite my decline, the transaction still went through. Shouldnt the bank be responsible and stop the payment immediately? 

With the substantial evidence Ive mentioned, which I could all provide, I don't believe my claim should be closed so hastily, and I believe further investigation needs to be done. The fraudulent transaction should not be paid by the customer.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION",NY,11354,None,Consent provided,Web,04/15/24,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8771991
04/12/24,Student loan,Private student loan,Getting a loan,High pressure sales tactics or recruiting,"I attended XXXX XXXX and graduated in XXXX. ( Later changed to XXXX XXXX ) Upon enrolling and during attendance to the school, I took out both Federal and Private loans to pay for the program. It later came to light that this school, along with lots of other schools engaged in misleading and pressuring students to enroll in their programs. In XXXX, I applied to Borrower Defense Program with the US Department of Education. XX/XX/XXXX, I was advised that my applications was part of a class action lawsuit- XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX ( XXXX. XXXX. ). XX/XX/XXXX, I was advised that my application for borrower defense was ineligible. XX/XX/XXXX, I was advised of a proposed settlement in connection with the XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX lawsuit. XX/XX/XXXX, I was advised that my school was named in the lawsuit. The settlement terms were as follows : "" If your borrower defense application related to federal student loans borrowed to pay for attendance at a school on the list attached to this letter, you will receive a discharge of federal loans associated with that school and a refund of any amounts paid to the Department on those federal loans, and the credit tradeline for those loans will be deleted from your credit report. Within 90 days of the date that the court 's approval of the settlement agreement becomes final, the Department will notify you that you will receive this relief. You will receive the relief within one year of the final effective date of the settlement agreement. Until this relief is provided, the Department will not take action to collect your debt. '' Since the school I attended engaged in these tactics, I believe my Navient loans should be discharged as well. 

I have diligently paid several thousands to Navient for a school loan that I was misled and pressured into taking out. I've carried this burden for far too long and would like relief from this.",None,"Navient Solutions, LLC.",NY,117XX,None,Consent provided,Web,04/12/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8756128
