04/08/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Closing your account,Company closed your account,"On XX/XX/XXXX, I applied for the Amtrak Guest Rewards Preferred credit card from the First National Bank of Omaha. I was instantly approved, and granted a credit limit of {$13000.00}. I waited for the card to arrive, and when I received the letter that I anticipated to be the credit card, it was in fact a letter stating my account had been closed due to elements associated with fraud, dated XX/XX/XXXX. I contacted the bank multiple times, very concerned about this letter, as I was quite shocked to receive such a notice. None of the representatives ever gave me a definite answer as to why this occurred. XXXX representative in the security and fraud department speculated that it was due to my recent move ( From XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX ), but could not formally confirm this. 

He explained that they attempted to contact me, but could not get through, and I confirmed this to be the case, as my spam filter blocked the unknown caller. Thus, by the time I received the letter, appeal was impossible. The agent apologized for the inconvenience, saying that had I been able to explain my recent move, and the fact that I applied on board an XXXX XXXX, the account would have been easily reopened. He recommended that I reapply for the card, and that explaining the situation should nearly-guarantee approval. 

I waited a few months, until XX/XX/XXXX, and reapplied for the card. Unlike last time, I did not receive instant approval. The next day, upon checking the online portal, I found that my application had been denied. I immediately called to explain my situation, and was offered a callback by management. I received this callback, and was spoken to very rudely by a representative who made no attempt to understand my situation, and brushed me off. 

When I finally received the letter with the reasons for denial, they were Length of time revolving accounts have been established, Number of inquiries on credit bureau report, and Length of time accounts have been established. Absolutely nothing changed regarding my credit score or income since the first ( accepted ) application, other than XXXX additional "" hard inquiry '' from applying for the card the first time. I tried to reach out multiple times to request a reconsideration, and each time I was denied. Rather, I was told to re-apply in a few months when inquiries on my credit report would be more than XXXX XXXX XXXX. 

I followed this advice, and waited again for my credit score to improve, and applied for the same card once again on XX/XX/XXXX. The application was denied once again, and only XXXX reason was provided : Past performance on associated account. Of course, the associated account in question was the original Amtrak Guest Rewards Preferred card I was approved for on XX/XX/XXXX, which was closed in error. I called, explained the situation and asked for a reconsideration given the incredibly frustrating situation I had dealt with. This request was denied, and I was rudely told to apply again. If this application was denied due to that past account, all future applications will obviously be denied too because that past account closure does not disappear. This advice to apply again was infuriating after everything I had dealt with, and after my credit had been damaged multiple times Now, I am left with XXXX hard credit inquiries on my credit report, XXXX of which were entirely unnecessary. My credit score has been damaged, and the company has routinely failed to fix the error they initially made by closing my account due to nonexistent fraud.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,FIRST NATIONAL BANK OF OMAHA,NY,10016,None,Consent provided,Web,04/08/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8723036
04/08/24,"Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service",International money transfer,Fraud or scam,None,"I am a XXXX citizen involved in an international wire transfer fraud, I used my checking account with XXXX XXXX XXXX Bank to transfer {$20000.00} to Wise XXXX  transfer service that was used to wire transfer funds internationally on XX/XX/2024 to XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ( License no. XXXX, Office : XXXX Al XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX ) and sister company XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ( Account No. XXXX ) under XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ID : XXXX ) Wise Transaction XXXX. I came across this company through an advert on website/app for local business listings called XXXX. The company was supposed to purchase a truck asset and provide me with a return on investment of {$1900.00} per month for the XXXX  year duration of the contract. The company violated the contract by defaulting the first profit payment on XX/XX/2024 and since getting the funds on XX/XX/2024 stopped responding to my phone calls and emails. They also did not use the funds to purchase a truck as as Vehicle plate XXXX shared with me as proof of purchase is no longer registered under the company per XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. The company mailed me XXXX undated security cheques from XXXX XXXX  ( Account XXXX ) for capital investment amount and for profit amount for 1 year. After the fraud was committed, I found out that these are local cheques that are not valid in XXXX be deposited in XXXX XXXX  account and victim does not have an account in XXXX to XXXX them, they are invalid. The company 's commercial license is also under transaction status with Department XXXX XXXX and XXXX XXXX since they committed the fraud. XXXX XXXX XXXX Bank was unable to help me get back the funds even though they left from my checking account. Wise money transfer service actually put this amount into the bank account of the scammer organization XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Bank Account XXXX ) but was unable to reverse the transaction or help retrive the funds. I need CFPB support to help get my money back from either XXXX XXXX, Wise, XXXX XXXX  XXXX ( XXXX : XXXX, Address : XXXX XXXX, AL XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ) or the XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ( License no. XXXX ), scammer XXXX XXXX XXXX ( XXXX ID : XXXX ) or XXXX Government. I have filed a police report with XXXX Police but have not heard back reference XXXX.",None,TransferWise Ltd,NY,10012,None,Consent provided,Web,04/08/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8722959
