06/06/24,Vehicle loan or lease,Loan,Problems at the end of the loan or lease,Unable to receive car title or other problem after the loan is paid off,"I have an auto loan with Bridgecrest. The vehicle was involved in an accident on XX/XX/year> and was declared a total loss on XX/XX/year>. Bridgecrest was notified by my insurance company of the total loss on XX/XX/year>. My Retail Installment Contract includes a XXXX XXXX which states : "" In the event of theft or damage to the Vehicle resulting in a total loss, there may be a gap between the amount due under the terms of the Contract and the sum of the actual cash value of the Vehicle ( as defined in your insurance policy if it is in effect on the date of the loss ) and any unpaid amounts under the Contract that accrued prior to the date of the loss as a result of your failure to fulfill the obligations under the Contract ( the 'Gap Amount ' ). We hereby waive our ability to recover any Gap Amount in the event of theft or physical damage to the Vehicle that results in a total loss. You will not be liable for the Gap Amount, as described, in the event of a total loss due to theft or physical damage to the Vehicle. '' Bridgecrest received the payout from my insurance company on XX/XX/year>, which satisfied the terms of my contract in full. When I contacted Bridgecrest on XX/XX/year> requesting a Loan Satisfaction Letter, I was informed that I would need to wait an additional XXXX business days for the payment to clear. Since my next payment is due before the XXXX business day, I requested that payments be suspended and confirmation be provided in writing. Bridgecrest declined to provide written confirmation, stating that the phone line was being recorded and they were assuring me there would be no impact on my credit if autopay was turned off. They claimed that they could only provide "" form letters '' and were not permitted to send personalized correspondences. 

According to the terms of my XXXX XXXX, all payments should have been suspended at the very least on the day Bridgecrest was notified of the total loss, XX/XX/year>. Refusing to suspend the payment and provide written confirmation constitutes an unfair and unreasonable business practice.",None,Bridgecrest Acceptance Corporation,NY,121XX,None,Consent provided,Web,06/06/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9195330
