10/30/22,Credit card or prepaid card,Store credit card,"Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers",Didn't receive advertised or promotional terms,"On or around the summer of 2021 I opened a Home Depot credit card and project loan card. I purchased kitchen cabinets. I was offered 18 mos zero percent financing at the time. I made the purchase of the cabinets in XXXX of 2021 and after a few months of getting my bills I noticed it said six months for the expiration date of the offer. I realized something was wrong. I called both the store and the issuing bank of the card and told them I was supposed to get 18 months and I only got six. The bank changed it to the 18 month offer. I have no idea how this mistake occurred. About five months ago, I applied with the bank to see if I can get it extended. I realized that there was no way I was going to be able to pay off this purchase in 18 months. It is over {$9000.00} originally. I was denied. They told me I didn't qualify because I had already extended it. I said, no I did not. When? They were referring to the error, the six months to the 18 months. I said but that was an error. That was not an extension. I was supposed to get 18 months originally. Someone made a mistake. Period. Either the store, someone did. I know what I was offered and they for sure have 18 month plans. All the time. How could they even try to deny it? So, now, because of that original error, that went against me and I can't extend the terms.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,10314,None,Consent provided,Web,10/30/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6143404
