03/26/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account status incorrect,"Around XX/XX/XXXX, Comenity encountered a customer service outage, leaving cardholders unable to manage their accounts or make payments. My account was affected and I was unable to make my payment on XXXX XXXX and thereafter. Comenity Bank later stated on XX/XX/XXXX, that their system update was taking longer than expected, causing disruptions. Despite this, they failed to inform customers beforehand. On XX/XX/XXXX, I received an email regarding a billing statement update, acknowledging the website 's temporary downtime. The email provided alternative payment options. Despite attempts to contact customer service on XX/XX/XXXX and XX/XX/XXXX, no assistance was available, leading to late payments and credit score impact. Although Comenity claimed access restoration on XX/XX/XXXX, ongoing system outages persisted, affecting account access and payment capabilities. On XX/XX/XXXX, Comenity admitted to continued disruptions, contradicting their earlier statement. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, Comenity acknowledged on XXXX that intermittent outages were still affecting its services, without extending late fee waivers or providing further accommodations for affected customers. Despite instructions to use XXXX and telephone channels, I couldn't pay my bill during the outage, resulting in late fees. 
Despite assurances from Comenity Bank that the outage would be brief, I couldn't access my account for weeks, missing the credit card payment deadline. Comenity attempted to ease concerns by waiving late fees for payments due between XX/XX/XXXX and XX/XX/XXXX, and assured that late payments wouldn't impact credit scores, urging the use of XXXX online. 

It wasn't until XX/XX/XXXX, that I regained account access, allowing me to make an immediate payment. However, on XX/XX/XXXX, XXXX XXXX notified me of past due status reported to all three credit bureaus. Despite disputing this, Comenity insisted on the accuracy of their reporting. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, I sought a goodwill adjustment from Comenity, but they failed to acknowledge their error. Instead, on XX/XX/XXXX, they reiterated their obligation to report accurate information under the FCRA. 

Comenity 's actions violate the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act and the Federal Trade Commission Act by providing misleading information and causing substantial harm to my credit report. Their failure to ensure operational payment sites and customer service lines led to significant damage to my credit history. I request an investigation and the correction of payment histories across all three credit bureaus for XX/XX/XXXX, supported by attached evidence.",None,"Bread Financial Holdings, Inc.",NY,10940,None,Consent provided,Web,03/26/24,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8633715
