The FCRA mandates that XXXX promptly investigate and rectify the issues raised in this communication within four business days from the receipt date, as stipulated in 605B ( a ). Attached are relevant sections of the Fair Credit Reporting Act, namely 605B ( Block of information resulting from a Data Breach [ 15 U.S.C. 1681c-2 ] ) and 604 ( Permissible purposes of consumer reports [ 15 U.S.C. 1681b ] ). I did not authorize these actions, constituting a breach of my privacy rights. Kindly scrutinize the listed accounts and inquiries, taking immediate corrective action based on your findings or for non-compliance. Per FCRA, XXXX must liaise with the creditor and validate the item within 30 days or remove it. I have submitted an affidavit affirming clear instances of fraud and unauthorized inquiries in my credit report, urging prompt resolution to avoid legal action.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,10023,None,Consent provided,Web,03/11/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8519991
