03/19/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Upon reviewing my credit report, I noticed that these late payments listed below are inaccurately reported, which is adversely effecting my creditworthiness. 
XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX with account number XXXX XXXX XXXX with account number XXXX Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act : 15 USC 1681 Section 602 guarantees my right to privacy. This ensures the confidentiality of my credit report and mandates that information on it must be reported in a way that is fair and accurate to protect the consumer 's privacy.

15 USC 1681 Section 604a Section 2 stipulates that a consumer reporting agency can not furnish a report containing information on a consumer 's credit worthiness, credit standing, credit capacity, character, general reputation, personal characteristics, or mode of living without the consumer 's written instructions.

In light of these provisions, I challenge the authenticity and validity of the late payments recorded on my account and request your agency to produce evidence or documentation that validates this reporting in accordance with my written instructions.

Moreover, in alignment with 15 USC 1666b, a creditor may not treat a payment on a credit card account under an open- end consumer credit plan as late for any purpose unless they have adopted reasonable procedures designed to ensure that each periodic statement contains the required information. Hence, I demand proof that the said procedures were correctly adhered to in my case.

If you can not produce the necessary documents validating these late payment entries, or if the entries are found to be inaccurate, I kindly demand that they be deleted immediately or be updated to reflect as "" Paid on Time '' or "" OK ''.

It is essential for credit reporting agencies to ensure that all consumer reports are accurate, and any inaccuracies are dealt with in a swift manner. I trust that you will handle this matter with the urgency and attention it demands.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10458,None,Consent provided,Web,03/19/24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8567696
