06/01/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Funds not handled or disbursed as instructed,"On XX/XX/year> on my Chase checking joint account with my partner, there were two auto-pay withdrawals for my joint credit card on XXXX XXXX XXXX Not only should there have just been XXXX payment, but this also caused the ledger to be incorrect simply in terms of addition and as a result we are missing {$500.00} from our bank account. 

Here are the relevant line items on our checking account to demonstrate the issue : [ XX/XX/year>XXXX XXXX XXXX, Charge : - {$140.00}, Balance : {$5700.00} ], [ XX/XX/year> XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, Charge : - {$1100.00}, Balance : {$5800.00} ], [ XX/XX/year> Chase Credit Card Payment, Charge : - {$4.00}, Balance : {$7000.00} ], [ XX/XX/year> XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, Charge - {$1100.00}, Balance : {$5800.00} ], [ XX/XX/year> XXXX XXXX, Charge : - {$1.00}, Balance : {$7500.00} ] ( Note the order of these charges is reverse chronological when you read from the top ). 

If you look at the balances, you can see that they are incorrect. The math on even just one of the transactions is incorrect : {$7500.00} - {$1100.00} = XXXX but the balance goes down to {$5800.00} ( this is the first XX/XX/XXXX transaction ). Then the balance jumps up to {$7000.00} after a charge of - {$4.00} which doesn't make sense ( why would the balance go up with a deduction? ). Then the duplicate XXXX charge happens. Transactions afterwards are correct but the balance moving forward is incorrect. 

Because of that first incorrect transaction, I'm missing {$500.00} from my account and it still has not been resolved. 

I noticed this about a week after the transaction. I checked XXXX XXXX online and called them and confirmed my credit card was only paid once despite there being two charges. 

On XX/XX/year> I went to my local branch and spoke with a very helpful representative who was on the phone for approximately 2 hours trying to get this resolved for me with her back office. At the end of the two hours, she filed a form detailing the issue. Since then, she has been following up with the escalations department every week but there has been no progress made on their end to restore the {$500.00}. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, they reversed the payment to XXXX XXXX but since the balance after the first transaction wasn't calculated correctly to begin with, I'm still missing {$500.00} from my account. They effectively charged me {$1600.00} and then gave me back {$1100.00}. 

As mentioned, I have been in contact with the bank representative via email on XX/XX/XXXX, XX/XX/XXXX, XX/XX/XXXX, XX/XX/XXXX, and XX/XX/XXXX trying to get this resolved. She has been as helpful as she can but the back office is being incredibly unresponsive. 

I have attached the XXXX XXXX transactions, the Chase checking account transactions, and my email correspondence with the Chase representative.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,105XX,None,Consent provided,Web,06/01/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9157134
