Subsequently I contacted Bank of America asking why they were unable to verify my identification and how I could assure them of my identity. During the conversation their representative requested that I provide the Social Security Administration permission to verify my existence. Instead I provided a copy of my original Social Security Card and my REAL ID driver license on XX/XX/XXXX. 

On XX/XX/XXXX I received a denial identical to the XX/XX/XXXX letter citing the reason : Unable to verify identification. Once again I contacted Bank of America by telephone and asked why they could not identify me to their satisfaction. The banks representative stated that the Social Security Card copy and REAL ID driver license did not meet their requirements and that the bank needed a form SSA-89 Authorization for the Social Security Administration To Release Social Security Number ( SSN ) Verification and a copy of my XXXX IRS Income Tax filing. I provided the cited documents mid XXXX, XXXX and have received neither the requested VISA card, nor a third denial from Bank of America. 

It is my suspicion that Bank of America does not wish to honor the promotional bonus of XXXX XXXX Airline miles which were promised. My credit score is exceptionally high ( greater than 800 ) and my income stable. 

