11/03/22,Credit card or prepaid card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers",Didn't receive advertised or promotional terms,"While buying plane tickets with XXXX, a popup appeared to apply for their XXXX card and get a {$250.00} rebate. Nowhere did it say that there would be an annual fee. I bought and used the ticket and was approved for the card. I recently got the statement and noticed that a {$99.00} annual fee had been added to my bill. I called XXXX at XXXX and spoke with rep XXXX and then XXXX XXXX on XX/XX/22 and they stated that I would be charged an annual fee. I let them know that's not what I signed up for and that's not what their offer specified. I also let them know that their offer on line for a barclays XXXX card SAYS there's a "" XXXX '' annual fee ( see screenshot ). My card looks exactly the same as the one on line. They stated nothing could be done and I let them know this was bate and switch and I demanded that the annual fee be erased as that's not what I signed up for. They refused. I let them know I would be paying my bill minus the fraudulent {$99.00} fee.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,BARCLAYS BANK DELAWARE,NY,10009,None,Consent provided,Web,11/03/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6161995
11/11/22,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Problem using a debit or ATM card,"On XX/XX/2022, my husband 's wallet was stolen in the subway system in XXXX, XXXX. He lost his JP Morgan Chase debit card along with driver 's license, credit cards, etc. We notified Chase about the theft as soon as possible the same day. ( We were in a XXXX XXXX  with limited cell phone functionality, so we weren't able to report the theft as quickly as in the XXXX ) The thief or his accomplice used the debit card to make XXXX purchases totaling {$1000.00}. All transactions took place on Friday XX/XX/XXXX and were processed on Tuesday, XX/XX/XXXX. 
At first, Chase reversed the charges, then changed course, said we were responsible for them after all, and removed the funds from our checking account. We had XXXX fruitless phone calls to the service line to try to understand the bank 's reasoning. The only information we were able to get was a schedule of the charges ( with dates, no time stamp ) and a statement that they were deemed valid because we approved or authorized them. We know the theft took place between XXXX XXXX  and XXXX XXXX  because we were on the subway during that time, on our way to a lunch date at XXXX. Chase must have a time stamp for the disputed charges that would show they took place after XXXX or so.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11217,Older American,Consent provided,Web,11/11/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6190089
