03/19/24,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"**Statement Regarding Unauthorized Reporting of Private Information** I am deeply concerned about the unauthorized reporting of my private information to credit bureaus by Bank of America XXXX This violation of my privacy rights undermines the integrity of my credit profile and contravenes regulations outlined in the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and the Privacy of Consumer Financial Information ( Regulation P ). 

As outlined in the FCRA, consumer reporting agencies must only furnish consumer reports in accordance with the written instructions of the consumer to whom it relates ( 15 U.S. Code 1681b ). Furthermore, Regulation P mandates that financial institutions provide notice to customers about their privacy policies and practices, including the conditions under which nonpublic personal information may be disclosed to third parties ( 12 CFR 1016.4 ). 

The unauthorized sharing of my personal information by Bank of America is unacceptable and must be rectified immediately. I hereby demand that Bank of America take prompt action to remove all unauthorized information from my credit report and cease any further unauthorized reporting of my private information. Failure to comply may result in further legal action to enforce my rights and seek appropriate remedies for any damages incurred. 

-- - Sincerely, XXXX XXXX",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION",NY,109XX,None,Consent provided,Web,03/20/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8586934
