03/15/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Problem with a lender or other company charging your account,Transaction was not authorized,"To Whom It May Concern, I am compelled to submit a formal complaint against Capital One due to their handling of my fraud investigation case, referenced as Case No. XXXX # XXXX. This complaint arises from not only the unjust denial of my appeal based on misinformation but also from Capital One 's failure to provide any form of communication regarding their decision. Despite my proactive efforts, reaching out to them over five times to request clarification and to rectify the misinformation on their part, my attempts were met with empty assurances, and no representative has made an effort to contact me throughout the process. 

To my dismay, I discovered an unauthorized deduction of more than {$1200.00} from my account, executed without prior notification or explanation. This action by Capital One is unacceptable and contradicts the principles of fair customer treatment and transparency that financial institutions are expected to uphold. 

The banks refusal to engage in meaningful dialogue, coupled with their decision conveyed without notice, underscores a grave disregard for consumer rights and the integrity of their fraud investigation processes. It leaves me not only financially aggrieved but also deeply concerned about the standards of accountability and customer service at Capital One. 

Given these circumstances, I seek the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau 's intervention to secure a just resolution. This situation demands a thorough review of both my individual case and the broader practices of Capital One concerning customer communication and the handling of fraud investigations. I am prepared to supply all requisite documentation and evidence to substantiate my claims and to demonstrate the neglect and procedural failures on the part of Capital One. 

I appreciate your prompt attention to this urgent matter and look forward to your support in ensuring a fair and equitable outcome. 

Thank you for your assistance.",None,CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION,NY,11757,None,Consent provided,Web,03/15/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8558129
