06/23/23,Student loan,Private student loan,Dealing with your lender or servicer,Received bad information about your loan,"In XXXX I had my XXXX XXXX and XXXX XXXX Subsidized loans consolidated with XXXX XXXX ; these were subsequently serviced by Navient. In XX/XX/XXXX I requested a temporary forbearance due to COVID-19 and the fact that my FFELP consolidation loans were not a part of the student loan pause created by the CARES act. They had me believe this was my only option and that I was not eligible to reconsolidate these loans to take advantage of the student loan pause and more importantly to me the pause on student loan interest. I resumed payments in XX/XX/XXXX and have continued to make payments on time, and often above the minimum amount due, throughout this time. I have recently ( XX/XX/XXXX ) become aware that I am able to apply for a Direct consolidation loan and immediately applied after learning this from a studentaid.gov representative. I have contacted Navient ( XX/XX/XXXX ) asking if there were any way to adjust my account and remove the interest charged during this time and apply it towards the principal and was told the only thing they can do is a forbearance or possibly lower my payments. 
This is a company that no longer services federal student loans, yet is allowed to continue to deceive it's customers and profit from the misinformation it provides. I have paid thousands of dollars in interest during this time that would have all gone towards the principal had I consolidated with direct loans years ago as a direct result of this deception by Navient.",None,"Navient Solutions, LLC.",NY,146XX,None,Consent provided,Web,06/23/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,7157879
