03/29/23,Debt collection,Other debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt was paid,"Received two collection notices from TSI ( https : //tsico.com/ ) on behalf of XXXX for one of my companies. Called them to see what they are referring to since we're usually pretty current on our shipping bills. Was told it was for two shipments back in XXXX or so. Said I'd have to verify with XXXX to confirm they were unpaid. Had a pleasant conversation with someone there who, when I asked, advised me that yes, I can still pay them directly thru XXXX ( and therefore save the agency 's 14 % fee ). 

Went to the XXXX site, called them, paid the bills in full. TSI has been calling me about the so-called 'late charge '. The thing is the XXXX doesn't have a late charge. When I called they confirmed the bills were satisfied in full. 

TSI continues to call me and say they want their money. My response is always civil ; I speak with them and explain they're not entitled to a debt processing fee since they didn't process any payment. I've told them several times I am not ever going to pay. They continue to call and are belligerent when I respond that way. 

BTW 14 %!? Really? How is that legal? How can that be a fair percentage for sending a biull and processing? It's not as if they own the debt ; XXXX still was the debt carrier. 

I'm guessing this is happening to hundreds of individuals and firms as XXXX is a large company. I have even reached out to them to make note that perhaps TSI isn't the best collection arm to align themselves with.",None,TRANSWORLD SYSTEMS INC,NY,10024,Older American,Consent provided,Web,03/29/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6760326
