07/28/23,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I write this in reference to the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) and believe my federally protected consumer rights ; specifically my right to privacy and confidentiality under 15 USC 1681, have been breached. The accounts involved in this violation are as follows : XXXX - Account number : XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX - Account number : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  - Account number : XXXX XXXX XXXX - Account number : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX - Account number : XXXX Section XXXX ( A ) of 15 U.S.C 1681 safeguards my right to privacy. Additionally, Section 604 ( A ) ( 2 ) of the same code outlines that a consumer reporting agency may not provide account details without the written consent of the concerned consumer.

Section 1681c ( a ) ( 5 ) of 15 U.S.C mandates that a consumer reporting agency can not include any adverse information other than criminal conviction records that predate the report by over seven years.

As per 15 U.S.C 16 1681s-2 ( A ) ( 1 ), it is illegal for anyone to furnish consumer-related information to any consumer reporting agency if they are aware, or have justifiable reason to believe, that such information is inaccurate. 

These inaccuracies are currently obstructing my ability to purchase a home for my family and are negatively impacting my financial prospects. I hereby request the immediate deletion of these inaccuracies from my credit report. 

I anticipate your swift attention to rectify these inaccuracies, as this matter is crucial to my financial future.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,11210,None,Consent provided,Web,07/28/23,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,7319415
