11/01/24,Debt collection,Credit card debt,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt is not yours,"In XX/XX/year>, I received notice from a debt collection agency, Midland Credit Management, regarding two debts they claim are associated with retail credit cards originally issued by XXXX XXXX XXXX  and XXXX XXXX. I believe these debts may not be mine or are inaccurately reported. 
XX/XX/year> : I formally disputed these debts with Midland Credit Management, requesting debt validation under the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ). I asked them to provide : Proof of their legal right to collect these debts, including original agreements.

A breakdown of amounts owed, including fees, interest, and charges.

Verification of accurate reporting to credit bureaus. 
XX/XX/year> : I also submitted dispute letters to major credit bureaus, indicating potential inaccuracies. These debts are reported as charge-offs, yet I have not received a 1099-C Cancellation of Debt form, which is usually issued when a debt is officially canceled. As of today, Midland Credit Management has not provided adequate documentation to validate the debts or confirm their right to collect.

Due to the lack of validation and necessary 1099-C documentation, I believe these accounts are inaccurately reported. I request the CFPBs assistance to either validate these debts or remove them from my credit report if Midland Credit Management can not comply.",None,ENCORE CAPITAL GROUP INC.,NY,11729,None,Consent provided,Web,11/01/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,10655984
