08/15/24,Mortgage,Conventional home mortgage,Trouble during payment process,Interest rate,"This relates to XXXX XXXX XXXX  There are XXXX specific issue : XXXX ) There is a pervasive error in which they communicate the XXXX reset date as 1 month later. They are instead providing customers the first month payment due after 1 month of XXXX  XXXX. 
XXXX : The letter and their online banking system reminder states the XXXX XXXX  date as XX/XX/XXXX. They Reset the rate on XX/XX/XXXX. XX/XX/XXXX is the first payment due after 1 month of the new rate. 

XXXX ) They conduct the loan calculation on the wrong principal amount. 
The letter sent to customers is between XXXX months before the reset of the loan. So an XXXX loan might have a letter dated in XXXX. They do a calculation at that time assuming no additional prepayment of the loan. This becomes the new payment regardless of whether additional principal is paid down during the XXXX months. 

Given this rate environment AND ALSO the fact people are paying down, this is not a small difference. I calculate for item XXXX my new payment is over {$100.00} from what it ought to be on the principal balance. If I add in additional principal I have already paid and further intend to pay by XX/XX/XXXX then the number is quite high. 

In a falling interest rate environment, particularly if the XXXX  moves are > XXXX this is a significant calculation error. 

When I asked their customer service, they didn't appear to understand any of the above or its implications. I got tired of trying to escalate this properly as their only response was that the letter said the XXXX reset is in XX/XX/XXXX and therefore the mortgage payment is correct ( both of which are false, aka they are clearly resetting XX/XX/XXXX, and the calc on payments is clearly from XX/XX/XXXX assuming no additional principal payments ). 

I suspected this was done last year in 2023 as well. But I didn't have time to really catch them as I was traveling.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,WELLS FARGO & COMPANY,NY,10023,None,Consent provided,Web,08/15/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9811579
