03/19/24,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Closing an account,Company closed your account,"I noticed on XX/XX/2024 that my Citibank checking and savings accounts were inexplicably and suddenly closed by the bank, causing some recurring ACH transfers to fail. I logged in to my Citi account online and saw that there was a letter addressed to me on XX/XX/XXXX stating that my account was due to be closed, and the "" decision was made following the results of a review of bank information and records. '' There is otherwise no substantial reason given for the closure. I immediately tried to call the customer support number on my debit card but I was unable to get through to a human agent. I then went to my local Citibank branch office, but the staff there expressed puzzlement about what happened and were unable to help me or give me any explanations for the decision. I then called Citi 's Executive Response Unit and talked to an agent, they claimed that the decision was made by the Know Your Customer department at Citi and gave me a number to call. I called the provided number and got through to a second agent, who then told me that they were not responsible for the decision and claimed it is the branch office that conducted the account closure. But I have already been to the branch office, and they had no idea what happened! 

This is a nightmare. I am locked out of access to XXXX of dollars that I need to pay my bills, and I am not given any information on when I should expect to be paid back my balance amount from Citi. No one at Citi seems to take responsibility or can give me a reasonable explanation for why this is happening and what recourse options I have. I have been banking with Citi for almost XXXX  years and it is absolutely unacceptable that this is how they treat their most loyal customers.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,11101,None,Consent provided,Web,03/19/24,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,8576976
