04/10/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Credit inquiries on your report that you don't recognize,"On XX/XX/XXXX I went to XXXX XXXX XXXX to purchase a used XXXX XXXX XXXX. The total price was given en route to the dealer despite having multiple calls prior XXXX. The grand total was {$13000.00}. I paid {$8000.00} in cash, {$5000.00} on personal check and the remaining $ XXXX on a credit card. The salesman told me my social was needed for DMV. He then used it to run a soft credit check which in fact was a hard inquiry. A policy the dealer has when using personal checks. The salesman told me he would drive me to the bank to avoid using the personal check and credit card and then within 1-2 minutes came back and said they already ran my credit. This is fraudulent and a horrible business practice. I spoke with the manager who only offered a solution of an apology and they will re-train their salesman. No consolation for me. Im applying for a mortgage and my score has dropped which means I have to pay points to get my rate back.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NY,10309,None,Consent provided,Web,04/10/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,8745792
