05/20/24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"After careful review of my consumer report again, I still noticed that you continue to furnish misleading and inaccurate information on my consumer report that should not be there pursuant 15 USC 1681i and 15 USC 1681e ( b ) Accuracy of Report ; You have furnished inaccurate information which is illegal! You've reported transactions and experiences that are to be excluded from the consumer report pursuant 15 USC 1681a ( d ) 2 ( A ) I and charge offs are considered income according to the IRS and excluded from the consumer report. You continue to violate my federally protected consumer rights so Im exercising my right to OPT-OUT of reporting these accounts on my credit file pursuant 16 CFR 313, The Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act and The Privacy Act of 1974. Im opting out pursuant 15 USC 6802, 15 USC 6803 and 15 USC 6804 ; any authorization given, written or verbal is now RESCINDED! It is effective immediately! I demand these attached accounts be deleted from all consumer reports including XXXX, XXXX, XXXX, and XXXX . And according to the documentation provided by the Secretary of State Uniform Commercial Code Certification, there is no record of any lien from any company against me. I have supporting documentation from the Secretary of State to validate my claim. I also have proof of public legal notice, that all current liabilities have been transferred to the Revocable Living Trust XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ''. Therefore, the inaccurate and erroneous accounts must be DELETED from my credit file. I am exercising my OPT-OUT RIGHTS as you continuously violate my consumer rights, and I intend to accelerate legal actions pursuant 15 US Code 1681n - Civil liability for willful noncompliance -Please See Attached",None,DISCOVER BANK,NY,11217,None,Consent provided,Web,05/20/24,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,9056611
