11/05/23,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Getting a credit card,Card opened without my consent or knowledge,"XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, SD XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, DE XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX, ME XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX EXPERIAN XXXX Consumer Financial Protection Bureau XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX, XXXX XXXX Subject : Request for Assistance with Unauthorized Inquiries and Identity Theft Dear Sir/Madam, I hope this letter finds you well. I am writing to seek assistance regarding unauthorized inquiries on my credit report, which I believe are a result of identity theft and a data breach. I have made several attempts to resolve this issue by contacting the credit bureaus and various banks, but unfortunately, the unauthorized inquiries still remain on my credit report. This situation has been adversely affecting my credit and my financial future, and I kindly request your jurisdiction to step in and help me address this matter. 

I have diligently reached out to all three major credit bureaus, Experian, XXXX, and XXXX, to inform them about the unauthorized inquiries on my credit report. Moreover, I have also contacted several banks, including but not limited to XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX consolidated, and XXXX XXXX, in order to report the identity theft and the data breach that I have become a victim of. Despite my efforts, the inquiries have not been removed from my credit report, and I believe this is unfair and unjust. 

Given the impact these unauthorized inquiries are having on my creditworthiness and financial standing, I kindly request your intervention in this matter. I urge you to investigate the situation, assess the evidence I can provide, and take appropriate action to ensure that these unauthorized inquiries are promptly removed from my credit report. Additionally, it would be greatly appreciated if you could facilitate any necessary communication between the credit bureaus, banks, and myself to ensure a swift resolution. 

E I am grateful for your attention to this matter and for any assistance you can provide. Should you require any further information or documentation, please do not hesitate to contact me at XXXX or XXXX. I eagerly await your response and resolution to this pressing issue. 

Thank you for your time and consideration. 

Sincerely, XXXX XXXX XXXX",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,NY,10550,None,Consent provided,Web,11/05/23,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,7805412
