10/08/22,Credit card or prepaid card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"In XX/XX/XXXX, we made a deposit of {$1000.00} on our Chase credit card for a hut tub based on incomplete information provided by the salesman. He told us that it might be delayed but that a form we signed didn't really apply as the hot tub was in their showroom. We prepared the site and had electrical work done. 

We were told it was to be delivered and it was not. Finally, in XX/XX/XXXX we said we wanted a date certain or a refund. We were offered various concessions which we declined. We were then offered a full refund of $ XXXX SEE ATTACHED Exhibits L 1-3 ( as we paid other monies on another card ). The other bank is working to get us a refund. 

In part per Exhibits L, we were told that "" We understand if these terms aren't acceptable we will gladly refund your deposit and allow you to cancel your hot tub order. '' Also, "" It will be the full amount you paid and will be handled Monday. If it was on credit card it will be refunded to the same card. '' To this day, we have no tub and no refund. Despite this, Chase claims the charge was valid! SEE ATTACHED letter of XX/XX/XXXX.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11793,None,Consent provided,Web,10/08/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6065554
