07/26/22,Checking or savings account,Savings account,Managing an account,Funds not handled or disbursed as instructed,"On XX/XX/2022, Citibank executed XXXX wire transfers out of my accounts totaling {$240000.00} without my authorization. XXXX of the transfers were from the checking account and XXXX from a savings account. 
I have made perhaps XXXX wire transfer in the last 35 years, and I never make any payments from savings accounts, only through the checking account. Before the wire transfers were made, the money was shuffled between our checking and savings accounts. Citibank negligently did not fully recognize these gross aberrations in these activities, as it sent me only XXXX email asking if I approved the wire transfers. I did not see this email before the bank quickly released the wire transfers. Notwithstanding the cumulative total of the wire transfers or that these wire transfers effectively emptied all my wife and my joint Citibank accounts, the bank executed the XXXX wire transfers without contacting me by phone or insuring that any response purportedly by me was authentic. I have filed a complaint with Citibank and also with the XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX Police Department.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,10025,Older American,Consent provided,Web,07/26/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5812333
