10/06/22,Credit card or prepaid card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Card was charged for something you did not purchase with the card,"This happened with Barclays credit card two days ago and they haven't resolved the problem. I checked my checking account as I do every morning to avoid surprises. Unfortunately, I noticed a double charge of {$350.00} from Barclays on that account in regard to this credit card payment. I automatically called their customer service, spoke to the manager who insured me that many customers, especially customers from U.S have been calling in that regard, and they are working to fix the problem. Because I already paid my credit card bill and budget my account accordingly, this checking account went on overdraft mode, and I was forced to quickly replenish my account to avoid fees. The manager promised to do everything at her end to fix the problem before the end of the day. Unfortunately, I woke this morning and noticed that my checking account was credited and debited right away. I called again spent time explaining again, and they apologized and promised to fix it. I believe that they have a breach in their security system, which is really alarming. As of the time I am writing this they haven't fixed the problem.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,BARCLAYS BANK DELAWARE,NY,10460,None,Consent provided,Web,10/06/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6054239
