07/24/22,Credit card or prepaid card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Other features, terms, or problems",Problem with rewards from credit card,"I signed up for XXXX reward program credit card with Chase for three free nights certificate if spend $ XXXX within 3 months of the account opening. Within few weeks Chase offered exactly same credit card for five free nights if spend $ XXXX. Chase asked existing customers to call customer service if a customer wants to switch to new five nights to check their eligibility. I called Chase customer service on XXXX Sunday at XXXX and spoke with a lady from Chase XXXX I requested to switch my offer from 3 nights to 5 nights and the rep said everyone here knows the process. Please call us back as soon as you spend {$5000.00} within 3 months and we will file a report with our marketing department to get you 5 nights certificate. The lady put a note in my account that I intended to spend {$5000.00} to get the 5 free nights certificate. Account was opened on XX/XX/XXXX so I needed to spend {$5000.00} by mid XXXX to get the 5 nights certificate, which I spent ahead of the deadline to get the promised 5 nights reward certificate. 

Chase never issued me the 5 nights reward certificates, although I followed up with them few times. On XX/XX/22, I spoke with a Chase customer service representative and the rep said she read all the notes in my account and she said since they advised you to spend $ XXXX, I will escalated the issue and said they should approve as per the previous conversation customer already spent $ XXXX. Chase definitely should honor the 5 nights certificate to me as they promised and avoid discrimination as I was eligible for 5 reward certificates. Please kindly investigate the whole program for innocent customers.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,14051,None,Consent provided,Web,07/24/22,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,5804650
