08/16/22,Credit card or prepaid card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Other features, terms, or problems",Problem with rewards from credit card,"I purchased tickets through my chase rewards card with XXXX XXXX for 4 family members in the amount of {$1100.00}. The flight got cancelled due to the COVID-19 pandemic. I got a credit for the airfare through Chase with XXXX XXXX. Please see the file attached. Now, in order for me to obtain this credit a Chase representative told me that I have to first purchase new airline tickets with XXXX XXXX only with my own money for same or greater amount of credit. Which I did, see file attached in the amount of {$1.00}, XXXX. I was told that I will then get refunded. Now, I was denied the refund and didnt get the original credit! 

I was trying to resolve this case with multiple Chase representatives and spent more than 20 hours on the phone with them unsuccessfully. 

I am filing this complaint to get a full refund that should include the original credit in the amount of {$1100.00} plus the airfare that I paid in the amount of {$1200.00} for a total of {$2400.00}. Originally, they shouldve let me use my credit of {$1100.00} to buy my new tickets, and I would have to pay only the difference ( $ XXXX {$1100.00} ). However, I was told that to get my credit back, I had to first pay for the tickets out of pocket and then I would be refunded for everything, which is the total of {$2400.00}. If I am refunded ONLY the {$1100.00}, I will still be in debt of {$1200.00}, instead of {$130.00} ( the difference between the tickets ).",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,11235,None,Consent provided,Web,08/16/22,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,5882277
