07/31/23,Credit card or prepaid card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,"Other features, terms, or problems",Problem with customer service,"The complaint is regarding my Chase Sapphire Preferred Card and ability to file customer complaints with Chase. 
1. I had a reservation booked with points at the time I closed my Preferred Card. It was voluntary closure as we decided to open Reserve card in stead. As my travel plans changed, I had to cancel that reservation. Chase declined to give me back points worth ~ {$450.00} that were used for the canceled reservation or to transfer them to my new card. Stated reason was that rewards not used withing 30 days of cards closure are forfeited. However, I started attempts to claim the reward points or cash equivalent back immediatly upon canceling the reservation. 
2. Chase does not give customers ability to open complaints and track their resolution. When I attempted to file complaint regarding the above issue, I was told that when/if Chase representatives create complaints, they send them elsewhere to be processed. They do not give complaint numbers to customers to allow following up on resolution. There is no way for customers to know if complaint was actually filed, and no way to learn how it was resolved. Moreover, it was only from the third representative agreed to file a complaint on my behalf and the two just flat out refused.",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,115XX,None,Consent provided,Web,07/31/23,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes,N/A,7324726
