07/18/22,Mortgage,FHA mortgage,Applying for a mortgage or refinancing an existing mortgage,None,"I tried to access federal information about insured mortgages and then searched for an online application. I did not notice that the link I clicked on, which appeared to be a website supported by HUD, was actually something called Rocket Mortgage. I was very clear that I was seeking a first time mortgage, clicked on something to that effect, requested application to apply for first time mortgage. I was redirected to a site that entailed my creating an account with Rocket Mortgage, which I, reluctantly, did. Only when I had completed that account creation did it become apparent that my "" account '' was for refinancing a mortgage. I exited the account platform and tried to sign in to access a first home buyer interface. I was not permitted to do so unless I created a second account -- a completely additional account, new password, with all my personal info. This doubling up of a single company 's account with dual accounts for me is part of a persistent scam of impersonators for me on line. I tried to locate information to close the scam account and was not permitted to do that, either. I submitted a complaint to the company about this state of affairs. I have zero confidence that the scam account will be closed even if I get a ( probably fake ) email being all kinds of solicitous of my belief to that effect. So now there is a fake Rocket Mortgage account out there with my personal information and good credit score to be used by people impersonating me on line and very little I can do about it.",None,"Rocket Mortgage, LLC",NY,14424,None,Consent provided,Web,07/18/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5783183
