12/17/22,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Problem with a credit reporting company's investigation into an existing problem,Investigation took more than 30 days,"hello I was due to begin paying a loan for the total amount of {$2000.00}, with the first statement being billed on XX/XX/22 for {$170.00}, a private loan through XXXX XXXX and XXXX. The email in which I was receiving notifications on was hacked at the time and I did not have access to the notifications being received as well as the mails being sent to the wrong address. Given the unprecedented pandemic situation related to XXXX loans, and unclear communications constantly changing, I was under the impression after not receiving clear communication that all of my loans were under the federal deferment related to XXXX. These loans were subsequently late by 2 months due to the miscommunication rather than my inability to pay the loan in full, one on XX/XX/22 and one on XX/XX/22, however had three alerts on my credit report negatively affecting my credit score, two being after the date the loan was paid in full and two late payments on my credit report. The loan was paid in full on XX/XX/22, however negatively affected my credit score in the medium term and also causing me to get denied for a credit card in which I was applying for through my place of employment ( Chase Credit Card denied for on XX/XX/22 ). 

I believe at the very least I should have one late payment on my credit score, not two, given the loan was paid in full on XX/XX/22 and I got docked for XX/XX/22 and XX/XX/22 so that is just an error. However, I believe given the unprecedented nature of the communication, my clear ability to pay the balance promptly when properly notified, and the error of late payments justifies the fact to discredit the negative affects of the 2 late payments on my credit score as well as a denial of application of credit. 

I hope these comments are taken into consideration and the righteous improvements due to the error of the debt collection agency and or/XXXX XXXXXXXX in inaccurately reporting a credit past due is worthy of a correction and subsequent improvement to current credit score. 

Thank you, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX",None,JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.,NY,100XX,None,Consent provided,Web,12/17/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6330472
