08/25/22,Debt collection,Other debt,Written notification about debt,Didn't receive notice of right to dispute,"In XXXX I bought a business in our mall. It was an XXXX XXXX  XXXX The first year and a half were great. Then XXXX happened and the mall had very little business. We were pulling in on average {$100.00} a day. I didnt have the capital to keep the business up during the hard times, so we had to close. 

I owed a food service about {$16000.00} at that time of which I was served a judgment in XXXX or so. I started paying {$44.00} a week every week. This year XXXX I have the debt down to {$4300.00}. I then received a letter from the collection agency that another {$5000.00} was attached to the judgment for interest. This bumped me back up to {$9400.00}. 

I have already paid about {$23000.00} on a {$16000.00} debt and now when I am close to being paid off, they are tacking on another {$5000.00}. In the letter they sent me that was dated, and post marked for the XXXX of XX/XX/XXXX they offered me a payoff but only if I paid on XX/XX/XXXX. I didnt receive the letter until the XXXX. How can this be right. I was given no chance to rectify this situation. 

Furthermore, six months ago, I called the creditor to try to negotiate a payoff and they wouldnt return my call. Now they wait until they can hit me with all this interest and offer a fake payoff because the date was after the letter was received.",Company believes the complaint is the result of a misunderstanding,Lacy Katzen LLP,NY,136XX,None,Consent provided,Web,09/12/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5915715
