10/03/22,Mortgage,Conventional home mortgage,Trouble during payment process,None,"he mortgage originated with XXXX, acquired by Wells Fargo at some point. The account was in two names - mine and my then spouse 's name. We separated in XXXX at which time he moved out and I made all of the payments. I was awarded the home in the divorce in XX/XX/XXXX and my ex-spouse signed a quit claim deed in XXXX when I refinanced with another institution. 
Several months prior to my closing I asked Wells Fargo to research a {$970.00} fee they had added to my account for what they indicated was "" foreclosure expenses ''. They never reversed those charges, and they were included in my payoff quote and paid in XXXX. I received a letter on XX/XX/XXXX reimbursing me for those fees along with an added amount for "" the time these funds were unavailable ''. This check was made payable to me "" and '' my former spouse. 
Any checks for funds to the account ( class action lawsuits ) have always been issue to us both, and my former spouse refuses to endorse them for me. I had to use our divorce attorneys ( a XXXX process ) each time I needed a check endorsed. 
In this case, the final payoff was sent to them on my behalf by my new financial institution. This check included an amount I had disputed. There is a divorce decree and a quit claim deed showing he has no interest in the property. I have contacted Wells Fargo by phone and by fax to request they reissue this check in my name alone and the responses have been refusals at each attempt. I should not have to hire an attorney every time I need a check signed by him. They already have a copy of the quit claim deed, and my banks will not allow me to cash or deposit the check without the other signature. Wells Fargo correspondence stated they would replace "" and '' with "" or '' on the check but would need a NOTARIZED authorization signed by both parties to do this. ( I guess they think he will give me a signature on a piece of paper knowing he won't on a check ). 
The company is not working with me to find a solution to this, and I simply want MY money back, which I paid, for fees that were NOT supposed to be charged and were DISPUTED before they were paid for. I request they send any future checks in the same manner - payable to me alone.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,WELLS FARGO & COMPANY,NY,13440,None,Consent provided,Web,10/19/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6044114
