08/01/22,Student loan,Federal student loan servicing,Dealing with your lender or servicer,Received bad information about your loan,"I was enrolled as a XXXX at XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX beginning in Fall of XXXX through Fall XXXX when I officially withdrew with a leave of absence. When I withdrew I did so within the window that allowed my student loans to be return to lender. ( {$2500.00} XXXX Stafford Unsub & XXXX XXXX Stafford Sub ) For whatever reason this info was not adjusted correctly and it was shown that these 2 loans were dispersed. But they had been cancelled and returned. 
After many years of the incorrect information being provided to me without the ability to view accurate information. I began payment of the loans, based upon the false belief that once loan was satisfied, I would be able to have access to the details of the loan. 
Basically loans were cancelled, but I was unable to verify that until recently. 
I reached out to the loan servicer, which is Navient and was met first with a representative that was as shocked and confused as I was regarding the inaccuracy status history of my loans. I was told a case would be opened to look into the loans and a promissory note would be obtained to establish an idea of what had happened. I was told resolution would be within a two week time frame. 
When I received no update I reached out to Navient again for clarification of the validity of the actual loans, I was met with a hostile representative that talked in circles and offered no assistance. 
When I look on the studentaid.gov The loans I have been paying on for the past 25 years states that the loans were disbursed but returned and cancelled. 
I have been accruing interest as well as late fees on these loans that are not even valid. I also have been paying them for the past several years and I am so annoyed that I can not get clarification or help regarding this. Attached are statements that show the loans were cancelled. The only valid loan was FFELP Stafford Sub Loan XXXX. 
I really need help figuring this all out. Navient will not help me with this and refuses to acknowledge that the loans were cancelled and have not require any payment. 
If any additional information is required, please let me know and I will forward whatever info is required.",None,"Navient Solutions, LLC.",NY,117XX,None,Consent provided,Web,08/01/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5832295
