03/20/23,Student loan,Private student loan,Dealing with your lender or servicer,Received bad information about your loan,"To Whom It May Concern : I am writing to lodge a formal complaint against Navient, my student loan provider, for their refusal to grant me the full 48 months of in-school deferment eligibility as outlined in the terms of my loan. Despite multiple attempts to resolve this issue, Navient has consistently attempted to gaslight me by suggesting that I have already utilized some months of eligibility with my prior loan servicer. I am absolutely certain that I have never used in-school deferment with my previous servicer, and Navient is well-aware of this fact. 

Navient has sent me documents from my previous servicer ( please see the attached files ) which they seem to have used to arbitrarily determine the number of months I have already spent in in-school deferment. However, nowhere in these documents is there any indication that in-school deferment was ever applied. In a poor attempt to resolve the issue, Navient has arbitrarily applied additional months of in-school deferment to my account, but this solution is neither satisfactory nor accurate. 

As it stands, one loan has in-school deferment expiring in XX/XX/XXXX, and another in XX/XX/XXXX. According to Navient 's own documents, in-school deferment was first applied in XX/XX/XXXX. With 48 months of eligibility, this would mean that my in-school deferment should not expire until XX/XX/XXXX. 

This issue has been inadequately resolved and poorly managed. Every attempt I have made to contact Navient has resulted in copied and pasted responses suggesting that the issue is being "" researched. '' I am disappointed and frustrated with Navient 's lack of transparency and failure to fulfill the terms of my loan agreement. 

I kindly request the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau 's assistance in resolving this issue and ensuring that I receive the full 48 months of in-school deferment to which I am entitled. I have attached all relevant documents for your review and consideration. 

I appreciate your time and attention to this matter and look forward to a prompt and fair resolution.",None,"Navient Solutions, LLC.",NY,11217,None,Consent provided,Web,03/20/23,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6725380
