12/01/22,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Problem using a debit or ATM card,"I filed a complaint through Wells Fargo Claims Assistance Center for unauthorized transactions in my checking account amounting to approximately {$390.00} from XXXX between XXXX and XX/XX/2022. I never used this account for XXXX shopping and I realized that there have been charges without my knowledge. 

I received communication from Wells Fargo including email and physical letter stating that they conducted investigations and they confirmed unauthorized use of my account and refunded {$220.00}. The letter indicated that transactions that occurred more than 60 days after the activity appeared in the bank statements are beyond Well Fargo 's liability and so they are not refunding such amount. 

I called the Claims Assistance Center to make an appeal on their decision. I explained that this case should not be covered under such 60-day policy because it is not my fault that their system is not able to protect customer 's bank accounts. I'm losing more than {$160.00} because Wells Fargo is not able to protect my funds and they don't want any liability for the reason that I did not report it within 60 days. 

The first agent that I spoke to on XXXX XXXX refused to take any action and did not entertain my appeal and instead, transferred me to another department, but eventually hung up on me. I called again and the second agent said the same thing and I insisted that I be given the chance to appeal whether they provide a person or email to write to or through any leadership in Wells Fargo. I indicated to them that if they refuse to take my appeal, I will file a complaint in CFPB. 

How can people trust these banks if there are policies that are unfavorable to consumers? {$160.00} is not a lot of money but for a single parent like me who work 2-3 jobs to feed my family, every dollar counts and these bank policies do not help in any way.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,WELLS FARGO & COMPANY,NY,11379,None,Consent provided,Web,12/01/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6267053
