07/28/22,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"It has been brought to my attention that you are not blocking files when theyre sent with an FTC fraud report. Since it is a requirement by law 605b of the FCRA Im sending this letter certified mail to help establish a legal recourse. If you choose to not block the following items listed below which are reporting inaccurately due to identity theft, I will be handing my documents over to my attorney to start a legal action. Its my intention to not pursue any legal action so please adhere to the law Please remove/block the following accounts as they are fraudulent & were opened without my consent or knowledge CITICARDS CBNA XXXX Date Opened : XX/XX/2013 Balance : {$25000.00} and CITICARDS CBNA XXXX Date Opened : XX/XX/2013 Balance : {$14000.00} If you claim these accounts are 100 % accurate and verifiable then I need you to provide me with copies of any documentation associated with this account which bears my signature, as I know none exists. In the absence of any such documentation bearing my signature, I formally request that this information be immediately deleted from the credit file you maintain under my Social Security number.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,11205,None,Consent provided,Web,07/28/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5816568
09/20/22,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Problem with a credit reporting company's investigation into an existing problem,Was not notified of investigation status or results,"I have disputed the referenced accounts to the 3 main credit bureaus and do not owe your company anything. I dont know this company and I do not recall ever having this debt and appears to be fraud, see attached FTC Report. Moreover, no adequate information has been given and noticed these accounts appear to violate my rights as well, per 15 USC 1692 ( e ) ( f ) ( g ). Moreover, you stated the account was verified as accurate by law 15 USC 1681 ( e ). Per 15 USC 1681 ( e ) The term investigative consumer report means a consumer report or portion thereof in which information on a consumers character, general reputation, personal characteristics, or mode of living is obtained through personal interviews with neighbors, friends, or associates of the consumer reported on or with others with whom he is acquainted or who may have knowledge concerning any such items of information. However, such information shall not include specific factual information on a consumers credit record obtained directly from a creditor of the consumer or from a consumer reporting agency when such information was obtained directly from a creditor of the consumer or from the consumer. Investigations weren't completed as described by law and no factual information should be on credit reports. Im requesting the removal of accounts and/or monetary compensation due to violations of my rights. Im currently seeking litigation regarding consistent harassment, unfair debt practices, adding without my permission/authorization within 5 days, and more. As the original creditor, only I can validate the debt therefore Im requesting removal and this account violates my consumer rights in several ways. Please remove and provide some updates within 4 days of receipt, as this has been ongoing for over 3-4 months.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10462,None,Consent provided,Web,09/20/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5999274
09/20/22,Credit card or prepaid card,Gift card,Problem with a purchase or transfer,Charged for a purchase or transfer you did not make with the card,"I was given a {$500.00} Vanilla Visa gift card. Around XX/XX/XXXX, I discovered when the card was rejected by a vendor that the card did not have the balance I had expected. I then tried to register online with Vanilla via its website to obtain information about the card 's transactions but the card # was rejected online. Further, I called the number printed on the card, and the most appropriate recorded voice prompt/option only provided the dates and amounts of the last five charges, not any information about the entities charging, not even their names. I was able to determine that on XX/XX/XXXX, {$23.00}, was charged to my card but was unknown/unauthorized, leaving a balance of {$160.00}. Subsequently, I spent days trying to obtain information about the company or entity that charged the {$23.00}. However, the Vanilla website continued to reject my credit card #, and the telephone number did not produce a live person or the information I sought. 
On XX/XX/XXXX, I called Visa customer service, spoke to XXXX who attempted to contact Vanilla on my behalf, unsuccessfully. He filed an incident report to submit to Vanilla and suggested that I call Vanilla, again, and choose the option for "" stolen cards. '' That same day, I tried Vanilla, and followed XXXX 's advice. I finally spoke to live person, XXXX of Vanilla, who informed me that XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX billed that {$23.00}, but she had no telephone # for the company. Being unfamiliar with that company, I filed a telephone complaint with Vanilla, via that representative, who explained to me that the {$160.00} left on my card will be on hold for ONE WEEK while they investigate the disputed {$23.00} and that after one week I must call an additional time to have the card activated again. 
On XXXX, I called Vanilla as instructed to activate the remaining undisputed {$160.00} balance. On that day, I spoke to another rep, XXXX, from Vanilla who informed me that no investigation began, that I must report the details of the complaint to her again via telephone, and then wait to receive a written form, complete that, and return it. She then assigned # case # XXXX to my complaint and told me that after Vanilla receives the completed written form the investigation ensues but I must wait up to an additional 90 days after that receipt of the form for a decision regarding the {$23.00} charge AND the release of my {$160.00} card balance! 
There is no reason to hold {$160.00} of MY funds for 90 more days while they investigate {$23.00}! Notably, Vanilla added an extra week to this waiting period by not filing my telephone complaint and not submitting the written form to me when I first spoke to its rep on XX/XX/XXXX, not to mention the days and time I spent prior to that attempting to reach them via online and telephone about the disputed charge. 
I even asked Vanilla if they could just issue immediately another card for the {$160.00}, while we await the determination regarding the {$23.00} charg

e. Vanilla said no. I complain about the delay to investigate and refusal to promptly release the {$160.00} for my use- to be denied funds that are undisputedly mine for a total of over 100 days is unacceptable.",None,Incomm Holdings Inc.,NY,11203,None,Consent provided,Web,09/20/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5999353
