06/24/22,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit repair services,Fraud or scam,None,"I got my credit repair account with Credit Saint XX/XX/XXXX. I was not charged until XX/XX/XXXX. Throughout my tenure with this company I was actively reviewing the progress that was being made on my account. I saw that multiple removals were being made so I decided to stay with this agency as it seemed they were making great progress. It wasn't until I decided to comb through my credit report in XXXX of XXXX ( after 8 months with Credit Saint ) that I realized that majority of the "" removals '' they were reporting to my account weren't actually being removed from my credit reports. I called, and spoke to the representatives and they told me they would conduct an audit of my account so I could get a more accurate reporting and they would call back with my results in 2-3 days. They never called back. I went into my client portal and they updated my account with the accurate reporting from the audit, and to my surprise majority of the "" removals '' they reported had not actually been removed. I called Credit Saint to cancel my service immediately on XX/XX/XXXX, and they told me that I didn't qualify for any refunds ( even though they mislead me for months on the productivity of their services ) I fought back and they ended up granting me their 3 month guarantee refund as well as my last payment that they deducted from my bank account resulting in 4 months of my money returned. I also learned that they are suppose to conduct a monthly audit on their end to ensure they are reporting accurate information to their customers and that they "" dropped the ball on my account, and will do an internal investigation to make sure this doesn't happen to future customers ''. Fast forward to 15 days after the "" refund '' and still no money in my account. I called my bank to see what the hold up was and they confirmed that they never received a refund from Credit Saint. I call Credit Saint with this information, and they told me its the banks fault and that they issued the refund on the XXXX of XXXX. I have receipts stating that they refunded me on the XXXX as well. After fighting back I learn that they didn't actually issue any refund. I gave them my information yet again, but as of now I have not received anything from Credit Saint in my account. -I was mislead with the productivity of my account. - I was told verbatim from the higher ups that they dropped the ball are reported false information for the entire time I was their client -Im not sure if any work was done prior to them charging me",Company believes the complaint is the result of a misunderstanding,Saint Services LLC,NY,111XX,None,Consent provided,Web,07/13/22,Closed with monetary relief,Yes,N/A,5705036
11/25/22,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Problem with a credit reporting company's investigation into an existing problem,Was not notified of investigation status or results,"I have disputed the referenced accounts to the 3 main credit bureaus and do not owe your company anything. I dont know this company and I do not recall ever having this debt and appears to be fraud, see attached FTC Report. Moreover, no adequate information has been given and noticed these accounts appear to violate my rights as well, per 15 USC 1692 ( e ) ( f ) ( g ). Moreover, you stated the account was verified as accurate by law 15 USC 1681 ( e ). Per 15 USC 1681 ( e ) The term investigative consumer report means a consumer report or portion thereof in which information on a consumers character, general reputation, personal characteristics, or mode of living is obtained through personal interviews with neighbors, friends, or associates of the consumer reported on or with others with whom he is acquainted or who may have knowledge concerning any such items of information. However, such information shall not include specific factual information on a consumers credit record obtained directly from a creditor of the consumer or from a consumer reporting agency when such information was obtained directly from a creditor of the consumer or from the consumer. Investigations weren't completed as described by law and no factual information should be on credit reports. Im requesting the removal of accounts and/or monetary compensation due to violations of my rights. Im currently seeking litigation regarding consistent harassment, unfair debt practices, adding without my permission/authorization within 5 days, and more. As the original creditor, only I can validate the debt therefore Im requesting removal and this account violates my consumer rights in several ways. Please remove and provide some updates within 4 days of receipt, as this has been ongoing for over 3-4 months.",None,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NY,10462,None,Consent provided,Web,11/25/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,6248540
