06/22/22,Mortgage,Conventional home mortgage,Closing on a mortgage,None,"I applied for a loan with Rocket Mortgage, the loan originators name is XXXX XXXX ID : XXXX. When I spoke with XXXX I explained that I was applying for the loan to see if I would qualify and that if I did I would need to sell my current home first before closing on the acquisition of this home. I explained that this would be a process and it would likely take a while, putting me past my rate lock period. He explained no problem and told me rate locks are about XXXX dollars each and that they are due at the time of closing. I was ok with this as I understand that the rate would need to be extended. I extended it a total of 3 times and I am now ready to close the transaction and purchase the new property. I then get a call from XXXX with Quicken Loans XXXX ID : XXXX stating that he has great news and he worked his magic. My rate went up, and because the second rate lock expired I now need to go from XXXX cash to close to over XXXX cash to close. I said I was told it was XXXX, and that those numbers do not add up. He said he would look into it and called me back the next day ( XX/XX/2022 ). When he called me back today he said he looked into the issue with another department and it turns out "" They failed to disclose the penalties and cost of extending the rate 3 times. '' After telling me that he then proceeded to tell me that Quicken Loans has decided there is nothing they can do to credit these costs. Now I am a week out from closing and have my current house about to close and I have to come up with an extra almost XXXX to buy the new house, or I will not have a new home for myself and 4 kids. This is the definition of predatory lending and not disclosing the costs of the loans. I am not sure what I can do as I hurry to find the additional funds.",None,"Rocket Mortgage, LLC",NY,13212,None,Consent provided,Web,06/22/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5698329
