06/28/22,Credit card or prepaid card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem when making payments,Problem during payment process,"I am in the middle of applying for a mortgage. It was reported on my credit report a debt that hadn't been aware of from Citi Bank. I contacted the bank and they said the debt was past the statute of limitations and I can only make a voluntary payment. I begged them to make a payment over the phone but they said I can only pay with a cashiers check to a facility in XXXX KY. It was very hard for me, but I put together the money for a full payment. I overnighted a cashiers check together with a letter of my ss # and a request for it to be expedited. I had the package tracked and on my end I see that it was received XXXX AM on XX/XX/22. I called numerous times and after many hold times and even getting hung up on by a representative, they gave vague responses "" that it is probably in middle of processing '' or that "" it takes time for it to post and update.. '' I contacted XXXX bank who issued the check and although the money had been debited from my account at the time of purchase, XXXX bank told me that as of today XX/XX/22 the money has still not been deposited by Citi bank . I spoke to many reps and they all claimed that they have no way to contact the facility that processes the payments. 
Then the reps told me that even after the payment posts I will have to wait another 15 days for the check to clear before they give me a paid in full XXXX balance letter as per company policy, I told them that if they require a bank check there is no processing time, but was just told that is the bank 's policy.. 
I'm under contract to buy a house my deadline is approaching and I need this matter resolved ASAP that I can show the loan officer that I paid in full. The reps contradicted each other one told me that I should send in another payment others told me that it takes time to process. 
They reported the debt I expect them to be fair, I tried to make a phone payment, I tried to send in a payment..",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,10312,None,Consent provided,Web,06/28/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5717711
