When checking my Account Summary online on XXXX XXXX I saw a pending charge for an unauthorized cash advance of {$64.00}. I called Citi and was told that the charges were related to the XXXX cash advances that were placed back on my account. I asked for a supervisor and spoke to XXXX XXXX, a XXXX XXXX XXXX at XXXX. After explaining that the scammers had obtained my Citi account information directly from my credit card account information stored at XXXX she assured me that the charges would be reversed. I received a letter, dated XX/XX/2022 saying the dispute has been closed and the charges would be rebilled to my account. I again called the fraud department at Cit and was advised to send a letter asking them to re-open the case. The letter is in the mail, addressed to XXXX XXXX XXXX in XXXX XXXX, SD XXXX. 
