06/24/22,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Funds not handled or disbursed as instructed,I was contacted via phone by someone claiming to be from my baking institution : Citibank the Friday of XXXX XXXX  weekend. It was a call in response to a text I received ( presumably ) from citi saying my XXXX card was compromised and I would be getting a call to secure my account. While speaking with this gentleman I provided no information as I thought he was in fact a citi customer service rep. The hold music was the same. His script was theirs and he was listing transactions that I had made. He ordered me a debit card which was delivered the next day at XXXX. He then put me on hold. While I was holding I noticed funds were transferred from my savings to my checking and a wire transfer was authorized. As I was in the middle of an oil change I assumed we lost connection so I called citibank back. I told them money was wired from my account without permission. They told me I authorized it however they couldn't tell me how it was authorized. I was on the phone with them when it was authorized. So the woman I was speaking to immediate transferred me to the wire fraud department. While on hold the original citbank gentleman who I now knew was a scammer applied for a loan ordered me a new debit card and moved money and wired money to a person I don't know. When speaking with a teller at the XXXX NY location I showed her the emails and texts the original call instigated and she confirmed that they were real citibank correspondence. When I tried to tell them this on the phone they blamed me for authorizing transactions I in fact did not. The loan is now on my credit score. Citibank told me no other accounts were opened in my name but I kept receiving emails from them saying I had for 72 hours after the scam. I tried so hard and quickly to resolve the issue and between wait times and citi employees not believing what I was telling them the scammer had access to my account and compromised it within the 2 hours it took citibank to close and block the account. The tell I referred to before called her supervisors and other higher ups and they didn't belive what she was saying about my case. I was told the money was gone and my account was frozen but that I can open a new one.,Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"CITIBANK, N.A.",NY,125XX,None,Consent provided,Web,06/24/22,Closed with explanation,Yes,N/A,5702748
